{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter","id":1321831,"title":"TC: Aberrant Kickstarter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-01T22:27:59-07:00","id":1321831,"title":"TC: Aberrant Kickstarter","content":"Holding topic for the Kickstarter itself. For now - <b>How would advertise Aberrant to other gamers?</b> I run polish Storypath FB group, but do not know about setting. Only it's twist on normal superhero genere and heroes are like celebrities in it it. Any points to raise in advertisement for fandom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-01T22:41:19-07:00","id":1321833,"title":"","content":"This part of the celebrities is one that really get the attention of people, but Aberrant is more about what people would do if they had the power of a god (that\u2019s the slogan...), they can be super strong, be invisible, be super fast, bullet proof, and control the elements, but they can also be super the ultimate baseline guy (all dots in all skills and all attributes and all edges (formerly backgrounds) with not a single supernatural ability), or be a super social capable of mind control by skill and not power, the appearance capable of making people kill for just by looking at you (literally).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not about superheroes, it\u2019s about a world full of regular people capable of more than the laws of physics allow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T01:36:25-07:00","id":1321855,"title":"","content":"Aberrant's emphasis is on superhumans, and their interaction with the wider human societies beyond them. It's as much 'what would you do with the power of a god' as 'what would humans do if people with the power of gods showed up'.<br /> <br /> In that, it taps into a particular strain of supers fic, which has become more prominent after the original edition's release, that tries to ask &quot;how would people actually react to having superhumans in their midst?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Its starting point is ten years after the first superhumans (novas) appear, so the initial shock of their appearance has passed, and we get to see some of the ways the world has adapted to them.<br /> <br /> Novas can include superheroes, but it's not limited to them - it can include celebrities, mercenaries, criminals, people who emphasise the 'super' over the 'human', seeing themselves as something apart from humankind, people like Antaeus in the webcomic, who've come to value other priorities than humanity... anyone can become a nova, with their own view of the world.<br /> <br /> Aberrant is one of the very few RPGs in its genre, most supers RPGs looking to emulate superhero comics - off the top of my head, there's Godlike, and Wild Talents and its spinoffs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T11:20:25-07:00","id":1321898,"title":"","content":"KS and the first preview are up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T11:35:46-07:00","id":1321902,"title":"","content":"Aberrant Kickstarter link is <b><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aberrant\" target=\"_blank\">here</a></b> - for anyone looking for it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T12:28:42-07:00","id":1321907,"title":"","content":"Immediate notice is that the timeline is obviously a bit different. The murder of Slider never happened and is instead the murder of some baseline person.<br /> <br /> Also noticed is the fact the construction of an orbital station and the colonization of Mars, though both lack a section in the geography part at this point.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to seeing how things develop as further updates happen.<br /> <br /> I also notice that nothing really is mentioned about US politics, minus the fact that its declared as a Democratic wave in the 2020 elections. While Ican see why they did that I really don't see that happening that way if superpowered beings appeared.<br /> <br /> Really glad to see the Daedalus League and the Queer Alliance both being brought over and given direct timeline mention. I wish that the section on Divis Mal mentioned his partner, as that was a nice mention before.<br /> <br /> Oh, as a random question - did I miss the timeline moment when the Galatea station was built? Obviously it had to be one of the changes in the Aeon timeline as we don't have such a station. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-02-2019, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T13:18:44-07:00","id":1321909,"title":"","content":"Pledged, it\u2019s great so far!<br /> <br /> I like the new timeline, the Aberrants are not the reclusive investigators as before, they are the Bad Guys now (with capital letters), what\u2019s really nice...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T15:28:13-07:00","id":1321934,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for an appendix with rules for playing Novas in other time periods. One or two good pages no illustrations would do. And define the Node-Brain Merit for both the main setting and the Aeon setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T18:22:00-07:00","id":1321946,"title":"","content":"I'm pondering the marketing to non-Trinity/Aberrant players. I'm planning on blogging about the KS, like I did for Trinity. I agree about the importance of the societal emphasis between Novas and Baselines being an important difference to many other 'Supers' settings. Years ago I pitched the game to different players with comments like:<br /> --&gt; &quot;Imagine the X-Men, but then blur the clear answers away.&quot;<br /> --&gt; \u201cCharacters that die are dead!\u201d After the Death of Superman the comics world and character death = gah!<br /> --&gt; \u201cYour career is likely Mega, but it doesn\u2019t have to be. You are likely asked (harassed) to sponsor all sorts and got offered big pay deals\u201d<br /> --&gt; &quot;Having power is great, you've had it for a while, now what? What world would you build and who would you worry about?&quot;<br /> My long-term campaign took a Fatalistically Optimistic tone, the PCs tried to prevent fighting, focusing on psychology and MR research, which eventually led to a Nova Nation, but then things got really complicated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Fireman\u2019s dead! (But is he really?!) MR Node gone. The Aberrants being outright Bad Guys was a bit of a shock. I'm glad things are a bit different, since I already have the old setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I'm really looking forward to seeing how this campaign goes, as well as how the new TC:Aberrant develops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12253-batjutsu","name":"Batjutsu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12253_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T21:07:57-07:00","id":1321969,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, after reading the first part of the manuscript, my reaction is \u201cYeah!\u201d<br /> <br /> I like the Aberrant as the name that became the bad guys on Aeon...<br /> I like the fact that Divis Mal has arms... (hahahahaha)<br /> I like the changes in Teragen as a loose group of novas with no directions or factions, than Aberrant came together after some laws against them...<br /> I like the S\u00e3o Paulo Explosion being a big question but not the center of the metaplot.<br /> I like the space exploration groups that can lead directly to aeon a century latter...<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see the rules in the next few weeks so we can test it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T21:48:26-07:00","id":1321975,"title":"","content":"With the &quot;Aberrants&quot; name taken by Geryon and his ilk, I wonder what happened to people like Andre Corbin and Sophia Rousseau... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T21:57:14-07:00","id":1321976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321975#post1321975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &amp;quot;Aberrants&amp;quot; name taken by Geryon and his ilk, I wonder what happened to people like Andre Corbin and Sophia Rousseau... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Does their faction exist anymore without the sterilization conspiracy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T23:24:44-07:00","id":1321983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321975#post1321975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &amp;quot;Aberrants&amp;quot; name taken by Geryon and his ilk, I wonder what happened to people like Andre Corbin and Sophia Rousseau... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Main autor does not know he's setting? \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> ( Total newby on Trinity) Queer Alliance is what I think? LGBT+ Novas faction? \ud83d\ude2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-02T23:32:48-07:00","id":1321984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Batjutsu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321946#post1321946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aberrants being outright Bad Guys was a bit of a shock. I'm glad things are a bit different, since I already have the old setting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did not read preview yet - but Aberrants seems to be cructial to the setting. How Aberrants are Bad Guys now? Are they not fina\u0142 stage of Novas, after whole Taint from using Quantum powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":".  Edit 07-03-2019, 02:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T00:31:13-07:00","id":1321989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321984#post1321984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did not read preview yet - but Aberrants seems to be cructial to the setting. How Aberrants are Bad Guys now? Are they not fina\u0142 stage of Novas, after whole Taint from using Quantum powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... no. Thanks to the Aberrant War, the term used for novas in Aeon is Aberrants, and it's not helped by the fact the ones who've appeared in the 22nd century appear much less human, physically or mentally, than the ones who left after the War.<br /> <br /> First edition Aberrant had 'Aberrant' originally used as a negative term for novas, then taken by a nova group investigating some of the conspiracies of the setting.<br /> <br /> TC: Aberrant also has 'Aberrant' begin as a negative term for novas, but this time it's taken by a violent Teragen faction (the Teragen being a philosophy that holds novas are a separate species from baseline humans, and not subject to human laws or mores).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T00:34:45-07:00","id":1321991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321975#post1321975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &quot;Aberrants&quot; name taken by Geryon and his ilk, I wonder what happened to people like Andre Corbin and Sophia Rousseau... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>I idly note there're a couple of messages from (or apparently from) Sophia in the first preview, one of which is addressed to someone she calls 'pretty boy'. the other telling Project Utopia's Director she's embedded Team Tonight monitors in among Utopian elements patrolling the outer border of the Israel/Palestine border. Might just be me, but I think she's running Team Tonight, the covert ops counterpart to the Team Tomorrows, and Andre works under her.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T05:47:29-07:00","id":1322014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321984#post1321984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did not read preview yet - but Aberrants seems to be cructial to the setting. How Aberrants are Bad Guys now? Are they not fina\u0142 stage of Novas, after whole Taint from using Quantum powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrant is now Geryon's faction. They used to be Nova Vigilance.<br /> <br /> And honestly I think calling them &quot;the bad guys&quot; is a little... simplistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T08:16:50-07:00","id":1322030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321975#post1321975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the &quot;Aberrants&quot; name taken by Geryon and his ilk, I wonder what happened to people like Andre Corbin and Sophia Rousseau... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw one email from Rousseau as a shadow agent from Utopia (probably) (page 31)! Don\u2019t come to us with your trickery!<br /> <br /> I loved the way many of our known novas are back on different roles, Fireman as The Hero is awesome, Leviathan having a thing for people with scales made me laught, London Fog as a LGBTQ leader (formerly she was born a man, probably gay, who turn into a complete female body with eruption).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T08:21:56-07:00","id":1322033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322014#post1322014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aberrant is now Geryon's faction. They used to be Nova Vigilance.<br /> <br /> And honestly I think calling them &amp;quot;the bad guys&amp;quot; is a little... simplistic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It\u2019s really simplistic... they started defending their rights as humans to came and go, of course being super powered and racists (racists against baselines), they became a group to be feared by baselines, even not killing novas, so bad guys is a simplistic but still proper description of the Aberrants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T09:13:47-07:00","id":1322041,"title":"","content":"That reminds me, I think there should be room for a faction in the setting that rejects the separate-species/separatist-supremacist ethos of Teragen, but is willing to use force to defend Nova\u2019s rights from repression, and reject Project Utopia as an attempt to control the Nova population. Thar\u2019s what my table made Aberrant in 1e, once we were past the one conspiracy investigation plot line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T09:15:50-07:00","id":1322042,"title":"","content":"Remember...if you look to the chapters as listed in the KS, there is a settings secret chapters. That is going to be the exciting part for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T11:15:32-07:00","id":1322064,"title":"","content":"I notice the pledge tier where you could add your own NPC burned out almost instantly... too bad my paycheck doesn't come till later this week","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T11:15:35-07:00","id":1322065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322041#post1322041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, I think there should be room for a faction in the setting that rejects the separate-species/separatist-supremacist ethos of Teragen, but is willing to use force to defend Nova\u2019s rights from repression, and reject Project Utopia as an attempt to control the Nova population. Thar\u2019s what my table made Aberrant in 1e, once we were past the one conspiracy investigation plot line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Project Utopia still doing the \u201ccontrol the Nova population\u201d thing in 2e? I'm pretty sure that the whole \u201csterilize Novas\u201d thing didn't make the transition from 1e to 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T11:17:04-07:00","id":1322066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322064#post1322064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I notice the pledge tier where you could add your own NPC burned out almost instantly... too bad my paycheck doesn't come till later this week</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't have to pay for anything until the KS is over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T11:30:58-07:00","id":1322070,"title":"","content":"True enough, but I prefer to have the money where I can see it before I commit to ANYTHING.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T11:50:35-07:00","id":1322073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322065#post1322065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Project Utopia still doing the \u201ccontrol the Nova population\u201d thing in 2e? I'm pretty sure that the whole \u201csterilize Novas\u201d thing didn't make the transition from 1e to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sterilization, no - but there is still plenty of room for ambiguity in-setting as to whether Utopia is meant to serve as a regulatory check on Nova\u2019s personal ambitions, harnessing them toward a collective good instead.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t mean population numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T12:33:25-07:00","id":1322082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1321984#post1321984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did not read preview yet - but Aberrants seems to be cructial to the setting. How Aberrants are Bad Guys now? Are they not fina\u0142 stage of Novas, after whole Taint from using Quantum powers?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Breaking it down:<ul><li>&quot;Aberrant&quot; is a slur used against novas, something like how &quot;mutie&quot; is used against mutants in the Marvel Universe. By the time of Aeon, &quot;Aberrant&quot; is used near-universally in place of &quot;nova.&quot;</li> <li>In 1e, &quot;Aberrants&quot; was picked up as an ironic name by a Project Utopia offshoot group who wanted to expose the corruption within Utopia.</li> <li>In TC: Aberrant, the &quot;Aberrants&quot; are instead a violent terrorist group within the Teragen made up of the most inhuman monsters, named thus partly because they're trying to reclaim the slur, partly because they're trying to embody it.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T12:50:19-07:00","id":1322086,"title":"","content":"I really like the change on Aberrants. I think its a nifty change from the previous edition. <br /> <br /> I always thought it was weird that the game was called Aberrant when nobody in the actual game really used that term, but reading the timeline chapter there are ways that showcase how it fits and I like that. <br /> <br /> Changes like this are brilliant, and I am glad you were willing and open to make them. I look forward to seeing what comes next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T13:47:40-07:00","id":1322101,"title":"","content":"Are Aberrations going to be covered in the same chapter as Quantum Powers and Abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T16:14:36-07:00","id":1322117,"title":"","content":"One thing that always disturbed me in 1e was that the metaplot of Aberrant was useless in the long run.<br /> <br /> I mean, the sterilisation of novas would have some effects on the plot flow if the Aberrant war was not so close, and all the investigation on the Utopia end up as nothing when Aeon is back and even stronger after the war. It\u2019s not that it sounds implausible, actually it\u2019s one of the most plausible parts of the entire plot, but we as Novas are just... powerless... on the entire metaplot.<br /> <br /> We were not the main characters of the metaplot, obviously, and we can\u2019t change it, but the things we are working on are meaningless in the long run, nobody in Trinity recall the utopian sterilisation process, or the murder of Slider, or the fact that a Nova run for president. Probably the Antaeus plot (from 1e) was the one that would bring the long term results.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the new plot have a much strong appeal as it is about the rise of Aberrants against baseline, and how the acts of a few people created started the domino effect that end in a war declaration less than 20 years after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T17:11:35-07:00","id":1322121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322117#post1322117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that always disturbed me in 1e was that the metaplot of Aberrant was useless in the long run.<br /> <br /> I mean, the sterilisation of novas would have some effects on the plot flow if the Aberrant war was not so close, and all the investigation on the Utopia end up as nothing when Aeon is back and even stronger after the war. It\u2019s not that it sounds implausible, actually it\u2019s one of the most plausible parts of the entire plot, but we as Novas are just... powerless... on the entire metaplot.<br /> <br /> We were not the main characters of the metaplot, obviously, and we can\u2019t change it, but the things we are working on are meaningless in the long run, nobody in Trinity recall the utopian sterilisation process, or the murder of Slider, or the fact that a Nova run for president. Probably the Antaeus plot (from 1e) was the one that would bring the long term results.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the new plot have a much strong appeal as it is about the rise of Aberrants against baseline, and how the acts of a few people created started the domino effect that end in a war declaration less than 20 years after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone keeps saying how they were powerless in the old metaplot, but I don\u2019t get that. Our characters in almost all our games became movers and shakers in the world. I\u2019ve had more than one character that could fight Pax to a standstill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T17:15:26-07:00","id":1322122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322101#post1322101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Aberrations going to be covered in the same chapter as Quantum Powers and Abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it\u2019s on the New Rules chapter, as Quantum Flux, Space and other specific rules were inserted in Aeon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T17:19:08-07:00","id":1322123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322121#post1322121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone keeps saying how they were powerless in the old metaplot, but I don\u2019t get that. Our characters in almost all our games became movers and shakers in the world. I\u2019ve had more than one character that could fight Pax to a standstill.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, in my opinion, its because WE knew how it would end if the ST didn't do something to stop it. It would end in fire and war and great destruction. The future was already written and considered pretty much inescapable. Which isn't really the stuff that makes one feel powerful.<br /> <br /> I remember, in the many games of Aberrant I played in or ran the ST had to specify that the future was unwritten, that despite what was said in the books the players were in fact powerful enough to change things if they wanted. But this was always a sort of &quot;hey, just so you know how it is going in this game&quot; rather than an automatic assumption. Which it should be. Especially in a game about superpowered people, of people who now have the power and the ability to use it to change the world.<br /> <br /> Which is why the idea of the Continuum is PERFECT. We know the potential of one future, the one where the Aberrant War happens and ushers in an age of psions, but we also know that this world might be a different one. It also allows for in-game reasons for parallel and dimensional travel and vision, and that is brilliant.<br /> <br /> At least this is my opinion.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> On Aberrations, I hope they remain as I always liked them. I remember going through the book and picking the ones I liked the most for whatever character I was playing. I especially liked the ones that let me be different, but also improved in a small physical sense.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Actually, this leads to a question I was curious about, soo Aberrant fans, where are you the appearance of nova characters. Do you prefer more inhuman or human in appearances. <br /> <br /> For me I prefer human looking, though I don't mind (actually I like) supernal beauty for my characters, that is they seem like perfect humans. But honestly none of my characters were inhuman in appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-03-2019, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T17:25:03-07:00","id":1322124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322121#post1322121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone keeps saying how they were powerless in the old metaplot, but I don\u2019t get that. Our characters in almost all our games became movers and shakers in the world. I\u2019ve had more than one character that could fight Pax to a standstill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t get me wrong, the characters can be pretty strong and change the world, but the old Aberrant Metaplot had nothing to do with the Trinity Universe metaplot.<br /> <br /> Adventure was about the rise of Aeon Society, exploring the world and how the heroes form the pilot adventures would became the super heroes from the future.<br /> Trinity was about what happens in the world with the return of the monsters from the past.<br /> Aberrant shoud be about the super heroes become the monsters, but it\u2019s about murder investigation, some cults of personalities, things that get minor as the war arrive. It\u2019s could be more about the rise of Teragen, the fall of Utopia, the rise of baselines against novas, things like that, things that would have meaning dealing or explaining the war that came next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T17:35:27-07:00","id":1322126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322123#post1322123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this leads to a question I was curious about, soo Aberrant fans, where are you the appearance of nova characters. Do you prefer more inhuman or human in appearances. <br /> <br /> For me I prefer human looking, though I don't mind (actually I like) supernal beauty for my characters, that is they seem like perfect humans. But honestly none of my characters were inhuman in appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the liminal human appearance. Things that make the Nova not human but is not completely inhuman, for example:<br /> - weird colours in skin and hair<br /> - flaming/bright eyes<br /> - elemental hair (fire, shadow, smoke, etc)<br /> - 2,30m tall but perfect body proportions<br /> - over muscular (hulk like)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T17:39:37-07:00","id":1322129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322123#post1322123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, in my opinion, its because WE knew how it would end if the ST didn't do something to stop it. It would end in fire and war and great destruction. The future was already written and considered pretty much inescapable. Which isn't really the stuff that makes one feel powerful.<br /> <br /> I remember, in the many games of Aberrant I played in or ran the ST had to specify that the future was unwritten, that despite what was said in the books the players were in fact powerful enough to change things if they wanted. But this was always a sort of &quot;hey, just so you know how it is going in this game&quot; rather than an automatic assumption. Which it should be. Especially in a game about superpowered people, of people who now have the power and the ability to use it to change the world.<br /> <br /> Which is why the idea of the Continuum is PERFECT. We know the potential of one future, the one where the Aberrant War happens and ushers in an age of psions, but we also know that this world might be a different one. It also allows for in-game reasons for parallel and dimensional travel and vision, and that is brilliant.<br /> <br /> At least this is my opinion.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> On Aberrations, I hope they remain as I always liked them. I remember going through the book and picking the ones I liked the most for whatever character I was playing. I especially liked the ones that let me be different, but also improved in a small physical sense.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Actually, this leads to a question I was curious about, soo Aberrant fans, where are you the appearance of nova characters. Do you prefer more inhuman or human in appearances.<br /> <br /> For me I prefer human looking, though I don't mind (actually I like) supernal beauty for my characters, that is they seem like perfect humans. But honestly none of my characters were inhuman in appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322124#post1322124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong, the characters can be pretty strong and change the world, but the old Aberrant Metaplot had nothing to do with the Trinity Universe metaplot.<br /> <br /> Adventure was about the rise of Aeon Society, exploring the world and how the heroes form the pilot adventures would became the super heroes from the future.<br /> Trinity was about what happens in the world with the return of the monsters from the past.<br /> Aberrant shoud be about the super heroes become the monsters, but it\u2019s about murder investigation, some cults of personalities, things that get minor as the war arrive. It\u2019s could be more about the rise of Teragen, the fall of Utopia, the rise of baselines against novas, things like that, things that would have meaning dealing or explaining the war that came next.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it's just the kind of group I roll in. We've always taken metaplot as a suggestion. We pick a part of it that we like, then the rest can happen or not as we please. And our characters can always kick the thing in the teeth.<br /> <br /> Actually I've never understood <i>anyone's</i> complaints about metaplot, really. Who cares if the books say something happens? They're not running the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T21:04:39-07:00","id":1322150,"title":"","content":"My impression right now is the Aberrant to Aeon timeline is \u201ccanon\u201d in so far as it is what officially happens if the player characters do nothing. But the game assumes the actions of PCs can absolutely overt the Aberrant War or change its outcome, etc etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T22:39:50-07:00","id":1322157,"title":"","content":"&quot;America has had enough of 'celebrity politicians'&quot; -Randall Portman.<br /> <br /> Well Done *slow clap*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-03T23:33:43-07:00","id":1322164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322150#post1322150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression right now is the Aberrant to Aeon timeline is \u201ccanon\u201d in so far as it is what officially happens if the player characters do nothing. But the game assumes the actions of PCs can absolutely avert the Aberrant War or change its outcome, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aberrant timeline deviated from the \u201caction\u201d timeline described in the Trinity core book last year, if not earlier (I don't know when the Galatea space station was launched in the Aberrant timeline, and it may yet to be launched in the Action timeline for all I know; but the Action timeline definitely doesn't have the Fireman Erupting in 2018); so it isn't just empty words that the future isn't written; it's demonstrably true. I'm hoping for a box somewhere in the text that makes this explicit \u2014 if not in Aberrant, then in Adventure, spelling out that Action and Aberrant are two possible futures of the Adventure setting, and maybe spelling it exactly when the divergences point occurred. <br /> <br /> I'm also interested in maybe seeing some settings set in the future of the Action timeline showing how it might end up developing without the Nova Age throwing everything for a loop. Maybe some notes in the Anima setting to describe how it might be recast as a future of the Action timeline? My point is that you've got a Continuum; you should use it as more than just a talking point or a bit of color. Actually develop multiple branches in the Continuum instead of concentrating everything into the Adventure-to-Aeon timestream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T00:00:55-07:00","id":1322167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322164#post1322164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Aberrant timeline deviated from the \u201caction\u201d timeline described in the Trinity core book last year, if not earlier (I don't know when the Galatea space station was launched in the Aberrant timeline, and it may yet to be launched in the Action timeline for all I know; but the Action timeline definitely doesn't have the Fireman Erupting in 2018); so it isn't just empty words that the future isn't written; it's demonstrably true. I'm hoping for a box somewhere in the text that makes this explicit \u2014 if not in Aberrant, then in Adventure, spelling out that Action and Aberrant are two possible futures of the Adventure setting, and maybe spelling it exactly when the divergences point occurred.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in maybe seeing some settings set in the future of the Action timeline showing how it might end up developing without the Nova Age throwing everything for a loop. Maybe some notes in the Anima setting to describe how it might be recast as a future of the Action timeline? My point is that you've got a Continuum; you should use it as more than just a talking point or a bit of color. Actually develop multiple branches in the Continuum instead of concentrating everything into the Adventure-to-Aeon timestream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ian <a href=\"https://twitter.com/VonAether/status/962557821542916096\" target=\"_blank\">mentioned on Twitter</a> last year that there'd be some settings that don't fit quite so neatly into the main timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T00:02:57-07:00","id":1322170,"title":"","content":"Your Twitter link isn't working for me right now, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T00:25:00-07:00","id":1322172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322150#post1322150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression right now is the Aberrant to Aeon timeline is \u201ccanon\u201d in so far as it is what officially happens if the player characters do nothing. But the game assumes the actions of PCs can absolutely overt the Aberrant War or change its outcome, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A more accurate way to look at it would be - Aberrant is the \u2018canon\u2019 history of AEon, AEon isn\u2019t the \u2018canon\u2019 future of Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 07-04-2019, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T01:10:59-07:00","id":1322183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322164#post1322164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Aberrant timeline deviated from the \u201caction\u201d timeline described in the Trinity core book last year, if not earlier (I don't know when the Galatea space station was launched in the Aberrant timeline, and it may yet to be launched in the Action timeline for all I know; but the Action timeline definitely doesn't have the Fireman Erupting in 2018); so it isn't just empty words that the future isn't written; it's demonstrably true. I'm hoping for a box somewhere in the text that makes this explicit \u2014 if not in Aberrant, then in Adventure, spelling out that Action and Aberrant are two possible futures of the Adventure setting, and maybe spelling it exactly when the divergences point occurred.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in maybe seeing some settings set in the future of the Action timeline showing how it might end up developing without the Nova Age throwing everything for a loop. Maybe some notes in the Anima setting to describe how it might be recast as a future of the Action timeline? My point is that you've got a Continuum; you should use it as more than just a talking point or a bit of color. Actually develop multiple branches in the Continuum instead of concentrating everything into the Adventure-to-Aeon timestream.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the caveat that, although Dataweaver likes to use &quot;Action&quot; to refer to the core rulebook setting, that is not anything official, and none of us use it internally:<br /> <br /> The core setting is intentionally much more vague than the other eras. We paint a broad brush and suggest a lot, but there's no strict timeline of events like you find in the setting sections of Aberrant or Aeon. It's much more of a toolbox for playing a certain kind of game, while the other eras are more specific settings.<br /> <br /> The core is set &quot;now,&quot; but it's a very general now. You can certainly decide to set your game in 2019 or 2020 with no novas, just as easily as you can set it in the 1980s.<br /> <br /> The closest we get to reporting on any specific dates is the section with the in-world artifacts at the front. Newspaper clippings, transcripts, pamphlets, etc. The furthest date is a single article from August 2018, but not including that, the latest is early March 2018, before the Galatea explosion.<br /> <br /> So while the core doesn't explicitly call out the Galatea or novas, there's nothing there which particularly contradicts it either. Aeon, Aberrant, and Adenture! are specific flashpoints, &quot;nodes&quot; on a timeline. That sort of thing happens to the timestream when there's a massive flux event. The core setting is not one of these nodes: it's more of a cloud of possibility.<br /> <br /> Anyway tl;dr: play the game you wanna play, I'm not the boss of you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T04:34:08-07:00","id":1322196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322041#post1322041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, I think there should be room for a faction in the setting that rejects the separate-species/separatist-supremacist ethos of Teragen, but is willing to use force to defend Nova\u2019s rights from repression, and reject Project Utopia as an attempt to control the Nova population. Thar\u2019s what my table made Aberrant in 1e, once we were past the one conspiracy investigation plot line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I so strongly agree. After all, since Novas can have Mega-Intelegence some of them should get it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T06:36:29-07:00","id":1322211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322183#post1322183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while the core doesn't explicitly call out the Galatea or novas, there's nothing there which particularly contradicts it either. Aeon, Aberrant, and Adenture! are specific flashpoints, &amp;quot;nodes&amp;quot; on a timeline. That sort of thing happens to the timestream when there's a massive flux event. The core setting is not one of these nodes: it's more of a cloud of possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s exactly the point I was about to set when reading Dataweaver post. Not everything is about Novas, even in the 2020s the Nova population is about 2k, \u2153 or less than 1e 2008, what means Novas do stuff and change the world, but they are far from being everywhere.<br /> <br /> Thinking about the Media Res stories, they would fit anytime up to 2025ish as tech would start to make everything a bit different, OPnet reaching everywhere all time, faster transportation, things like that. The novas themselves can be totally avoided by not being in a big city or in an area of interest of Utopia or Teragen. Of course the invasion from another dimension would be really hard with an army of novas defending, but still...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T14:57:05-07:00","id":1322287,"title":"","content":"Aberrations are what I want to see. What physical and mental deformities will occur and why? What are the effects of Quantum? Also, will the powers section include things that require a higher Quantum rating?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T15:38:51-07:00","id":1322295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322287#post1322287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aberrations are what I want to see. What physical and mental deformities will occur and why? What are the effects of Quantum? Also, will the powers section include things that require a higher Quantum rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>The interview posted this morning had Steve and Ian saying that all tiers of play will be supported by the core book, which implies that high Quantum powers will be in there. There are Psi 6 &amp; 7 powers in Aeon, so that'd make sense.<br /> <br /> That said, apparently Quantum 10 isn't a thing. Someone who gets to Quantum 10 goes... away, per Steve Kenson. I guess they transcend or whatever. So I don't think we're getting Universe Creation again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T16:51:54-07:00","id":1322303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322295#post1322295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, apparently Quantum 10 isn't a thing. Someone who gets to Quantum 10 goes... away, per Steve Kenson. I guess they transcend or whatever. So I don't think we're getting Universe Creation again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is kinda sad. While it is by my experience really unlikely to ever come up, my character of over 10 years is still quite far from it though our ST has been very strict about raising Quantum in general and especially going over 5, it still is quote unfortunate in any game if the ultimate reward is for you to stop playing.<br /> <br /> But at the same time I kinda understand as any character at that point is much more of a force of nature unconstrained by most of the rules of the game. But even though I kinda get the reason behind the decision I still find it to be kind of a let down. But we have to wait and see how things turn out when the final book is out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T16:59:42-07:00","id":1322305,"title":"","content":"I really like how its mentioned that the core book will have all Quantum levels worth of powers in it. Its a nifty way to do it, muxh better than stopping at Quantum 5. <br /> <br /> I wish Quantum went to 11, ten normal and one transcendence. Mostly because the number is more orderly. <br /> <br /> So much fun and interesting facts in this setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T17:46:32-07:00","id":1322314,"title":"","content":"Quantum 5 was not a limit, it just the point where the values went crazy on 1e. On TC, if they follow the same idea of growing power as the quantum rises as they did with Psi, I would say that every point in quantum would have a significant meaning.<br /> <br /> We will have some news in the next few weeks...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T18:10:12-07:00","id":1322320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322314#post1322314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quantum 5 was not a limit, it just the point where the values went crazy on 1e. On TC, if they follow the same idea of growing power as the quantum rises as they did with Psi, I would say that every point in quantum would have a significant meaning.<br /> <br /> We will have some news in the next few weeks...</div> </div> </div> </div>Quantum 5 was the last power level in the core rulebook though. The higher ones didn't come out till expansions. Which isn't bad, its just cool that they are present in the new edition's core. <br /> <br /> I'm really looking forward to all the news and updates and secrets and stuff. Its going to be quite fun! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T18:20:51-07:00","id":1322321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322305#post1322305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like how its mentioned that the core book will have all Quantum levels worth of powers in it. Its a nifty way to do it, muxh better than stopping at Quantum 5.<br /> <br /> I wish Quantum went to 11, ten normal and one transcendence. Mostly because the number is more orderly.<br /> <br /> So much fun and interesting facts in this setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Yeah...but...<i>this</i> Nova goes all the way up to 11!&quot; <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://memegenerator.net/instance/72288576/spinal-tap-but-james-this-one-goes-to-eleven\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://memegenerator.net/instance/72288576/spinal-tap-but-james-this-one-goes-to-eleven\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://memegenerator.net/instance/72288576/spinal-tap-but-james-this-one-goes-to-eleven\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T22:17:37-07:00","id":1322335,"title":"","content":"Thus far, any reference to the Directive shows them being a far more formidable organization this time around. With the various political superpowers all supporting the group officially or unofficially hoping for a failsafe, they'll probably be an even bigger problem than Proteus could ever be.<br /> <br /> I notice Anteus's personality is much more distanced than it was before, much more focused on the integrity of the ecosystem to the exclusion of whatever else is happening. I like it. He's like a Teragen Portent without actually being Teragen! (assuming that aspect of Teras/Chrysalis even remains)<br /> <br /> I can't wait till they get around to updating us with the completed power list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T22:27:54-07:00","id":1322338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322335#post1322335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thus far, any reference to the Directive shows them being a far more formidable organization this time around. With the various political superpowers all supporting the group officially or unofficially hoping for a failsafe, they'll probably be an even bigger problem than Proteus could ever be.<br /> <br /> I notice Anteus's personality is much more distanced than it was before, much more focused on the integrity of the ecosystem to the exclusion of whatever else is happening. I like it. He's like a Teragen Portent without actually being Teragen! (assuming that aspect of Teras/Chrysalis even remains)<br /> <br /> I can't wait till they get around to updating us with the completed power list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recall Antaeus always being like that. There was one bit in... Project Utopia I think... that said he was aware of the sterilization conspiracy but thought it was beneath his notice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-04T23:23:12-07:00","id":1322344,"title":"","content":"Been working 70 hour weeks and I raise my head and we have an Aberrant Kickstarter, sweet! Just signed up on the Kick Starter and I am very excited to see Aberrant underway.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T10:20:56-07:00","id":1322449,"title":"","content":"On my 3rd re-read I paid more attention to the document presenting the DHS complaints about the US hiring on it's own nova-force. I might have argued till I thought of the embarrassing morass of legal BS and political red tape they wrap themselves in. The crowdfunding thing is hilarious in how feasible it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:01:38-07:00","id":1322455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322449#post1322449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On my 3rd re-read I paid more attention to the document presenting the DHS complaints about the US hiring on it's own nova-force. I might have argued till I thought of the embarrassing morass of legal BS and political red tape they wrap themselves in. The crowdfunding thing is hilarious in how feasible it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh<br /> Oh!<br /> <br /> <br /> I just realized something...<br /> <br /> The US government can\u2019t afford to employ Nova national security forces given what the private sector pays.<br /> <br /> So the US government is forced to contract out to companies to employ Elites.<br /> <br /> Resulting in the privatization of the US military, and the groundwork for the FSA!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:25:29-07:00","id":1322461,"title":"","content":"Makes a lot of sense, since the Army can\u2019t contract people directly except through the regular ways (service, military selection, etc). Novas, even if they have to service, would be for a year and eventually they would join mercenary groups (for money and flexibility).<br /> <br /> It would be an international reality, as far as I know no army can contract employees as regular companies do, they need to do Via 3rd party companies, so that\u2019s why elites rule the battlefield.<br /> <br /> The focus on the military for overpower other countries would force US to employ a larger number of Novas, maybe even contract as many Elites as possible to avoid having to fight them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T11:41:11-07:00","id":1322467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322461#post1322461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes a lot of sense, since the Army can\u2019t contract people directly except through the regular ways (service, military selection, etc). Novas, even if they have to service, would be for a year and eventually they would join mercenary groups (for money and flexibility).<br /> <br /> It would be an international reality, as far as I know no army can contract employees as regular companies do, they need to do Via 3rd party companies, so that\u2019s why elites rule the battlefield.<br /> <br /> The focus on the military for overpower other countries would force US to employ a larger number of Novas, maybe even contract as many Elites as possible to avoid having to fight them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me wonder how sustainable it is for China to ruthlessly indoctrinate their citizenry so they can keep their &quot;secret&quot; force of military novas since they definitely don't have infinite resources necessary to try to outbid DeVries (who seem like they'll be WAY more powerful these days). With the sheer population in China, it was a given that the would have enough loyalists to create their EHM like in 1E, but the text seems to indicate that they severely clamp down on ANY nova that erupts in their population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T12:09:47-07:00","id":1322471,"title":"","content":"China has its own monetary power to be able to hire lots of Elitrs, it\u2019s the second market and rising quickly. Also they could ignore the time required to invest in tech (enough to compete with US military tech) by employing lots of Novas directly or thru DeVries.<br /> <br /> We are talking about 2k Novas, if you think most people would not join military or be relevant on combat, we may count the number of elites on a couple hundred, and the real elites are no more than 30. So they salaries are HUGE, but they are not so many to be impossible to keep a good part of them in the pocket...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T15:12:36-07:00","id":1322511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322467#post1322467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes me wonder how sustainable it is for China to ruthlessly indoctrinate their citizenry so they can keep their &amp;quot;secret&amp;quot; force of military novas since they definitely don't have infinite resources necessary to try to outbid DeVries (who seem like they'll be WAY more powerful these days). With the sheer population in China, it was a given that the would have enough loyalists to create their EHM like in 1E, but the text seems to indicate that they severely clamp down on ANY nova that erupts in their population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that in the official history, the Chinese state as we know it will be taken over from within by a Nova and redesigned into social science super-tech that no baseline can comprehend, I assume their current policies aren\u2019t going to work out like they\u2019re hoping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T17:15:26-07:00","id":1322529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322511#post1322511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that in the official history, the Chinese state as we know it will be taken over from within by a Nova and redesigned into social science super-tech that no baseline can comprehend, I assume their current policies aren\u2019t going to work out like they\u2019re hoping.</div> </div> </div> </div>What?!?!? I guess I missed this part...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T17:29:45-07:00","id":1322534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322511#post1322511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that in the official history, the Chinese state as we know it will be taken over from within by a Nova and redesigned into social science super-tech that no baseline can comprehend, I assume their current policies aren\u2019t going to work out like they\u2019re hoping.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322529#post1322529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What?!?!? I guess I missed this part...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh good, I'm not the only one surprised by that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T17:48:36-07:00","id":1322538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322534#post1322534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh good, I'm not the only one surprised by that...</div> </div> </div> </div>*points at the 2e Aeon book*. The Bodhissatva? The super-intelligent Nova that designs the post-People\u2019s Republic Chinese state. And baselines can\u2019t make changes to their government because no one understands how it works - but it does, and they\u2019re afraid the whole thing will come crashing down if they mess with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T19:37:41-07:00","id":1322550,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s one of the things that I erased from my mind to keep it working, now I will have to erase again. That is absolutely crazy, social super tech, a series of laws that work infinitely perfect on the Chinese society and allow the entire system to work...<br /> <br /> I always think on technology as objects, forgetting the fact that technology is the knowledge that allow you to build the things, including the society and human interaction.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reminding, now I need to clean it again or I will not be able to focus on my daily business for a week or so...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-05T23:57:23-07:00","id":1322566,"title":"","content":"I actually don't have the 2e Aeon book to read...but that's pretty efficient. Color me horrified.<br /> <br /> Moving along; I note that the Daedalus League is actually cooperating with Utopia and national governments as opposed to vehemently avoiding them. They always were one of the only consistently good orgs in 1e.<br /> <br /> I also see we finally got over that artificial block on fusion technology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T03:54:04-07:00","id":1322584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322566#post1322566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't have the 2e Aeon book to read...but that's pretty efficient. Color me horrified.<br /> <br /> Moving along; I note that the Daedalus League is actually cooperating with Utopia and national governments as opposed to vehemently avoiding them. They always were one of the only consistently good orgs in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though they had the advantage of getting a writeup late in the line, in the Aberrant Players Guide, the second-to-last book. (That said, Underworld, the last book, could have derailed them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T04:07:04-07:00","id":1322587,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s funny how the space explorers call themselves after the guy who said to his son \u201cDon\u2019t fly to high or you are going to die\u201d, and the son did and died... Now I noticed how stupid you can sound in English with a few not well chosen words...<br /> <br /> Anyway, Daedalus was the first guy who would be able to fly to space, as long he could wait until the night, but he chose not to... not very space explorer as I see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T09:28:46-07:00","id":1322608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322566#post1322566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't have the 2e Aeon book to read...but that's pretty efficient. Color me horrified.<br /> <br /> Moving along; I note that the Daedalus League is actually cooperating with Utopia and national governments as opposed to vehemently avoiding them. They always were one of the only consistently good orgs in 1e.<br /> <br /> I also see we finally got over that artificial block on fusion technology. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? What block on fusion? Hyperfusion was a thing in 1e too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T09:29:14-07:00","id":1322609,"title":"","content":"Well, the name probably sounded impressive to them before, whereas it sounds ironic now. I notice it seems to have been started up by the Karagians rather than Cyrus Katrak. I'm guessing those two were one of the 5 who got in quickly enough to add their characters as npcs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T09:48:15-07:00","id":1322614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322609#post1322609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the name probably sounded impressive to them before, whereas it sounds ironic now. I notice it seems to have been started up by the Karagians rather than Cyrus Katrak. I'm guessing those two were one of the 5 who got in quickly enough to add their characters as npcs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, not from the Aberrant KS; these tiers have always been for subsequent projects, not the project being backed. Waiting until after the KS is done means the backers are 'locked in', so you don't have to worry about someone dropping out during the KS.<br /> <br /> They might come from backers on the <i>Aeon</i> KS, but not Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T10:24:30-07:00","id":1322621,"title":"","content":"On Kickstarter, devs shared <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aberrant/posts/2558062\" target=\"_blank\">their notes on <b>Aeon Society</b> and it's history in <b>Aberrant</b></a> ( and TC in general )! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-06-2019, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T13:48:21-07:00","id":1322637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322550#post1322550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s one of the things that I erased from my mind to keep it working, now I will have to erase again. That is absolutely crazy, social super tech, a series of laws that work infinitely perfect on the Chinese society and allow the entire system to work...<br /> <br /> I always think on technology as objects, forgetting the fact that technology is the knowledge that allow you to build the things, including the society and human interaction.<br /> <br /> Thanks for reminding, now I need to clean it again or I will not be able to focus on my daily business for a week or so...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know I never actually thought of social powers being a sort of technology on its own. That's really nifty. That's really cool. The idea that a nova could design and build a society that works amazingly well on its own and with no novas tending to it, as long as its tenets are followed and baselines don't muddle with it. <br /> <br /> The idea of a nova-designed colony in a space station or another planet using such social tech is now a brilliant concept, one I wish to think on further.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T13:54:03-07:00","id":1322638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322621#post1322621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Kickstarter, devs shared <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aberrant/posts/2558062&amp;quot;]their</a> notes on <b>Aeon Society</b> and it's history in <b>Aberrant</b>[/URL] ( and TC in general )! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit, while I can deal with it in the specific genre context of Adventure!, how much \u201cGuardian Ethos\u201d is at work with the Aeon Society bugs me. Maybe I just have too much LRE in me, but the idea of rich philanthropists being the big heroes of the setting always make my eyes roll.<br /> <br /> For the Trinity Core setting, I reskinned the Global Cartography initiative to make Aeon Society academic explorerers/researchers, who in turn provide data to their sister organizations Triton (who seek to apply the information systemically to do long term good) and Neptune (who seek to apply the information acutely to do good where it is imminently needed) - both of which are established NGOs that do get philanthropic funding, but those donors aren\u2019t their members.<br /> <br /> I just can\u2019t fathom how Mercer and co are supposed to have acquired \u201cfortunes\u201d to fund Aeon adventuring if they weren\u2019t plundering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T14:03:24-07:00","id":1322640,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, only Michael vanishing and Max becoming a recluse kills my preferred image of that fight near the end of WW2: Michael was trying to hijack the first nuclear test to set off N-Day in 1945, he and Max had their all out smack down in the sands of TRINITY New Mexico, until the explosion leaves nothing behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T14:12:01-07:00","id":1322642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322640#post1322640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, only Michael vanishing and Max becoming a recluse kills my preferred image of that fight near the end of WW2: Michael was trying to hijack the first nuclear test to set off N-Day in 1945, he and Max had their all out smack down in the sands of TRINITY New Mexico, until the explosion leaves nothing behind.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay that is really cool. The idea that Michael wanted to establish an N-Day them but was forced to back down due to a fight with Max sounds brilliant.After said fight, Michael, reeling from the battle and the depression of his loss, slinks into the shadows to plan and such. <br /> <br /> I do have to admit that him being a Nazi (or at least working with them, if not actually one of them) never really sat well with me. [That said, him working with them and then realizing what they and he did was not good could lead to why he is a much more hands off person in the Nova Age, minus you know kickstarting* the the whole thing.) So maybe I could have his backstory be that he played both sides against each other in his attempt to gather the exotic materials necessary to create a 1945 N-Day. <br /> <br /> *Okay this just made me think of Michael using Kickstarter to get the resources needed to start N-Day. Everyone thought he was joking or it was a video game that sounded cool but the amount of funding got high enough he was able to bankroll his space station experiments that led to N-Day. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T16:02:34-07:00","id":1322657,"title":"","content":"Michael was not Nazi, he was not fighting for Germany and Max was not fighting for the Allies. I will talk about 1e, what I read and understand.<br /> <br /> Dr Primoris was fighting for himself, he had plans that were not clarified probably related to the rise of superhumans on large scale at the cost of civilians or something like it. Aeon discover the plans and go after him, that\u2019s the further it was discussed on this battle.<br /> <br /> Michael turned into Dr Primoris, even his appearance was enough to take some time for some of Aeon recognise him as a former colleague. Also he was fighting alone (as no army or sidekick was mentioned) against the entire Aeon Society, and they didn\u2019t finish him, they just make it impossible to follow his plan, so he left (he didn\u2019t want to kill them as he was a big fan and friend of them). That made Max see that the future he visited before was fated to happen and made him reclusive, that future is Aberrant War and latter Trinity. Max was expecting a different future, and they had a lot of letters written for the period while Michael was alone in the latter 30s and beginning of 40s, discussing what kind of impact they would cause in the world following the paths that they were heading on...<br /> <br /> TC is different, we may have a very different Michael as Divis is different too... so, he may be Nazi and the Aeon Society may be fighting for the allies... It\u2019s your game...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T16:13:27-07:00","id":1322660,"title":"","content":"So really it makes even more sense that Dr Primoris was using the events of the war, of the Allies and Axis, of the Nazi magic hunting, to gather resources and exotic goods in order to create something like N-Day. He's work was a bit underhanded, sometimes sinister, but never outright evil in the sense of him murdering millions. Still, despite the morally gray element there was enough dark things in his acts that Mercer was forced to stop him, leading to battle, Primoris' loss, the (temporary) end of his N-Day dreams, and him dissapearing once again for a few generations. When he did return, in the 2000s, he did so without the fanfare of his WWII era personality, which was perfect as it allowed him to push matters along so that nobody stopped him (or even realized what he was doing) in 2018, and the whole Galatea explosion leading to N-Day and the rise of the Nova Age.<br /> <br /> Now, obviously, this is all fan made, but its a nifty bit of timeline. It keeps him on the morally gray side of the debate rather than the outright evil side, thankfully. It also explains why he dissapeared and took his time, he was smarting from his loss at the end of WWII. Maybe he also made a promise to Mercer, one he refused to break.<br /> <br /> It also leads to an interesting idea - what would the world be like if the Nova Age occurred in the aftermath of WWII, just as (or right before, depending on the timeline one wants) the Nazi defeat. Said question is just as interesting as what would the world be like if Psions appeared in 2018 and Novas in the 2100s.<br /> <br /> As a note as a huge fan of the character (and his arc) there is no way I am ever going to make <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dr. Michael Daemon Donighal</span></span></span> or Dr Primoris or Divis Mal or whatever further name he decides to call himself an bad guy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T16:23:30-07:00","id":1322663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322660#post1322660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note as a huge fan of the character (and his arc) there is no way I am ever going to make <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dr. Michael Daemon Donighal</span></span></span> or Dr Primoris or Divis Mal or whatever further name he decides to call himself an bad guy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Michael is a good guy... his Ego is as big as his powers or even bigger... but in the end he just want some friends to play with that can handle his games...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T19:46:17-07:00","id":1322688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322609#post1322609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the name probably sounded impressive to them before, whereas it sounds ironic now. I notice it seems to have been started up by the Karagians rather than Cyrus Katrak. I'm guessing those two were one of the 5 who got in quickly enough to add their characters as npcs?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Aberrant 1e</b>, page 13: <i>January 1, 2007: </i>Nova astronaut Janos Karagian walks across the lunar surface without artificial life support gear. Plans are made to send nova astronauts to Mars.<br /> <br /> <b>Aberrant: Project Utopia</b>, page 52: <i>January 1, 2007: </i>Nova astronaut Janice Karagian walks across the lunar surface without artificial life support gear.<br /> <br /> Originally it was almost certainly a typo between books: someone heard &quot;Janos&quot; (probably pronounced with a J and not as &quot;yanos&quot;), misheard it, and copied down the misheard name as Janice.<br /> <br /> For TC:Aberrant, we decided they were twins and went to the moon together..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-06T19:56:34-07:00","id":1322692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322688#post1322688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Aberrant 1e</b>, page 13: <i>January 1, 2007: </i>Nova astronaut Janos Karagian walks across the lunar surface without artificial life support gear. Plans are made to send nova astronauts to Mars.<br /> <br /> <b>Aberrant: Project Utopia</b>, page 52: <i>January 1, 2007: </i>Nova astronaut Janice Karagian walks across the lunar surface without artificial life support gear.<br /> <br /> Originally it was almost certainly a typo between books: someone heard &quot;Janos&quot; (probably pronounced with a J and not as &quot;yanos&quot;), misheard it, and copied down the misheard name as Janice.<br /> <br /> For TC:Aberrant, we decided they were twins and went to the moon together..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea that basically a typo could lead to such an interesting and awesome change is really nifty. I like your solution, for instead of going &quot;well it's obviously a typo so lets pick one&quot; you went &quot;well, there was a typo but you know what that is cool, so lets have them be twins.&quot; So cool. <br /> <br /> I also like it as the work of the setting as being in a contiuum - in some worlds there is only one, though which one varies, but in another world, this world, there are two!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-07T02:35:04-07:00","id":1322726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1322688#post1322688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Aberrant 1e</b>, page 13: <i>January 1, 2007: </i>Nova astronaut Janos Karagian walks across the lunar surface without artificial life support gear. Plans are made to send nova astronauts to Mars.<br /> <br /> <b>Aberrant: Project Utopia</b>, page 52: <i>January 1, 2007: </i>Nova astronaut Janice Karagian walks across the lunar surface without artificial life support gear.<br /> <br /> Originally it was almost certainly a typo between books: someone heard &quot;Janos&quot; (probably pronounced with a J and not as &quot;yanos&quot;), misheard it, and copied down the misheard name as Janice.<br /> <br /> For TC:Aberrant, we decided they were twins and went to the moon together..</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I totally missed that typo somehow, in all the times I've read through that material it just never clicked. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T10:47:30-07:00","id":1323232,"title":"","content":"The character creation chapter is out, and there are some neat things in it \u2014 though the bulk of the good stuff will have to wait until next week. That said, there's a bit in there for those of you who like Talents in TC:Aberrant \u2014 a new Gift that makes it a bit easier for the likes of Batman or Hawkeye to take on Superman or Captain Marvel: \u201cThe Bigger They Are\u2026\u201d This Luck-based Gift lets you reduce an opponent's Scale-based advantage over you, and lets you pierce the overwhelming nature of an advantage of three or more levels of Scale. David vs. Goliath. <br /> <br /> There's also an Edge that allows characters (from the Directive, IIRC) to spend Momentum on a limited form of Dramatic Editing \u2014 namely, to always have exactly what gear you need exactly when you need it. It's available to <i>anyone</i> in the Directive, be they baselines, novas, psychomorphs, or Talents \u2014 though in the case of Talents, it's not so much there to provide a new capability as to provide a different means of paying for it. <br /> <br /> Finally, there's mention of psiads \u2014 though the reader is referred to \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion for details. All that's said is that there are some around during this era, but they're generally conflated with novas, as few outside of the \u00c6on Society are even aware of their existence. Oh, and Margaret Mercer <i>is</i> one. <br /> <br /> Every KS recently had featured a Stretch-Goal \u201ccompanion book\u201d. This one hasn't gotten around to that (yet, I assume); but when (if?) it does, I'm hoping it addresses psiads in the Nova Age in a manner that doesn't require you to pick up TC:\u00c6on in order to play one. Not that I'm opposed to doing so myself, as I already have TC:\u00c6on and will be getting \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion when it comes out; but I don't feel right with forcing fans of Aberrant who <i>aren't</i> fans of \u00c6on to buy a book (or two?) that's largely dedicated to an era they're not interested in just to get access to rules for psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T11:37:12-07:00","id":1323240,"title":"","content":"These references to &quot;Teragen Elders&quot; are making me hungry for a new Teragen supplement. Especially if they are aware of things like Psiads in the nova era (who honestly couldn't have escaped Apothecary's notice for long).<br /> <br /> That crack under transcendence about long-time associates of Aeon, along with some of the text in the manuscript v.1 leads me to believe they've chosen a new direction for Sophia Rousseau. one that's more interesting and long-term.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T12:41:03-07:00","id":1323255,"title":"","content":"I liked that the most recent manuscript update included blurbs about some of the Alligences from the TC Core and how they change with the Nova era. I hope we get a stretch goal that covers them in more detail, and also includes the ones they didn't cover, like Nine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T12:50:49-07:00","id":1323257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323255#post1323255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked that the most recent manuscript update included blurbs about some of the Alligences from the TC Core and how they change with the Nova era. I hope we get a stretch goal that covers them in more detail, and also includes the ones they didn't cover, like Nine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I totally agree. Also I really would like to see how the Global Cartography Society got updated for the Nova Age.<br /> <br /> Oooh, maybe it turns its focus more inward - while the Daedalus Society works to explore outer space the GCS instead begins focusing on parallel and alternate worlds and such. I'm not sure how they would do it but it would totally be cool if they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T13:15:41-07:00","id":1323266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323255#post1323255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked that the most recent manuscript update included blurbs about some of the Alligences from the TC Core and how they change with the Nova era. I hope we get a stretch goal that covers them in more detail, and also includes the ones they didn't cover, like Nine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nine actually became part of the Directive, so it\u2019s covered, but it would be nice to see the others. My favourite is GCS, if I could I would be part of it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T13:56:56-07:00","id":1323274,"title":"","content":"For my part, I\u2019m reading the Transcendence rules and... wondering. About the Fireman, and the S\u00e3o Paulo Blast, and what REALLY happened that day. Just because Utopia is cleaner in this edition doesn\u2019t mean they don\u2019t have ANY secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T14:01:40-07:00","id":1323277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323274#post1323274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my part, I\u2019m reading the Transcendence rules and... wondering. About the Fireman, and the S\u00e3o Paulo Blast, and what REALLY happened that day. Just because Utopia is cleaner in this edition doesn\u2019t mean they don\u2019t have ANY secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to that blast and the Fireman, I can't help but think he didn't die, maybe turned into fire or something. Maybe he learned something he wasn't supposed to know and so took a way out. Or something. <br /> <br /> I just don't think he is dead. I really don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T14:11:21-07:00","id":1323279,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a great \u201cdirty secret\u201d because it\u2019s the kind of thing you might cover up for entirely benign reasons. \u201cRandall was a good man! He was my friend! He deserves to be remembered as the hero he was, not the violently insane walking explosion he is now!\u201d But when the public finds out that Proteus is keeping the world\u2019s most beloved Nova locked away in a secret underground lab... oh man. (I don\u2019t know if the designers will take things in this direction, but I\u2019m definitely keeping it in mind for my campaign. If I ever get a chance to run one....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T14:41:35-07:00","id":1323286,"title":"","content":"While the idea that Randall is being detained in order to protect him from himself is interesting, and quite a flip on things, didn't the event happen first and then he arrived. He wasn't there when it started, so he couldn't be the one to cause it. At least not blatently.<br /> <br /> That said I do like the idea that the use of his powers to stop the blast was sooooooooo extreme it bumped him a bunch of levels in Transcendence to the point he became fire, his old body turned to dust, and he is now trying to slowly bring himself back into a more corporal form.<br /> <br /> He becomes the voice in the flames, or something like that. hehe<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> A random idea came to me from reading posts on the internet. Imagine novas saying something like &quot;If you plan on having anti-nova laws in your country then expect there to be no rain.&quot; <br /> <br /> Even more novas attached to UN or Utopia or national forces could work to make sure their allied forces have good weather and the enemy doesn't, etc. <br /> <br /> I think such things would create ripples of change that could make the world different in time. <br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> By the way, so one of the things I noticed that I am not really a fan of is that in order to purchase new powers and such with XP one must max powers. As I am not really a fan of Flux and such I will probably remove that requirement and just allow players to purchase new powers with XP as normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-09-2019, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T15:27:51-07:00","id":1323294,"title":"","content":"I really agree regarding Flux. No way to mitigate Transcendence, the Teragen's Crysalis actively pushing for Terats to gain more Transcendence. The way it's described is basically Taint 2.0. Flux needing to be gained to increase powers (as you gain Flux from Maxing a power and you need to Max a power in order to increase it). All of that makes it feel... just awful.<br /> <br /> So far it's the only thing I actually dislike. Some things I disagree with, but not enough to call it dislike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","user":"Bulshock","date":". 07-09-2019, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T15:43:02-07:00","id":1323296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bulshock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323294#post1323294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really agree regarding Flux. No way to mitigate Transcendence, the Teragen's Crysalis actively pushing for Terats to gain more Transcendence. The way it's described is basically Taint 2.0.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah. That\u2019s what it is. They never said they were dropping the concept of taint, just the word because of puerile giggling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T15:52:51-07:00","id":1323297,"title":"","content":"I think the real problem is you need months to get free of flux. If you can cool down for a few days and reset your Flux you could work it out with dormancy and not overusing quantum.<br /> <br /> That text about a secret identity is kind of stupid, secret identity that you use for 2 months is YOUR IDENTITY, and being a Nova is the thing you do once in a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T15:56:57-07:00","id":1323299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323297#post1323297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the real problem is you need months to get free of flux. If you can cool down for a few days and reset your Flux you could work it out with dormancy and not overusing quantum.<br /> <br /> That text about a secret identity is kind of stupid, secret identity that you use for 2 months is YOUR IDENTITY, and being a Nova is the thing you do once in a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>... You do realize that &quot;secret identity&quot; refers to a super hero's civilian identity, their everyday, &quot;real&quot; self, right?<br /> <br /> It's a secret because they're hiding the fact that, yeah, the go out and do superhero stuff periodically.<br /> <br /> The blurb &quot;Why have a secret identity,&quot; is saying &quot;Why keep the fact that you're a nova a secret?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T16:45:23-07:00","id":1323309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323299#post1323299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... You do realize that &amp;quot;secret identity&amp;quot; refers to a super hero's civilian identity, their everyday, &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; self, right?<br /> <br /> It's a secret because they're hiding the fact that, yeah, the go out and do superhero stuff periodically.<br /> <br /> The blurb &amp;quot;Why have a secret identity,&amp;quot; is saying &amp;quot;Why keep the fact that you're a nova a secret?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood what I mean, I mean exactly that, your secret identity is your baseline, but if you spends 99% of the time as a baseline your true identity is that.<br /> <br /> Pax, working every day for 10 years, would be at Trancendence 10 by now because he will botch every once in a while, probably 1 a day? Max out once a week? In 2 weeks you got 1 trancendence. If you don\u2019t relax for 5 months every 1 week of work, you are going to turn into a monster very fast. Do it for 10 years and...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T16:55:33-07:00","id":1323315,"title":"","content":"Yeah, even if he only botches or maxes two to three times a week that is still half a month of down time per week of work or more. Or months at a time at only half power. It's an insane rate of gain. There should have been hundreds of novas who have reached Transcendence 10 by now, especially among T2M, the Teragen, and the Elites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T17:16:04-07:00","id":1323316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323309#post1323309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You misunderstood what I mean, I mean exactly that, your secret identity is your baseline, but if you spends 99% of the time as a baseline your true identity is that.<br /> <br /> Pax, working every day for 10 years, would be at Trancendence 10 by now because he will botch every once in a while, probably 1 a day? Max out once a week? In 2 weeks you got 1 trancendence. If you don\u2019t relax for 5 months every 1 week of work, you are going to turn into a monster very fast. Do it for 10 years and...</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, that's how the term is used in the genre that this game is based on. Superman's secret identity is Clark Kent. Batman's secret identity is Bruce Wayne. Iron Man's secret identity used to be Tony Stark, but then he told everyone so he doesn't have one anymore.<br /> <br /> That's what &quot;secret identity&quot; means. That the super's identity is a secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T17:40:00-07:00","id":1323318,"title":"","content":"I just went to Aberrant 1e to check, because, as I remembered, the main reason to get taint was lack of quantum points. On 1e you had to botch the roll you used to Max out the power (and you had to spend will power to that, what limited you a lot). So most of the permanent taint my characters had came from buying powers on reduced rate, what is pretty controlled...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T17:47:55-07:00","id":1323321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323316#post1323316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, that's how the term is used in the genre that this game is based on. Superman's secret identity is Clark Kent. Batman's secret identity is Bruce Wayne. Iron Man's secret identity used to be Tony Stark, but then he told everyone so he doesn't have one anymore.<br /> <br /> That's what &quot;secret identity&quot; means. That the super's identity is a secret.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, not speaking English as main language is getting me wrong...<br /> I know what you mean and I know what the secret identity is... what I mean is, if you are a Nova that don\u2019t want to became a monster in a few months, you need to not be a Nova most of time, and by most of time I mean 99% of the time, so your secret identity is basically the only identity you have.<br /> <br /> Batman works every night, Superman is always ready to leave his clothes behind and save the day, but a Nova will gets a transformation every 2 weeks of working everyday... so Superman is not Superman, he is Clack Kent everyday for 5 months and than he works for a week as Superman and stop again for 5 months more... being Superman is like the thing he does on the Halloween...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T17:57:20-07:00","id":1323324,"title":"","content":"I mean, not necessarily? You're overestimating the likelihood of botches and the volume of rolls they'd typically make, in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T18:05:06-07:00","id":1323327,"title":"","content":"It's not just botches, Aiden. Any time you Max a power you automatically gain a Flux. If Maxing is seen like it was in 1E, i.e. your signature use of that power, then you can expect most novas that are utilizing their powers to a high degree daily would be Maxing them several times a week.You don't have to botch nearly as much as you're thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T19:28:56-07:00","id":1323339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323255#post1323255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked that the most recent manuscript update included blurbs about some of the Alligences from the TC Core and how they change with the Nova era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I was happy we managed to get those in there. Given how close the core setting and Aberrant are, a lot of those Allegiance are probably still active, and we wanted to provide some additional utility. I know some people will be tempted to just use the core rules and ignore the rest as irrelevant for their Aberrant games, so we wanted to show there was more in there that they could use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope we get a stretch goal that covers them in more detail, and also includes the ones they didn't cover, like Nine. </div> </div> </div>If you read the core's writeup on 9, you'll see that they're considering the possibility of working under the UN under the auspices of Directive 9. And Aberrant's Directive sprang from the UN's Directive 9. You've already heard about what happened to 9. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323277#post1323277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When it comes to that blast and the Fireman, I can't help but think he didn't die, maybe turned into fire or something. Maybe he learned something he wasn't supposed to know and so took a way out. Or something.<br /> <br /> I just don't think he is dead. I really don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>By our canon, he ded. He left behind charred remains. He's pretty much the embodiment of the &quot;sacrifice&quot; theme, so we're not eager to subvert that. But if you want to play around with that, by all means, don't let us stop you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T19:54:13-07:00","id":1323344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323339#post1323339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By our canon, he ded. He left behind charred remains. He's pretty much the embodiment of the &amp;quot;sacrifice&amp;quot; theme, so we're not eager to subvert that. But if you want to play around with that, by all means, don't let us stop you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I got so used to all the conspiracy theories that the Fireman being dead sounds like a big lie. I guess I will leave this door close in respect of his symbol in both worlds...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s funny how a character has so much meaning for us even appearing in 4 or 5 lines of text. I guess the 1e Fireman was a big symbol for me even not thinking much about it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T21:09:19-07:00","id":1323363,"title":"","content":"The actual cause of the Sao Paulo blast still stands a potential conspiracy hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T21:12:37-07:00","id":1323364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bulshock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323327#post1323327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just botches, Aiden. Any time you Max a power you automatically gain a Flux. If Maxing is seen like it was in 1E, i.e. your signature use of that power, then you can expect most novas that are utilizing their powers to a high degree daily would be Maxing them several times a week.You don't have to botch nearly as much as you're thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Maxing is more like Captain Marvel going Binary. It\u2019s a BIG DEAL, not something you do several times a week,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T21:13:36-07:00","id":1323365,"title":"","content":"Hm, so Chrysalis no longer actually unravels permanent taint(transcendence) while leaving the social penalties. Pity, I guess maxed out Dormancy is literally the only way to go then.<br /> <br /> I'm liking this Team Tonight. It's probably the thing I like the most about Utopia 2.0, and it seems like it would be the repository of literally every player I've ever run for who tried to do &quot;good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Somehow the Teragen seem more organized with some factions set under others as sub-factions. And it's interesting to have Antaeus contemplating Teras philosophy if not outright supporting it. <br /> <br /> Nice to have some clarification of Caroline Fong's powers since we've literally never know what exactly it was that she did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T21:20:27-07:00","id":1323368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323364#post1323364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Maxing is more like Captain Marvel going Binary. It\u2019s a BIG DEAL, not something you do several times a week,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if this is the same thing but; I remember back in 1e there were instances of novas using &quot;signature moves&quot; (ex; the Fist of Peace, Infinity Justifier, Core Meltdown), but they were referenced in such a way that they were considered separate powers &amp; not really maxing out. If these specific power expressions were built up separately, the novas wouldn't need to max them out anymore (though I imagine it would be a drain on exp to develop something like that) and they might be able to avoid excess flux from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T21:49:03-07:00","id":1323374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323365#post1323365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, so Chrysalis no longer actually unravels permanent taint(transcendence) while leaving the social penalties. Pity, I guess maxed out Dormancy is literally the only way to go then.<br /> <br /> I'm liking this Team Tonight. It's probably the thing I like the most about Utopia 2.0, and it seems like it would be the repository of literally every player I've ever run for who tried to do &quot;good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Somehow the Teragen seem more organized with some factions set under others as sub-factions. And it's interesting to have Antaeus contemplating Teras philosophy if not outright supporting it.<br /> <br /> Nice to have some clarification of Caroline Fong's powers since we've literally never know what exactly it was that she did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the new Proteus. They're still dark as hell without being moustashe twirlers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-09T22:27:14-07:00","id":1323379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bulshock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323327#post1323327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just botches, Aiden. Any time you Max a power you automatically gain a Flux. If Maxing is seen like it was in 1E, i.e. your signature use of that power, then you can expect most novas that are utilizing their powers to a high degree daily would be Maxing them several times a week.You don't have to botch nearly as much as you're thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's wait until we see what Maxing Out actually looks like before we jump to conclusions about how often you would likely use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T02:28:39-07:00","id":1323399,"title":"","content":"People are saying they would abandon Transcendence rules entirely, I would not go that far.<br /> <br /> For Flux gathering: I would keep the Maxing out and quick recover and abandon the botch rule (you will know when you get some Flux because it on propose)<br /> For Flux releasing: I would make 1 week of low power (with test), 3 days now quantum spend or 1 day on dormancy per dot of Flux<br /> <br /> I loved the idea of quantum instability, much better than a sudden transformation, it starts unstable and if you do t cool down for a few days it will be permanent... nice.<br /> Chrysalis should be at any moment you are unstable, not just when you are 10 Flux, otherwise you will get in your cocoon mid fight because you botched twice... that would be a bit... uncomfortable...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T08:22:51-07:00","id":1323449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323374#post1323374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the new Proteus. They're still dark as hell without being moustashe twirlers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They manage to be at least on the necessary side of evil instead of basically catalyzing the thing they hope to prevent. Between them, the new UN-centric Directive, and Team Tonight you have a certain degree of overlap, even though they don't all know they're technically working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T10:48:09-07:00","id":1323468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323374#post1323374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the new Proteus. They're still dark as hell without being moustashe twirlers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm tempted to play a Teragen infiltrator who reports to Proteus.<br /> <br /> The reason he's still there is because he's a born-and-bred Terat; when he's speaking about the necessity of accepting your own godhood, he's not echoing the party line, he's excitedly expounding on his opinions. He just doesn't like the kind of gods he sees other Terats becoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T13:13:01-07:00","id":1323498,"title":"","content":"I don't think most Terats are putting themselves out as gods with the exception of members of Pandaimonion and some of the Cultus Nova. And even of those groups not all of the members are thinking that way. Specifically the Cultus is no longer all about religion, 'The theology of the Cultus Nova is ultimately apotheosis, the notion that each nova has the potential to grow into a god-like being, and the right and responsibility to explore this potential.' which to me sounds much more like Buddhism but without the zen aspects. Pandaimonion is less deeply philosophical and more about hedonism (and is the one whose members actually try to get worshipers).<br /> <br /> But of those two general types (introspective vs. hedonistic) you could make an argument for dislike one of them. Honestly it sounds to me like he's closer to Cultus Nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T13:47:22-07:00","id":1323510,"title":"","content":"I think one of my Storypath Nexus publications will be a bunch of new Allegiances. Should be several built around super-intelligent Novas with various agendas for the world that don\u2019t align with Utopia or Teragen\u2019s forswearing of humanity. Not to mention a Utopia-skeptical activist group against Nova-regulations that are pro-Zurich hardliners who want to be treated EXACTLY legally the same as baselines (that\u2019s what I made \u201cAberrant\u201d in my 1e game after the sterilization plot was resolved).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-10-2019, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T14:04:28-07:00","id":1323513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323510#post1323510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of my Storypath Nexus publications will be a bunch of new Allegiances. Should be several built around super-intelligent Novas with various agendas for the world that don\u2019t align with Utopia or Teragen\u2019s forswearing of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds awesome and something very fun to read. <br /> <br /> I can't help but think of all the advantages that can come from the agenda of a Mega-Intelligent nova, be it corporate (all the things a megacorp can do) or political (much could be done by a union or social group or political party led by one). So yeah, so much options. <br /> <br /> Another idea I had was for a very rich nova who set something up with various other Nova Age organizations to establish something like an mobile orbital station colony or even a cityship with the capability of ground to space flight. (Looking forward to the Quantum Tech chapter for info on such things.)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T15:41:55-07:00","id":1323528,"title":"","content":"I admit, I'd still like to see SOMETHING that could eat away at Trenscendence. Maybe something the opposite of Chrysalis, and you can't have both? Because it sure does seem like anyone involved with Chrysalis is ona greased slide to True Aberrancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T16:22:57-07:00","id":1323537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323528#post1323528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I'd still like to see SOMETHING that could eat away at Trenscendence. Maybe something the opposite of Chrysalis, and you can't have both? Because it sure does seem like anyone involved with Chrysalis is ona greased slide to True Aberrancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that Divis Mal should already be there, if he's the same as he was in 1e. Q8 (5 Transcend), Chrysalis x 3 (3 Transcend), and whatever Transcendence he picked up <i>prior</i> to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T16:33:04-07:00","id":1323540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323528#post1323528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I'd still like to see SOMETHING that could eat away at Trenscendence. Maybe something the opposite of Chrysalis, and you can't have both? Because it sure does seem like anyone involved with Chrysalis is ona greased slide to True Aberrancy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll probably just rework one more kludgy WW/OPP &quot;storytelling&quot; mechanic to suit my needs, personally. Taint/Aberrations/Chrysalis were a right mess in 1e, and this looks to have most of the problems, minus the propensity for people to make dirty jokes when you used the &quot;T word&quot; too many times at 1am after everyone was loaded with red bull.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T16:33:07-07:00","id":1323541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323537#post1323537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue that Divis Mal should already be there, if he's the same as he was in 1e. Q8 (5 Transcend), Chrysalis x 3 (3 Transcend), and whatever Transcendence he picked up <i>prior</i> to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't so much like this as in liking it but I like it cause I think based on rules, its kind of true. Which, in my estimation, makes the whole Transcendence thing utterly ridiculous. <br /> <br /> Which is why I think it either needs to be downplayed or an ability that lets one bleed it off (and which does not involve spending more months not using powers then using powers in a year) at some rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T17:00:40-07:00","id":1323549,"title":"","content":"The rules for Chrysalis in 1e were a kind of cheat code to power up faster than Goku, one year off and I came back to refit you with only my left leg.<br /> <br /> About the Taint, as a non English native, I never knew it had the meaning it has... but instead of Transcendence it could be Corruption, as it was in 1e Taint in Aberrant and Trinity.<br /> <br /> About the rules. It\u2019s hard to predict anything without the power rules, maybe maxing out is really powerful or you hardly roll dice for activating powers, than It\u2019s not a big deal...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T17:23:42-07:00","id":1323551,"title":"","content":"Maybe instead of Flux and Transcendence being two different things just keep it Flux, with both a temporary and permanent rating. Temporary ratings naturally fade at some setting level while permanent ratings require Chrysalis. At Flux 10 the nova's very being is now permanently out of whack with things, which is what makes them unplayable.<br /> <br /> Flux is not a good or bad thing, its not a morality system, its not reaching for a different state, or becoming something else, its also not unnatural, rather it is what happens when beings at our level of existence use energy that is basically much more dynamic and fundamental.<br /> <br /> The whole reason current novas gain Flux at higher Quantum's is because humanity's psychogenetic makeup is not fully ready to tap into the quantum energy source. But a more advanced version of humanity could in theory gain Quantum without gaining Flux, but most of us are not there yet.<br /> <br /> Maybe Divis Mal, by his presence at the Hammersmith Event, is naturally resistant to Flux gain and buildup. Maybe he needs to gain more than 10 temporary flux to make it a point of permanent flux. Maybe permanent flux naturally fades away in time. Just some thoughts.<br /> <br /> The book's three ways of gaining flux remain, but not the requirement that Flux is gained when one learns new Quantum powers.<br /> <br /> Soooo, well, without realizing it I basically just summed up 1e version of Flux, lol. Which is funny as I wasn't a fan of it back then. (And really am not a fan of it now, but I know its not going anywhere, so I figure might as well not try and get them to remove it and instead provide input on its morality nature and the whole idea of a Transcendent 10 nova loosing all emotional ability.) <br /> <br /> Ooh, and I had an idea. If permanent Flux can bleed off imagine a story of a Flux 10 nova suddenly becoming Flux 9, and regaining his more human oriented mindset. Which could be an interesting story seed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-10-2019, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T18:05:30-07:00","id":1323562,"title":"","content":"Mateus Luz, part of the problem comes from having to max out a power in order to advance it. There is also an aberration that causes novas around you to gain Flux and non-Novas to gain Transcendence. Meaning we can potentially have novas that are making the people around them gain aberrations.<br /> <br /> LordHeru, I would personally prefer it where Transcendence 10 didn't make PC's into NPC's, maybe something that plays with Aspirations by giving them an Aspiration that they have to either continually try to fulfill or that would be amazingly hard to fulfill (such as an aspiration to bring all of humanity to the 'next step' ala eruption or similar... which could be one for Mal if he actually triggered N-Day). Calling it Temporary and Permanent Flux also works for me, maybe with Transcendence being 10 because your body stops changing to adapt to the power. At 10 it would also make sense for no longer needing to max a power to increase it, which in turn would make Crysalis a mini Transcendence and overt control over how you change (the latter of which it already is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T18:20:52-07:00","id":1323565,"title":"","content":"I hadn't thought about forced Flux gain and yeah, that is horrible. I would never say to a player &quot;Your character just gained 10 Flux points due to being next to that nova&quot;. I could see using it in a setting element - &quot;You hear rumors of an explosion in some city which seemed to have caused some rapid mutations in the people around there&quot; - but never against a player, be they playing a nova, psiad, talent, or baseline. <br /> <br /> I agree. Making Transcendence 10 characters into NPCs reminds me too much of how in the D6 Star Wars a character that goes to the Dark Side became an NPC. Its a morality system and that never sat well with me. <br /> <br /> That said I do think that there has to be something that happens at a 10 Flux rating, something that makes a player want to not stay in that area. The idea of it being tied to Aspirations could be interesting, especially in tandem with numerous penalties for social interaction with others. Another idea could be the sacrifice of Quantum dots to reduce permanent Flux, with no XP refund. The benefit of Chrysalis is that said reduction can also happen, just without sacrifice. <br /> <br /> I would never require a player to max a power to increase or gain it, so that part isn't for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T18:33:14-07:00","id":1323570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323565#post1323565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't thought about forced Flux gain and yeah, that is horrible. I would never say to a player &quot;Your character just gained 10 Flux points due to being next to that nova&quot;. I could see using it in a setting element - &quot;You hear rumors of an explosion in some city which seemed to have caused some rapid mutations in the people around there&quot; - but never against a player, be they playing a nova, psiad, talent, or baseline.<br /> <br /> I agree. Making Transcendence 10 characters into NPCs reminds me too much of how in the D6 Star Wars a character that goes to the Dark Side became an NPC. Its a morality system and that never sat well with me.<br /> <br /> That said I do think that there has to be something that happens at a 10 Flux rating, something that makes a player want to not stay in that area. The idea of it being tied to Aspirations could be interesting, especially in tandem with numerous penalties for social interaction with others. Another idea could be the sacrifice of Quantum dots to reduce permanent Flux, with no XP refund. The benefit of Chrysalis is that said reduction can also happen, just without sacrifice.<br /> <br /> I would never require a player to max a power to increase or gain it, so that part isn't for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Flux radiation Aberration is there because that's what a lot of Aberrants do in Aeon. They corrupt areas with Flux.<br /> <br /> Also Psiads are immune to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T18:42:35-07:00","id":1323571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323570#post1323570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Flux radiation Aberration is there because that's what a lot of Aberrants do in Aeon. They corrupt areas with Flux.<br /> <br /> Also Psiads are immune to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right but novas aren't and they then gain Flux from it, which could push them over the threshold into another point of Transcendence. Which was the point, it means a nova can be forced into higher levels of Flux against their will. Which is something I am not a fan of. <br /> <br /> Obviously the easiest answer si that a nova is immune to flux gain from any source that is not themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T18:54:56-07:00","id":1323573,"title":"","content":"I like your idea of calling Flux as a neutral word (transcendence is quite good, corruption is bad), but at same time it\u2019s not a good word for what it\u2019s representing. Maybe a name more related to charge or filling would give the idea better... unfortunately I am horrible with words, even in Portuguese...<br /> Corruption came from Cor Ruptus, Brocken Core (technically it\u2019s broken hearth, not the hearth from the feelings, but the hearth core of yourself), it would be a good representation of what the Nova is passing thru, mental or physically.<br /> Other possibility would be Aberrancy, as it\u2019s going out of normal, abnormal, aberrant...<br /> anyway, the name is not the point here... so I will keep Transcendence for the permanent and Flux for the temporary.<br /> <br /> I think that the Transcendence value taking the character out of game is good, not because of the player wanting to keep the character, but because it is hard for the character to be like that, maybe the discomfort that they cause to people around them affect them too.<br /> <br /> If we keep Flux gain and loss in check, an Nova can keep going on balance.<br /> Chrysalis can be the way the Terat deal with the excess of Flux (not the permanent but the temporary), you make the transformation permanent but don\u2019t get more Transcendence, so you are twisted somehow, but don\u2019t feel it (you accept your self, both physically and mentally). The process is the one described in the book, but it don\u2019t require que character being on 10 Flux, just on the quantum instability, the time is locked on the number of times you did it, not your Transcendence value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-10-2019, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T18:57:12-07:00","id":1323574,"title":"","content":"Forced Flux is exactaly what the Aberrants do in Aeon, and becoming a mindless drone is exactaly what means Transcendence 10 in this case...<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a severe transformation, so it\u2019s going to be really rare, supposing a Nova can avoid accumulating Flux on a daily basis...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-10-2019, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:16:51-07:00","id":1323581,"title":"","content":"Maxing out to be able to train the power is not the point, it\u2019s just wrong as I see because it\u2019s not how our body works, we can learne and devolve abilities and knowledge on a daily effort that don\u2019t take us to the limit. Taking to the limit helps, but not that much as it causes fatigue and may even make future training harder.<br /> <br /> The two options for gaining Flux on a natural way is Maxing Out and Rapid Recovery. They represent that extra effort you do to the point you hurt yourself a little (or a lot in the case of Fireman).<br /> <br /> If you can take a week of to handle this every once in a while, it should be ok. Using the rules as we see you need to take a few months off, what is wrong as there are lots of novas that are still in balance.<br /> <br /> I would like to have the rules alloying is to do the same as Fireman, no I don\u2019t want my character to die, Just want to have a chance to do so by an spectacular effort or by a lost of control. So I maybe writing something about it soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-11-2019, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T23:32:16-07:00","id":1323621,"title":"","content":"I see why they went with Flux over Taint, and that\u2019s just fine, though Taint as a name never bothered me much. Transcendence seems like what a Terat might call a permanent Flux rating as it does have a positive connotation. If not Transcendence then, perhaps you might call it Metamorphosis (a more neutral word), or Alienation (which points directly at the deleterious effect they\u2019re drawing attention to)?<br /> <br /> Back in 1e the whole point of Chrysalis was to reduce permanent Taint rating in order to retain sanity/control of oneself. I rather liked the idea of choosing an aberration I might tolerate (enjoy even), and accepting slightly increased social penalties due to being inhuman-looking. The whole system of transforming Chrysalis points into \u201cquasi-xp\u201d that is used to build up quantum abilities, while interesting, wasn\u2019t at all necessary. The idea was finding a way to reduce permanent taint, and that\u2019s all it should focus on. Being out of character for extended periods of time was a price I was willing to pay in order to retain control of my character. The beta version of Chrysalis 2.0 seems a lot easier to manage, but it merely selects aberrations instead of removing any permanent ratings, so it really isn\u2019t solving the problem the way it used to.<br /> <br /> LordHeru\u2019s idea of voluntarily reducing Quantum to wipe out permanent Fluxseems like a process that the medics at AEON might come up with given some kind of insight into how Flux works. Terats would avoid this like the plague since their focus is realization of quantum potential (which would now fast-forward them to self-destruction). Or...maybe losing Quantum while reducing Flux might be a side-effect of a <i>failed</i> Chrysalis<br /> <br /> Honestly though, since temporary Flux burns off naturally now and seemingly faster (I thought it took twice as long in 1e to get rid of), it doesn\u2019t seem like it should be as much of a problem. Even having to max out to be able to gain new powers (if that stays the way it is) can be managed carefully, and just having Dormancy would burn it off steadily.<br /> <br /> The aberration that creates a field of contagious Flux establishes a historical point in canon so it has a place in the setting, but I\u2019d probably never afflict a player with it as it\u2019s essentially a death-sentence. As soon as that kind of issue manifests, the world will know almost instantly thanks to the information age. Then EVERY Proteus, Directive, and T2N member along with a squadron of DeVries combat elites hired by the (as yet unmentioned) Michaelites would be redirected to kill your ass dead <b>immediately</b>. Not only are you a danger to yourself, you\u2019re an incurable plague to literally everyone else, including baselines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T03:50:14-07:00","id":1323639,"title":"","content":"Reminder that there's a playtest form available: if the mechanics as written aren't working for you, please say so in the form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T05:43:17-07:00","id":1323652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323639#post1323639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminder that there's a playtest form available: if the mechanics as written aren't working for you, please say so in the form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Ian, just waiting for the powers to start testing the way Flux is working, so far the only thing that is really bothering me.<br /> <br /> The idea of taking the Nova Points away and use just experience is great. On 1e it would be a little bit difficult with all the progressive costs, but with a fixed cost it\u2019s much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T05:59:25-07:00","id":1323654,"title":"","content":"Darksol, agree with you in every aspect.<br /> <br /> The only thing that I don\u2019t think is working is gaining Flux on botches, tha is a rule that didn\u2019t exist on 1e. Max out give taint but only on a botche (it was a bit different the way botch worked, if I am not wrong, easier to botch).<br /> <br /> I spend a lot of time thinking about maxing out for evolving powers and it make sense, as it forces the character to use it to train it. It\u2019s a Nova characteristic, it\u2019s quantum powered, it\u2019s not a knowledge you are studying, or pumping iron to get bigger muscles, it\u2019s firing quantum bolts from your hand. A Nova can do basically everything he can set their mind to believe he can, that\u2019s the limit, so he maxes out to learn how far he can go. We open a problem for new powers and other abilities, but let\u2019s see how maxing out works first to discuss the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:24:42-07:00","id":1323672,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm one of the people who thinks the tragic decline into inhumanity was one of the better parts of Aberrant. I never liked that Terats could basically accrue an infinite amount of Taint. The new system for Chrysalis is better in, my estimation because there is no way to erase Transcendence. Sure, you can manipulate your Transformations, and avoid some Flux by buying powers through it, but that's it. I also thought it was way too hard to get Taint in the first edition. I can't think of a single character I played who even got one point of permanent Taint from play.<br /> <br /> Once you Erupt, you're on the path to being an Aberrant. It's what you do on that journey which matters and shows your true nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T08:36:35-07:00","id":1323693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323672#post1323672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm one of the people who thinks the tragic decline into inhumanity was one of the better parts of Aberrant. I never liked that Terats could basically accrue an infinite amount of Taint. The new system for Chrysalis is better in, my estimation because there is no way to erase Transcendence. Sure, you can manipulate your Transformations, and avoid some Flux by buying powers through it, but that's it. I also thought it was way too hard to get Taint in the first edition. I can't think of a single character I played who even got one point of permanent Taint from play.<br /> <br /> Once you Erupt, you're on the path to being an Aberrant. It's what you do on that journey which matters and shows your true nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it\u2019s not true. Not all novas in Aeon are Aberrants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T08:40:13-07:00","id":1323695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323672#post1323672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I'm one of the people who thinks the tragic decline into inhumanity was one of the better parts of Aberrant. I never liked that Terats could basically accrue an infinite amount of Taint. The new system for Chrysalis is better in, my estimation because there is no way to erase Transcendence. Sure, you can manipulate your Transformations, and avoid some Flux by buying powers through it, but that's it. I also thought it was way too hard to get Taint in the first edition. I can't think of a single character I played who even got one point of permanent Taint from play.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, agree about the new Chrysalis being a good way to make Terats not imune to Transcendence. The problem her is the speed you go down.<br /> <br /> In the first edition we planed our characters to deal with our powers, and as most of the mega attributes worked with no quantum expenditure, it was quite easy to keep working with no worries about the quantum pool and recovery. My character that got T5 was basically power focused and had to recover quantum pool faster than usual to stay useful. I think he had even high node and that quantum recovery power, not sure, but it was quite common to get close to gain taint every story.<br /> <br /> Using the option where mega attributes consume quantum, the need for quantum increase for everyone, and the chance of gaining taint increases too. Imaging every mega punch used consuming 1 quantum, after a combat you would need to wait for a few hours to refill or a few minutes for fast recovery, and a chance to get taint.<br /> <br /> Another point is Maxing Out in 1e consumed Willpower and didn\u2019t give automatic taint, so you would not go full power (what Maxing Out means) all the time as you had better situations to spend willpower, like doing things the character don\u2019t like too, and even when you used, you would not gain taint, only if botches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-11-2019, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T08:58:48-07:00","id":1323699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323693#post1323693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except it\u2019s not true. Not all novas in Aeon are Aberrants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But how many who erupted in the Aberrant time aren't? My understanding was Eden was populated by novas born after the time of the Aberrant setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:05:32-07:00","id":1323701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323699#post1323699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But how many who erupted in the Aberrant time aren't? My understanding was Eden was populated by novas born after the time of the Aberrant setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apollo, the main nova we meet from Eden, was born early 2000s and Erupted during the Nova Age, per previous edition. Which means he managed to remain mostly Taint (since he is 1E Nova) free for over a century. We don't know about other novas of Eden but I doubt he is the only one. Additionally, there are the novas who hid on Earth after the Aberrant War who also didn't get corrupted.<br /> <br /> Oh and lets not forget that Divis Mal, for all his power, did not become an inhuman monster willing to let the world burn.<br /> <br /> While the worry of what happens when you abuse your power makes perfect sense I can't see how having a core setting element that all novas fall actually helps move the story along.<br /> <br /> As well I would not use what we see in Aeon as a core fundamental of the Aberrant game, because while both games are set in the same broad cosmology they are also quite different in theme and purpose.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh, Mateus Luz, the funny thing is I actually like the idea that Botching a power roll gives the user temporary Flux. I think the idea that utter failure in the attempt to use quantum power causes some sort of negative feedback is a cool one. As long, that is, said temporary Flux fades somewhat rapidly. <br /> <br /> I am a fan of a nova being able to learn how to channel his abilities into being able to function better - which would have the effect of reducing his permanent Flux rating. To me the idea of Chryalis is that the nova is becoming more in tune with the flows of quantum energy, which means he finds it easier to handle and such. Which means a reduction in Flux.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-11-2019, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:26:13-07:00","id":1323703,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking of different dials (not the sterilization plot!) to bring up the shadows a bit in the setting.<br /> <br /> Does it stand to reason to other people that hyperfusion would have resulted in economic collapses in those countries and regions economically based on the fossil fuel industry - this leading to anti-Nova politics in those places (Church of Michael Archangel surging in Appalachia, the Dakotas, Oklahoma, and east Texas for example)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:49:50-07:00","id":1323709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323703#post1323703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m thinking of different dials (not the sterilization plot!) to bring up the shadows a bit in the setting.<br /> <br /> Does it stand to reason to other people that hyperfusion would have resulted in economic collapses in those countries and regions economically based on the fossil fuel industry - this leading to anti-Nova politics in those places (Church of Michael Archangel surging in Appalachia, the Dakotas, Oklahoma, and east Texas for example)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make sense, in a similar way of what happened on countries that live utterly from it, like Middle Eastern (what was talked about in the book), probably on a lesser scale, but still bringing a lot of people against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T09:57:02-07:00","id":1323710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323703#post1323703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m thinking of different dials (not the sterilization plot!) to bring up the shadows a bit in the setting.<br /> <br /> Does it stand to reason to other people that hyperfusion would have resulted in economic collapses in those countries and regions economically based on the fossil fuel industry - this leading to anti-Nova politics in those places (Church of Michael Archangel surging in Appalachia, the Dakotas, Oklahoma, and east Texas for example)?</div> </div> </div> </div>When i read the blurb about hyperfusion I thought two things; the first was &quot;finally, they're past that fictional barrier preventing fusion tech&quot;, the second was &quot;well, that just sent the fossil fuels industry to the crematorium&quot;. As a result of the changing landscape of world economy there will suddenly be; millions of unemployed, rich nations that are suddenly bankrupt, trade agreements that dissolve instantly, and a tsunami of malcontent. I'd expect riots all over the place once the enormity of that kind of change finally set in. You'd think T2M would have to start their careers diffusing uprisings along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:04:10-07:00","id":1323712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323549#post1323549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for Chrysalis in 1e were a kind of cheat code to power up faster than Goku, one year off and I came back to refit you with only my left leg.<br /> <br /> About the Taint, as a non English native, I never knew it had the meaning it has... but instead of Transcendence it could be Corruption, as it was in 1e Taint in Aberrant and Trinity.<br /> <br /> About the rules. It\u2019s hard to predict anything without the power rules, maybe maxing out is really powerful or you hardly roll dice for activating powers, than It\u2019s not a big deal...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a fair analysis of the Chrysalis rules as written. Yes, you could get discounts on everything, including Quantum. But it would take a good, long time to build up enough Chrysalis to actually enter one, and Terats had to pool XP before they entered Chrysalis to spend.<br /> <br /> The net result was their power curve became a series of looooong plateaus. Yes, they could avoid the effects of Taint 10, but it wasn't a free ride.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:07:35-07:00","id":1323714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323701#post1323701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Mateus Luz, the funny thing is I actually like the idea that Botching a power roll gives the user temporary Flux. I think the idea that utter failure in the attempt to use quantum power causes some sort of negative feedback is a cool one. As long, that is, said temporary Flux fades somewhat rapidly. </div> </div> </div> </div>I understand the idea of the misfire that taint yourself, but I don\u2019t think it is the point here. Imagine the Nova is rising a car with his hands, he roll Athletics + Might and add 6 Enhancements, if he fails it\u2019s not because he overused quantum, it\u2019s because he didn\u2019t grab it properly or his arm was in a bad position. To over use quantum we are talking about overcharging, and that\u2019s what I think is Maxing Out, the same guy needs Scale 4 but he can reach only 3, so he Max Out and reach 4, but his body is charged with bad Flux.<br /> <br /> Same for shooting quantum blasts, he is not trying to emit the energy, that\u2019s easy, the hard part is focus it on a blast and aim it, he fails not because he put too much quantum on the hand, he fails because it flows out with low control, to get a overuse of quantum he would need to try to throw more quantum than his hand can hold, so Maxing Out.<br /> <br /> On the opposite direction we have something like magic, that can fail and misfire causing Warping, that\u2019s not the setting but still the point is, the Magus is gathering magical power that is not part of himself or stored inside him, and trying to focus on a external effect, if botches, the magical energy will enter the Magus and warp him.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the way I see the use of quantum and the tests necessary, I don\u2019t know if that\u2019s the way you see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-11-2019, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:14:51-07:00","id":1323716,"title":"","content":"Totentanz, you are right, but it was far cheaper do it thru Chrysalis than on regular evolution, so the results were long plateaus followed by huge jumps on power creating a gap that increased every time the character entered Chrysalis.<br /> <br /> Also it was over-complex, transforming everything in XP is FAR better as I see. Nova Points were great, but the only moment we used it was in the character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:28:46-07:00","id":1323719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323701#post1323701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a fan of a nova being able to learn how to channel his abilities into being able to function better - which would have the effect of reducing his permanent Flux rating. To me the idea of Chryalis is that the nova is becoming more in tune with the flows of quantum energy, which means he finds it easier to handle and such. Which means a reduction in Flux.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not a bad idea, I would make a Nova with high Transcendence lose Flux faster than a lower Transcendence. Less control on the way you gather Flux or the amount needed to rise, but you can lose faster...<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say, you bleed Flux every week a total of 1 + \u00bd Transcendence, so the higher Transcendence means you are less human and more quantum Flux entity. So a week of for a T9 would release 5 Flux, if he have Dormancy it would take a day dormant to loose 5 Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:33:54-07:00","id":1323720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323699#post1323699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But how many who erupted in the Aberrant time aren't? My understanding was Eden was populated by novas born after the time of the Aberrant setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a lot. Most of the aberrants we see in Aeon are just one group put together by The Colony. The rest seem to have screwed off and not looked back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T10:54:19-07:00","id":1323725,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> I see a difference in the active use of Quantum abilities and the inactive use. I don't think I would require a nova who uses Mega-Strength to lift something, unless he maxes out or the equivalent, to worry about gaining Flux if he fails to lift up the car. But a nova who uses a quantum bolt and utterly fails in a spectacular way, yeah, him getting a point of Flux would be fine with me. That said I would need to see the actual power rules and the way things are for me to fully decide if that is how I want to go. <br /> <br /> All I know is that in theory the idea that if you spectacularly fail (that is botch) in using an active quantum enhanced ability you can gain Flux doesn't entirely bother me. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I guess a part of my problems is I don't truly really like Dormancy. To me a novas powers are his powers and while he can actively not use them they aren't gone. When Superman is Clark Kent he isn't dormant, his powers are still there, he just isn't casting. Same with Tony Stark or Thor or even Bruce Banner, who I see as probably ahving access to certain Mega-Attributes in his Bruce Banner state. <br /> <br /> On loosing Flux I totally like the idea that by not maxing out a power one can speed up flux, I just don't see the need to be something other than what one is. <br /> <br /> Though I admit none of the novas I want to play are ever physically inhuman, so maybe that is part of my thought process on that. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> In the podcast on the Polyhedron they mention something that I thought was fascinating. (They also mention something about Transcendence that had me negatively shaking my head, but still.) In it they talk about Divs Mal and how awesome he is, (cough, sorry not sorry), no but really they talk about how he released the Null Manifesto and then said to his novas do as thy will and then he realized he should have added &quot;but not that, or that, or that&quot;. It makes his later getting involved all the more interesting. At a certain point even his patience is at an end and when it does he acts. <br /> <br /> And that acting leads to all sorts of good (for his allies) and bad (for his enemies) things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T11:18:45-07:00","id":1323730,"title":"","content":"Regarding dormancy. One word: SHAZAM!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T11:34:14-07:00","id":1323732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323730#post1323730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding dormancy. One word: SHAZAM!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, right, yeah, that's true, he totally has Dormancy. <br /> <br /> BUT, most others with secret identities don't. They pretend to be normal baseline humans but really they still have their powers and can use them at a moment's notice. They don't need to power up as it were. <br /> <br /> Now, don't get me wrong, I'm not saying Dormancy doesn't have a place in Aberrant, I'm just saying I don't think it is as common in the superhero world as it is made to seem like in the Aberrant world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T11:53:13-07:00","id":1323737,"title":"","content":"The problem with dormancy in other settings is that most of the superheroes are not humans with powers, even X-Man don\u2019t work as Aberrant. So it\u2019s quite hard to say when it\u2019s dormancy in other settings and when it\u2019s not.<br /> <br /> As a side note Hulk as I see is the best case of Dormancy, unfortunately it\u2019s also the Hyde syndrome... so hard to point the access to the powers as Banner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T12:34:37-07:00","id":1323751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323710#post1323710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When i read the blurb about hyperfusion I thought two things; the first was &quot;finally, they're past that fictional barrier preventing fusion tech&quot;, the second was &quot;well, that just sent the fossil fuels industry to the crematorium&quot;. As a result of the changing landscape of world economy there will suddenly be; millions of unemployed, rich nations that are suddenly bankrupt, trade agreements that dissolve instantly, and a tsunami of malcontent. I'd expect riots all over the place once the enormity of that kind of change finally set in. You'd think T2M would have to start their careers diffusing uprisings along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the flipside of those economies drying up is that now their is cheap and plentiful energy, so the need for a lot of that revenue generation goes away. It doesn't make the malcontent go away, but it softens the blow, and then there are ripple effects from there.<br /> <br /> There are then also new boom economies, like laying Eufiber lines and setting up that network that wouldn't necessarily require a huge change in skills.<br /> <br /> I'd be really interested to see Freakonomics or something cover such a hypothetical situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T14:03:09-07:00","id":1323773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323751#post1323751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think the flipside of those economies drying up is that now their is cheap and plentiful energy, so the need for a lot of that revenue generation goes away. It doesn't make the malcontent go away, but it softens the blow, and then there are ripple effects from there.<br /> <br /> There are then also new boom economies, like laying Eufiber lines and setting up that network that wouldn't necessarily require a huge change in skills.<br /> <br /> I'd be really interested to see Freakonomics or something cover such a hypothetical situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the case with current economic displacement though, and it\u2019s hardly satisfying consolution to the public that is hit. Automation and international trade means more goods much cheaper - great for consumers, but sucks if you lose your old economy job even though the goods are cheaper for you too. The new economy jobs generally require skill sets the people who lost their jobs don\u2019t possess.<br /> <br /> Point is this seems like a potential setting factor worth exploring in terms of current political relevance (especially if people in said demo are radicalized right-ward).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T14:58:16-07:00","id":1323783,"title":"","content":"I think that besides technological development based on Nova projects Project Utopia should also have thought of economic systems and such to help relieve the issues that come from economic development. I'm pretty sure a set of Mega-Intelligent Novas could probably come up with a transition system that allows for those people who loose their jobs based on old technologies some sort of economic relief. <br /> <br /> In the US the idea of implementing nova-designed programs become all the more believable when one considers the setting has a Democratic Party wave in the 2020 elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T17:15:25-07:00","id":1323808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323783#post1323783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that besides technological development based on Nova projects Project Utopia should also have thought of economic systems and such to help relieve the issues that come from economic development. I'm pretty sure a set of Mega-Intelligent Novas could probably come up with a transition system that allows for those people who loose their jobs based on old technologies some sort of economic relief. <br /> <br /> In the US the idea of implementing nova-designed programs become all the more believable when one considers the setting has a Democratic Party wave in the 2020 elections.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that that\u2019s happened in Russia though is noteworthy. I don\u2019t think the US has been so reformed (yet) - the Harris Administration* is specifically trying to walk a tightrope on Nova issues.<br /> <br /> *it\u2019s canonically a moderate, which makes her the most likely fit; if the book characterized it as a progressive Democratic Administration, I\u2019d have said Warren","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:23:06-07:00","id":1323824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323808#post1323808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fact that that\u2019s happened in Russia though is noteworthy. I don\u2019t think the US has been so reformed (yet) - the Harris Administration* is specifically trying to walk a tightrope on Nova issues.<br /> <br /> *it\u2019s canonically a moderate, which makes her the most likely fit; if the book characterized it as a progressive Democratic Administration, I\u2019d have said Warren</div> </div> </div> </div>I did think it was nifty that Russia had it, though I wish something similar happened in America. That the path towards the FSA wasn't already being set up and stuff. <br /> <br /> Oh, did gender get mentioned on which Democrat won in Aberrant? I noticed democrat but I didn't see gender. <br /> <br /> The whole trying to keep a balance seems a bit sad, but at the same time it totally makes sense from a politican's standpoint. <br /> <br /> But yeah I wish that America was trying to adapt to all the potentials that Novas could bring forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:32:51-07:00","id":1323828,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a> <br /> <br /> Real talk here. THANK YOU!!!! I am so glad that you guys love the Trinity Continuum as much as you do and thus brought it back. <br /> <br /> There was never any doubt that I was going to support the core and Aeon kickstart, just like there was never a doubt that I was going to support Aberrant when it was made. <br /> <br /> I complain because I care. Aberrant was a game that I remember connecting with, especially because of its prominent gay character. It called to me. It was also a game that I ran and played in multiple times, even more than others. <br /> <br /> But I can also firmly at 110% truth that while the previous kickstarter started with me being worried by the end there was nothing, NOTHING, that had me throwing things at the screen asking Why, or Why!! <br /> <br /> You all did good, real good. <br /> <br /> Its been the same with Aberrant as it was with the other kickstarter. Though there are some things I go &quot;why?&quot; the majority is like &quot;Yep, love it.&quot; I love over 90% of things, no even more than 90. <br /> <br /> You have done a good job. You and all the others. <br /> <br /> But here's the thing Ian, you aren't just a person that was brought in. You know the game. Your semi-official (and only that because it wasn't officially published) Trinity Storyteller's Guide is AWESOME. As are the other expansions that were never made, sadly. <br /> <br /> I want you to know that. That I comment and critisize some things not out of anger but out of love, a love of a game and its design and all. Of a wish to make sure this new edition is just as awesome - no, even better - than the first one. <br /> <br /> The thing is Trinity, Aberrant, it all, is in good, no great, hands. <br /> <br /> I want you to know that! <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T19:53:02-07:00","id":1323832,"title":"","content":"Thank you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a>. Writers, developers, artists and everyone else involved in these projects throw their hearts into them. We can\u2019t please everyone all the time, and we\u2019re aware that unhappy voices make the most noise on the internet. But it truly helps when we see people trying out what we\u2019ve put down before declaring dislike, and where they do like something, declaring that like and letting us know it hit the mark. It\u2019s very much appreciated. So thank you again. \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:05:11-07:00","id":1323835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323824#post1323824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, did gender get mentioned on which Democrat won in Aberrant? I noticed democrat but I didn't see gender.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn\u2019t. That\u2019s not why I said Harris and Warren, they\u2019re just the best moderate and progressive candidates that have a real shot respectively, and since the book said centrist, I assumed Harris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:06:42-07:00","id":1323836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323832#post1323832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>. Writers, developers, artists and everyone else involved in these projects throw their hearts into them. We can\u2019t please everyone all the time, and we\u2019re aware that unhappy voices make the most noise on the internet. But it truly helps when we see people trying out what we\u2019ve put down before declaring dislike, and where they do like something, declaring that like and letting us know it hit the mark. It\u2019s very much appreciated. So thank you again. \ud83d\ude42</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely looking forward to trying it out, just can\u2019t do that yet without the powers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:14:26-07:00","id":1323838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323835#post1323835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It didn\u2019t. That\u2019s not why I said Harris and Warren, they\u2019re just the best moderate and progressive candidates that have a real shot respectively, and since the book said centrist, I assumed Harris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, gotcha. That makes sense. <br /> <br /> In some ways its interesting that a moderate won, I can see it of course, but its still interesting. Especially since by the election two years have passed since N-Day. <br /> <br /> Actually, it makes me wonder if any of the politicians running erupted. Either then or later on. Imagine a politician erupting after being elected. That would be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:18:55-07:00","id":1323839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323838#post1323838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, gotcha. That makes sense. <br /> <br /> In some ways its interesting that a moderate won, I can see it of course, but its still interesting. Especially since by the election two years have passed since N-Day. <br /> <br /> Actually, it makes me wonder if any of the politicians running erupted. Either then or later on. Imagine a politician erupting after being elected. That would be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>As in 1e, i\u2019d keep the first Nova candidate in the setting \u201cnow\u2019s\u201c Presidential Campaign.<br /> <br /> Actually... might be interesting if it\u2019s a mega-Social Republican Nova industrialist putting out the ultimate bootstrapping image, and pulling his party away from the xenophobes and social conservatives, so you the Church of Michael Archangel backed splinter Far Right party.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Democrats try to stay the course with cautious Utopia-friendly economic centrism, praying that despite coming off a second term and unable to run on change accordingly, the right will be divided between the other two candidates enough to hand them the election by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-11-2019, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:38:32-07:00","id":1323841,"title":"","content":"I love OPP because of this.<br /> <br /> We are here discussing the game we love, and all things we love we know the defects, that\u2019s why we can say we love it.<br /> <br /> Guys like Ian and Bunyip are her everyday seeing us talk bad about their work. Where can we find a company with the importance OPP have in the industry, with some of the greatest names working for, and still we have them here reading all the things we write.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my relationship with Aberrant is different form LordHeru, I was playing RPG for at least 10 years when find out about Aberrant, reading comic books for more than that, had been thru the first few years of Ultimate Marvel and the deconstruction of the traditional superheroes. When I saw Aberrant it was not new, neither innovative, yet I was mesmerised by the entire plot, from Adventure to Trinity, with all the possibilities and genres in one single game line.<br /> <br /> Trinity universe is the setting I loved for the last 15 years, and I never thought that would be replace so easily as it was by TC. This love may be new (my computer have OPP Forum and Aberrant KS tabs opened straight for 2 weeks now, that\u2019s the kind of thing people in love do...), but it\u2019s an old love that was renewed by you guys.<br /> <br /> Thanks a lot! I love your works!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-11-2019, 11:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T20:49:44-07:00","id":1323845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323839#post1323839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in 1e, i\u2019d keep the first Nova candidate in the setting \u201cnow\u2019s\u201c Presidential Campaign.<br /> <br /> Actually... might be interesting if it\u2019s a mega-Social Republican Nova industrialist putting out the ultimate bootstrapping image, and pulling his party away from the xenophobes and social conservatives, so you the Church of Michael Archangel backed splinter Far Right party.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Democrats try to stay the course with cautious Utopia-friendly economic centrism, praying that despite coming off a second term and unable to run on change accordingly, the right will be divided between the other two candidates enough to hand them the election by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea of a Mega-Social Nova who is a Republican industrialist working to push his party in a different direction, but still similar message, from the xenophobic and social conservative group. What a very interesting idea. Very interesting. <br /> <br /> A nova who is against the Church of Michael Archangel backed group. <br /> <br /> That's kind of brilliant. <br /> <br /> But I also like the idea of the Democratic party also being split by various nova sponsored groups. Thus also creating some sort of internal complex. <br /> <br /> Nod. Nod. I gotta tell you there being a Republican nova industrialist really intrigues me, really does. And this is from a guy who, well, lets just say isn't a fan of their current policies. <br /> <br /> The thing is I really want a nova corporate leader, a Tony Stark slash Bruce Wayne slash Lex Luthor sort of character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T01:28:52-07:00","id":1323887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323836#post1323836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely looking forward to trying it out, just can\u2019t do that yet without the powers!</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that list of powers is as comprehensive as they can make it. Throw in everything so we can truly stress-test this system. The missing stretch power, that bizarre information manipulation power, a finished momentum control, the obscure extradimensional quasi-obtenebration power like 3 sample characters had, <b>everything</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T02:31:31-07:00","id":1323894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323737#post1323737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with dormancy in other settings is that most of the superheroes are not humans with powers, even X-Man don\u2019t work as Aberrant. So it\u2019s quite hard to say when it\u2019s dormancy in other settings and when it\u2019s not.<br /> <br /> As a side note Hulk as I see is the best case of Dormancy, unfortunately it\u2019s also the Hyde syndrome... so hard to point the access to the powers as Banner.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of superheroes have a few points in Dormancy, in Aberrant terms. <br /> <br /> In Edngame, Captain Marvel doesn't glow, or have the Super Saiyan hair when she's not using her power and Thor doesn't crackle with lightning, or have his eyes go white. But when they step up to combat, they stop holding their powers down and they become noticeably <i>super</i>. They have, in Aberrant terms, an anima banner and aberrant eyes that get suppressed with Dormancy. <br /> <br /> What most heroes <i>don't</i> have is Dormancy 4 or 5. In the MCU, that's Bruce Banner and in DC it's Shazam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T03:22:12-07:00","id":1323898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323894#post1323894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of superheroes have a few points in Dormancy, in Aberrant terms. <br /> <br /> In Edngame, Captain Marvel doesn't glow, or have the Super Saiyan hair when she's not using her power and Thor doesn't crackle with lightning, or have his eyes go white. But when they step up to combat, they stop holding their powers down and they become noticeably <i>super</i>. They have, in Aberrant terms, an anima banner and aberrant eyes that get suppressed with Dormancy. <br /> <br /> What most heroes <i>don't</i> have is Dormancy 4 or 5. In the MCU, that's Bruce Banner and in DC it's Shazam.</div> </div> </div> </div>About Captain Marvel and Thor, I think it\u2019s more about maxing out than dormant. They are still superhumanly strong, they still can use their powers, they are just not on their Max.<br /> Possibly they are using a halfway dormancy, power down but not all the way to baseline, not sure if that\u2019s possible, in my games we had this option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T03:37:24-07:00","id":1323902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323898#post1323898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About Captain Marvel and Thor, I think it\u2019s more about maxing out than dormant. They are still superhumanly strong, they still can use their powers, they are just not on their Max.<br /> Possibly they are using a halfway dormancy, power down but not all the way to baseline, not sure if that\u2019s possible, in my games we had this option.</div> </div> </div> </div>They definitely have a higher baseline than well, Baselines. But they're also, in Aberrant terms, suppressing Transformations and the only way we've seen to do that (So far) is Dormancy.<br /> <br /> I was actually thinking about this in response to a post elsewhere, and in retrospect, they're more likely running around at half their power ratings so that they can bleed off Flux. Doesn't quite fit with their Transformations being suppressed (Unless they respond to Quantum used, I guess?) but it's close enough .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T04:00:33-07:00","id":1323907,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your kind words, everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T05:15:30-07:00","id":1323920,"title":"","content":"What's the stretch goal for Raoul Duke?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T05:59:43-07:00","id":1323932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323902#post1323902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They definitely have a higher baseline than well, Baselines. But they're also, in Aberrant terms, suppressing Transformations and the only way we've seen to do that (So far) is Dormancy.<br /> <br /> I was actually thinking about this in response to a post elsewhere, and in retrospect, they're more likely running around at half their power ratings so that they can bleed off Flux. Doesn't quite fit with their Transformations being suppressed (Unless they respond to Quantum used, I guess?) but it's close enough .</div> </div> </div> </div>Our house rule was basically you can use dormancy to reduce your taint and quantum by up to your Dormancy rating. Let\u2019s say you have Q4, T5 and Dormancy 3, you could reduce your quantum to 1, 2 or 3 reducing your taint to 2, 3 or 4. For as long your quantum and taint and lowered you lose access to powers that required higher quantum and have a reduced quantum pool, but also are free from the taint aspects and are you resonate as a low quantum Nova (for quantum detectors).<br /> Dormancy 4 and 5 allow the Nova to cut both quantum and taint to 0 (no matter how high it was), and 5 would change your body to the point you didn\u2019t even show a M-R node on scans.<br /> That\u2019s probably what I will use on TC: Aberrant, let\u2019s see...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:01:09-07:00","id":1323933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323898#post1323898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About Captain Marvel and Thor, I think it\u2019s more about maxing out than dormant. They are still superhumanly strong, they still can use their powers, they are just not on their Max.<br /> Possibly they are using a halfway dormancy, power down but not all the way to baseline, not sure if that\u2019s possible, in my games we had this option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thor has Dormancy in the not MCU, Donald Blake era comics. Where dormed down he had to spend a moment activating his Thor powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:05:37-07:00","id":1323935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323933#post1323933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thor has Dormancy in the not MCU, Donald Blake era comics. Where dormed down he had to spend a moment activating his Thor powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, Dr. Blake could actually be prevented from turning into Thor (like Shazam). A little off-topic, but that reinforces how dormant it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:10:47-07:00","id":1323937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323933#post1323933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thor has Dormancy in the not MCU, Donald Blake era comics. Where dormed down he had to spend a moment activating his Thor powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But he also needed his umbrella to do so, as his power came from the transformed Mjolnir.<br /> <br /> My favourite Thor was the ultimate, the entire first Ultimates story arc was fantastic, but the characters were by far the best part (Cap kicking Banners face after he transform back after destroying a good part of NY). Ok, nothing to do with Aberrant, but still good memories...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:14:38-07:00","id":1323938,"title":"","content":"I wanted to echo the positive statements made about this edition of the game. I was concerned initially about the tone of the game changing. The tone of the first podcast put me off, because I felt an indictment (\u201cdark bullshit\u201d) was being made against the original. Yet, I\u2019ve come to see, especially with the example of today\u2019s update, that the changes have only been additive. I imagine it\u2019s very hard to hear someone question your decisions when you can only show them your reasons in very small chunks, once a week.<br /> <br /> Thank you for persevering. You\u2019ve made a believer out of me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:27:00-07:00","id":1323939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323887#post1323887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hope that list of powers is as comprehensive as they can make it. Throw in everything so we can truly stress-test this system. The missing stretch power, that bizarre information manipulation power, a finished momentum control, the obscure extradimensional quasi-obtenebration power like 3 sample characters had, <b>everything</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The powers are gonna have to look different in any case. No levels, every dot is 12 XP. That means that Quantum is the only power barrier, and bioluminescence can\u2019t really exist like it did :P 12 XP for biolum 5 would still be too much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Prediction: Claws will be a Mega-Edge, not a distinct Quantum Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:33:00-07:00","id":1323940,"title":"","content":"I'm liking the optional rules mentioned in today's post, although I'd still be fond of a way to actually mitigate Transcendence, and not just slow it down since you're still going to get it from raising Quantum, no matter what. But these are presumably just summaries...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T06:47:52-07:00","id":1323944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323939#post1323939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The powers are gonna have to look different in any case. No levels, every dot is 12 XP. That means that Quantum is the only power barrier, and bioluminescence can\u2019t really exist like it did :P 12 XP for biolum 5 would still be too much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Prediction: Claws will be a Mega-Edge, not a distinct Quantum Power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think powers will be really basic, than you add Tags to it, like extras and techniques from the level 3 powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T08:55:05-07:00","id":1323964,"title":"","content":"The update today was interesting, especially in that it shows the writers (go you!!) know and understand that people want different things and that there is room in Aberrant for those things, maybe not in a single game but in the overall system. <br /> <br /> So that's cool. <br /> <br /> I like the mix of the two systems, the one about connections and the one about a focus, and I could see using something like them with some changes in my sort of game. <br /> <br /> For example, a major change I would make, is remove the whole need to lie about being a nova in the contact one. I don't like the idea that a Nova can't say he is a nova, so yep, that's out. <br /> <br /> Speaking of which, as we talked about it above, I still am not feeling that the Dormancy rules fit the way that the setting works. But honestly this isn't a 2e thing, more a Aberrant thing as a whole. Because Aberrant is about novas erupting and then taking jobs where their nova natures are known. But then we have rules that basically make it seem that most novas go about their lives with their powers hidden in a faded away sort of thing. Which doesn't seem to happen. So a disconnect. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I hope stuff like biolumenescence and other such physical abilities have a place in new Aberrant. I loved such little things like that. They really allowed for my nova character to reach his optimal state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T09:26:13-07:00","id":1323970,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think the point is being baseline, or hiding that you are a Nova. I think the point is interacting with people without use of power or without forcing them to be inferior to you, basically treat as equal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:02:50-07:00","id":1323984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323970#post1323970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think the point is being baseline, or hiding that you are a Nova. I think the point is interacting with people without use of power or without forcing them to be inferior to you, basically treat as equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you\u2019re talking about the optional rule in the new update, the requirement that you gaslight them means it fails at that goal.<br /> <br /> If the point is valuing baseline relationships, than that is what the system should do. No \u201cdon\u2019t use your powers\u201d or \u201cpretend to be baseline\u201d requirements. Just actively put the emphasis on the relationships themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> The problem is it\u2019s trying to capture Clark Kent and Peter Parker\u2019s daily lives as well, when the fact that Aberrant is as different a setting form those SPECIFIC* comics as it is is lost in the process.<br /> <br /> * i\u2019m not trying to do a \u201cnot a superhero setting\u201d thing ala 1e, just that there are diverse arrays of superhero genres and tropes, and Aberrant does some distinct ones.<br /> <br /> It works as an optional rule for a 4 color setting, it doesn\u2019t work as a patch for Aberrant core setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-12-2019, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T10:07:41-07:00","id":1323988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323984#post1323984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you\u2019re talking about the optional rule in the new update, the requirement that you gaslight them means it fails at that goal.<br /> <br /> If the point is valuing baseline relationships, than that is what the system should do. No \u201cdon\u2019t use your powers\u201d or \u201cpretend to be baseline\u201d requirements. Just actively put the emphasis on the relationships themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes, this!<br /> <br /> The character is a nova. Why should he have to pretend otherwise. No, let him be a nova. Let him use his powers. But also require him to actively attach himself to other people, with that being baselines.<br /> <br /> This could most easily be directly - he has a loved one who is a baseline and who he cares for - but it also could be more broadly - he visits orphanages or has charity groups or attends fairs and other community prrojects where he is surrounded by people, listens to them, etc.<br /> <br /> But him needing to not use his powers, not reveal his nova identity, yeah no.<br /> <br /> That all said. These rules are for the Four-Color Superheroes genre. So in that sense secret identities and such are important. But saying that I hope something similar exists for other genres, but without the need to hide one's self.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> A part of me, well all of me really lol, wishes that the &quot;Why Have A Secret Identity?&quot; sidebar was not present. The idea that dorming down, that not using your powers, that pretending to be someone your not is given such a prominent role, yeah, not a fan. <br /> <br /> Same with the whole &quot;Nova Trait Advancement&quot; sidebar, that is totally getting ignored. Experience can be spent to buy or improve nova traits without needing to max them, and thus gain Flux.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-12-2019, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:01:23-07:00","id":1324002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323984#post1323984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works as an optional rule for a 4 color setting, it doesn\u2019t work as a patch for Aberrant core setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it as being precisely that: an optional rule for a 4 color setting. Presumably, the other tones will include their own optional rules for this sort of thing. It's possible that the idea here is that there isn't a \u201cglobal patch\u201d; just different patches for each possible tone. <br /> <br /> Related to this, I would say that there's a decent chance that the Aberrant core setting doesn't assume any one tone: it walks a fine line of allowing for any of the three, and leaves it up to the Storyguide to decide which of the three will be featured in his games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:07:32-07:00","id":1324005,"title":"","content":"On the \u201cNova Trait Advancement\u201d sidebar, I'm wondering if it would make sense to include an exception: you still need to Max Out in order to advance a nova trait; but if you simultaneously spend the experience to advance it, you don't get the otherwise mandatory point of Flux. <br /> <br /> I'm considering this as potential errata. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:10:51-07:00","id":1324007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324002#post1324002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read it as being precisely that: an optional rule for a 4 color setting. Presumably, the other tones will include their own optional rules for this sort of thing. It's possible that the idea here is that there isn't a \u201cglobal patch\u201d; just different patches for each possible tone. <br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>*points at the secret identity sidebar that is part of the default rules*. The issue applies to the default rules for dealing with Taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:31:36-07:00","id":1324012,"title":"","content":"<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> Honestly, I think the basic idea of just removing that sidebar is the best. Characters gain experience and they can spend that experience on quantum traits without having to worry about Flux or using a power. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> Yep. Totally. Such a disconnect I feel. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Ooh. So I just had an idea. Dr Henri Mazarin is a bit upset that his name won't be separated from Dr. Rashoud. Well when you look at what Dr Mazarin studies (which is nova biology and the nature of flux as it pertains to them) I think we could always create something like the Mazarin Process, which is basically a variant method of undergoing Chrysalis. <br /> <br /> Hmm. Yeah, I like this. Gonna have to think on how to implement it or something like it.<br /> <br /> Of course this begs the question did someone connected to the Teras philosophy provide Dr Mazarin some information or feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T11:51:28-07:00","id":1324020,"title":"","content":"We had a big discussion since Tuesday, than suddenly they show the solutions they proposed months ago to the problems we saw. We had 3 days to think about it, they had months. Honestly, I will keep my criticism behind until we have all the book to read. They are several steps ahead of us...<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s talk about book ideas for our own projects... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T12:04:46-07:00","id":1324026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324020#post1324020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We had a big discussion since Tuesday, than suddenly they show the solutions they proposed months ago to the problems we saw. We had 3 days to think about it, they had months. Honestly, I will keep my criticism behind until we have all the book to read. They are several steps ahead of us...<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s talk about book ideas for our own projects... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They have not in fact shown a solution to the problem being raised, no. I would be happy to playtest stuff before discussing it, but they haven\u2019t provided the full text necessary to do that yet - so it\u2019s either discuss it now or we all shut up and stop talking for the next few weeks, which I don\u2019t think is what OPP wants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T12:11:20-07:00","id":1324029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324026#post1324026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have not in fact shown a solution to the problem being raised, no. I would be happy to playtest stuff before discussing it, but they haven\u2019t provided the full text necessary to do that yet - so it\u2019s either discuss it now or we all shut up and stop talking for the next few weeks, which I don\u2019t think is what OPP wants.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm with you on that. Today's update made some things more ambiguous and showed that they thought of some alternate ways to do things. But that's about it. An actual playtest will require the rules that drop next week, as right now we can't even make full characters. I think, but I'm not positive, that we'll be able to with next week's update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T12:26:06-07:00","id":1324030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324026#post1324026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have not in fact shown a solution to the problem being raised, no. I would be happy to playtest stuff before discussing it, but they haven\u2019t provided the full text necessary to do that yet - so it\u2019s either discuss it now or we all shut up and stop talking for the next few weeks, which I don\u2019t think is what OPP wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>AND<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bullshock</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with you on that. Today's update made some things more ambiguous and showed that they thought of some alternate ways to do things. But that's about it. An actual playtest will require the rules that drop next week, as right now we can't even make full characters. I think, but I'm not positive, that we'll be able to with next week's update.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I totally agree with this. We can only talk about that which we know, which at this time is a setting chapter and the basic character building chapter. Not powers. Not new rules. Not genre conversion materials. <br /> <br /> That all said some of my concerns aren't based on future materials I don't get to see. Some of my issues are up front and center, and have been mentioned by me numerous times. (identity and XP flux cost sidebars mostly, but also Transcendence as a thought; but now also Quantum Instability, which I don't mind as a general idea but I am not sure about its implementation). <br /> <br /> I do kind of wish that when they show us something like Scale or the Four Color section they give us a copy of the page in question, rather than what seems like a synopsis. I mean we are getting it within a week, so if they are preemptively showing us, can't they just show us. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> That all said the fact that I have decided to create something called the Mazarin Process as a variant to Chrysalis that brings a smile to my face, now I just need to figure out the details. hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T12:34:24-07:00","id":1324032,"title":"","content":"I agree it\u2019s not fully solved, but we are speculating on something that is partially (at best) known.<br /> <br /> But as you said, we cant play test without the rules from next week. Probably, next week will be the last restriction on character creation. But we will be limited by the lack of Q-Tech and Novatech info from the Technology chapter, so no Ironman / Gadgeter / Tinkerer yet.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it\u2019s impossible to not came back here on every break I take on the work. So I will be here to give my opinion and ideas even against my own will...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T13:41:26-07:00","id":1324040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324026#post1324026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so it\u2019s either discuss it now or we all shut up and stop talking for the next few weeks, which I don\u2019t think is what OPP wants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Discussion, sure.<br /> <br /> Arguing around and around in circles for days? Not so much.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of material that was dropped on Tuesday, and yet, all anyone has really talked about is their feelings on Transcendence and Quantum Flux. Cool, we get it, not everyone's thrilled with what they're seeing.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Continuing to argue about it at this point isn't resolving anything. People either need to dial their &quot;discussion&quot; methods way back, or change topics, please.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T14:07:55-07:00","id":1324042,"title":"","content":"So what's with the whole Michael Mercer, Maxwell's alleged son thing. Are we supposed to think that there is some sort of conspiracy or secret there? I don't entirely understand. Also, did he name his son after his best friend Donigal, cause that is awesome.<br /> <br /> Though a part of me thinks it would be cool that Michael Donigal doesn't actually totally disappear, sometimes he visits Maxwell and his son and granddaughter over the years.<br /> <br /> I also like the fact that the Margaret is a Psiad, that's a very nifty thing. It also showcases that the superior genes are inheretable but that one doesn't automatically need to be the same as t heir parent or grandparent is.<br /> <br /> It also makes me think that maybe Michael Mercer was an Inspired as well, though I have an image of him being at Adventure! level rather than Nova/Psiad level.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Soo in Project Utopia there is the Research Oversight division. I'm curious as to what sorts of technologies would be banned, which would be questioned but probably okayed, and which would be fine. Like are we talking weapons tech as banned or are we talking that they are even restricted things that effected the political life of nations even if they are safe.<br /> <br /> Also, technically, the UN has no authority to force nations to follow its laws. So if a country is like &quot;nope&quot; then legally speaking its hard to stop them. Sooo if something like a megacorp in a major country is like &quot;we got this!&quot; there might be something that can be done to stop Utopia.<br /> <br /> I ask because this reminds me of the scene in Iron Man 2 when the US Congress is like &quot;Tony Stark gives us your tech&quot; and he is all like &quot;FU!&quot; - That's the sort of nova industrialist I would want to play.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Oooh just focused my mind on Social Development section of Project Utopia. Hmm. That could be an interesting and under-appreciated section to work in. Imagine a Mega-Intelligent Nova that comes up with a set of social philosophies that would create a stable and efficient and free society. Now others - a mix of novas and talents - have to follow the plan laid out by said nova in order to establish said society in the country or region or city of choice. That could be an interesting game.<br /> <br /> Now imagine if some of those novas involved - or even the theory creator himself - actually followed the tenets of Teras but did so hiddenly. hmm. Sounds interesting to me.<br /> <br /> PS. Really kind of need the ability to create Novatech that is of a philosophy and such rather than actual technology.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Also related to the Environmental section, wasn't there a project in 1E that brought lakes and forests to the region of middle America. I could have sworn there was, though it might have been something else I read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-12-2019, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T14:33:47-07:00","id":1324047,"title":"","content":"The Michael Mercer thing was supposed to be a conspiracy that never happened as there was no support for aberrant back there. I like to think about Michael as the soon Max had on a time travel to the past, and actually he had it on an older age than when Michael shows up. That\u2019s why nobody knew about him, but Max knew, he met him in the future and know that he would be his father on a older age.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Margaret as a Psiad, one of the most awesome ideas I saw, and it\u2019s sad she will not be in the Prometheus Compendium.<br /> <br /> I dont think the gene is for Superhuman, I think it\u2019s for one of the 3 kinds of Superhuman, but Meggie has a psiad mother, or at least an strong latent mother, or maybe Michael was a psiad too and son of a psiad mother and Max from the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T15:24:48-07:00","id":1324055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324042#post1324042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's with the whole Michael Mercer, Maxwell's alleged son thing. Are we supposed to think that there is some sort of conspiracy or secret there? I don't entirely understand. Also, did he name his son after his best friend Donigal, cause that is awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Adventure! 1e, Max -- who was known to be a master of disguise -- stepped away from the Aeon Society for a while. Then his son &quot;Michael,&quot; who no one's heard of before, shows up out of nowhere to handle many of Max's affairs. There's an implication that Michael was actually just Max, perhaps covering up for the fact that Max didn't seem to be aging.<br /> <br /> Aberrant d20 introduced Margaret Mercer as Max's granddaughter. It's never technically stated that Michael was her father, but in the absence of other familial data, it's a reasonable assumption.<br /> <br /> So, if you subscribe to the belief that Michael Mercer was actually Max, then Margaret is in fact Max's daughter, not granddaughter.<br /> <br /> How much of this we'll use in the new edition is still up in the air. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T15:35:51-07:00","id":1324059,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea that Michael was the son of Max Mercer and Sarah Gettel, but for whatever reason he just wasn't as exceptional as his parents. I like the idea that he was just a regular guy trying to live up to parents that were super-heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T15:40:21-07:00","id":1324060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1323828#post1323828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a><br /> <br /> Real talk here. THANK YOU!!!! I am so glad that you guys love the Trinity Continuum as much as you do and thus brought it back.<br /> <br /> There was never any doubt that I was going to support the core and Aeon kickstart, just like there was never a doubt that I was going to support Aberrant when it was made.<br /> <br /> I complain because I care. Aberrant was a game that I remember connecting with, especially because of its prominent gay character. It called to me. It was also a game that I ran and played in multiple times, even more than others.<br /> <br /> But I can also firmly at 110% truth that while the previous kickstarter started with me being worried by the end there was nothing, NOTHING, that had me throwing things at the screen asking Why, or Why!!<br /> <br /> You all did good, real good.<br /> <br /> Its been the same with Aberrant as it was with the other kickstarter. Though there are some things I go &quot;why?&quot; the majority is like &quot;Yep, love it.&quot; I love over 90% of things, no even more than 90.<br /> <br /> You have done a good job. You and all the others.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing Ian, you aren't just a person that was brought in. You know the game. Your semi-official (and only that because it wasn't officially published) Trinity Storyteller's Guide is AWESOME. As are the other expansions that were never made, sadly.<br /> <br /> I want you to know that. That I comment and critisize some things not out of anger but out of love, a love of a game and its design and all. Of a wish to make sure this new edition is just as awesome - no, even better - than the first one.<br /> <br /> The thing is Trinity, Aberrant, it all, is in good, no great, hands.<br /> <br /> I want you to know that!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Everyone has so far done a good job. The one thing i disagree on was the one thing I disliked about first edition, so no harm no foul. Pretty much everything else has been on the money. <br /> <br /> So another call-out: Yay <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 07-12-2019, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:12:34-07:00","id":1324063,"title":"","content":"The potential for Psi, Quantum, or Flux are all linked to the same genes, but precisely how they manifest is case by case and depends a lot on individual circumstances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:25:14-07:00","id":1324067,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a> Ooh I see, well that is interesting. I could totally see the potential of Maxwell coming back and pretending to be his child so nobody questions thing. It is very much an Adventure! era concept.<br /> <br /> So while I would have no problem with that if it was so I kind of like the idea of Michael being a person all his own.<br /> <br /> It is nifty that there are plots with plots and potentials within potentials. Some that were dropped and others that were kept and others that got changed by time. hehe<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324063#post1324063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The potential for Psi, Quantum, or Flux are all linked to the same genes, but precisely how they manifest is case by case and depends a lot on individual circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that. Its like a gene sequence, one that can flip three ways when active.<br /> <br /> It also leads to the interesting an amusing question - what of a Michael Donigal who awakened as a Psiad due to the Hammersmith Event rather than a Nova. hmm. hehe<br /> <br /> But it also leads to the really nifty idea of a family which has members of all three different types. And honestly I really like the idea that the Mercer Family has a Flux user (Maxwell), a Quantum user (Michael), and a Psi user (Margaret). Too me the idea that overtime the Aeon Society has been led by all three types of users is really cool. As is the fact that the Quantum leader was NOT during the Nova Age, but rather that during that Age it was a Psiad that led the organization.<br /> <br /> Which, as a random thought, makes me wonder what happened to her. Psiads live longer than normal, right, and so chances are she could have still been alive during the Aeon Era. Hmmm<br /> <br /> Anyway, its a nifty thing for me. Just like I LOVED how the Hammersmith Event led to the creation of a person of all three categories.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Random thought on XP costs. So with technology having to do math isn't such a pain but a part of me wishes that the costs were more roundable - like 15 instead of 16 and 10 instead of 12. Not because I think 16 and 12 are too high, just that its easier to add stuff up in one's head when numbers are 15 and 10.<br /> <br /> Also, and obviously we will see this when the power rules come out, but I am crossing my fingers in hope that the various body manipulation powers are still available for purchase. I always liked them as they allowed, at cost, for a nova to gain minor physical enhancements without going full on power.<br /> <br /> When the XP chart says &quot;maximum 5 Paths&quot; does that mean no path can go higher than 5, or a nova can have up to five paths. I figure its the first but I wanted to make sure. <br /> <br /> And by the way the whole removal of Nova Points and stuff and just making it XP is really smart and really useful. I always thought that while nifty, nova points actually added more annoyances then they gave benefits. So it just being XP is brilliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-12-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:37:26-07:00","id":1324071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which, as a random thought, makes me wonder what happened to her. Psiads live longer than normal, right, and so chances are she could have still been alive during the Aeon Era. Hmmm </div> </div> </div>Psiads, as well as psions, novas and talents have their lifespan defined by their powers. Bk and VK make the character immortal, even the auxiliary mode is enough (it\u2019s somewhere on Aeon).<br /> <br /> Aberrant 1e had the lifespan defined by Mega-Stamina, but it also says that high quantum is basically enough to to increase lifespan.<br /> <br /> Most of the Aeon Society originals, are alive on Aberrant War, even later on Trinity, at least on 1e. There are exchange of emails between at least one of the originals (can\u2019t remember the name) in trinity original book.<br /> <br /> Edit: Whitley Styles","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-12-2019, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T16:50:39-07:00","id":1324072,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> The idea of the original founding members - no matter their later affiliation - that are still alive gathering together for a reunion in 21something is really amusing to me. Like a high school reunion they talk about their lives over the last century since the founding of the Aeon Society.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I fought a war, lost, hid out, then caused a global eruption, then stopped a war, then ran, and oh now I own my own universe but visit here sometimes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well you think that is bad I cleansed areas from the taint [everyone giggles because people are people] your people caused, then designed a category of power noone ever saw before, then created my own eruption effect, then got captured, held prisoner, escaped, and led a war against those who would manipulate humanity.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well I traveled through time and space and saw really nifty stuff. like dinosaurs. I thought about aiding them in getting powers but I didn't want to tempt fate.&quot;<br /> <br /> And on and on.<br /> <br /> Hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:02:09-07:00","id":1324077,"title":"","content":"Laughed twice, one for the idea of them talking about it and another on the \u201cbecause people are people\u201d<br /> I honestly don\u2019t have an automatic connection on the word Taint other than Aberrant Taint, so it\u2019s not funny, but than a bunch of 200 yo people giggling on a cafe somewhere... man it was a funny mental image...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:06:27-07:00","id":1324078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324077#post1324077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Laughed twice, one for the idea of them talking about it and another on the \u201cbecause people are people\u201d<br /> I honestly don\u2019t have an automatic connection on the word Taint other than Aberrant Taint, so it\u2019s not funny, but than a bunch of 200 yo people giggling on a cafe somewhere... man it was a funny mental image...</div> </div> </div> </div>Little behind the scenes note - I don't find it funny either (taint that is) but I know a lot of people who do so I had to include that little bit of a scene. And yeah, a couple of 200 year old people sitting in a cafe in Chicago (its where the Aeon Society was founded) is kind of hilarious.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Oh,and I looked it up. Yeah, anyone with a VK mode of at least auxiliary level are immortal. And since there is no reason to not get said mode, pretty much all the major psi users we have ever seen are gonna be around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-12-2019, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:07:54-07:00","id":1324079,"title":"","content":"Not trying to resurrect the earlier argument, but a separate issue related to Transcendence occurs to me - does anyone else think it should be possible to have Transformations at character creation without pumping your Transcendence over 3 first?<br /> <br /> I was thinking some Novas should just look less human than others from the get-go, but maybe i\u2019m thinking about it like Marvel mutants too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:15:29-07:00","id":1324080,"title":"","content":"While I do like novas who basically look human I do like them to have some sort of &quot;what?&quot; features - features that usually come from something that is mechanically an 1e Aberration or I guess a 2e Transformation. <br /> <br /> My thought is that maybe either there can be a mechanical way to get a Transformation without the resulting Flux OR maybe if a player chooses a Transformation and then later gets a Flux-imposed one the one he already has retroactively counts. For mechanical reasons rather than purely fluff ones. <br /> <br /> I kind of like the idea that Transformations can be bought and when they are bought they provide some benefit, small though it may be, as compared to when its a Flux infused transformation, which is almost entirely negative. <br /> <br /> Another way to go about this might be to have a sort of power category that gives some small effects that can be purchased, with these effects leading to mechanical benefits similar to Transformations. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> Unrelated, as I don't like to double post, the fact that we obviously don't know how powers work isn't stopping me from some creative inspiration. One the ideas that I am thinking about is a nova who uses either Warp or Teleport or some other Spatial Manipulation power (hint hint, nudge nudge) to basically bring with him modules into either orbit or to another planet. Modules that when expanded and connected create a whole outpost colony.<br /> <br /> The benefit of this is that it reduces the cost - no longer is it necessary to pay ground to space launch costs. All they need to do is build the module and then set it up in space. After the nova gets his either hundred plus thousand or million dollar pay for the whole earth to space teleport thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:27:30-07:00","id":1324082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324079#post1324079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying to resurrect the earlier argument, but a separate issue related to Transcendence occurs to me - does anyone else think it should be possible to have Transformations at character creation without pumping your Transcendence over 3 first?<br /> <br /> I was thinking some Novas should just look less human than others from the get-go, but maybe i\u2019m thinking about it like Marvel mutants too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea, even more now that the Transcendence, even without any transformation, causing personal issues.<br /> <br /> At least once my group used a temporary aberration idea that worked fine, on Taint 2 you could get a temporary aberration that worked every time the Nova spend quantum, usually it was Anima Banner, Aberrant Eyes or Aberrant Skin, as they are quite visual and reversible. It worked fine with our partial dormancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T17:41:01-07:00","id":1324086,"title":"","content":"Some powers can also force a change in appearance, like permanent armour, Elemental sheet, bodymorph, and all the body modifications...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T18:04:20-07:00","id":1324094,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping that Body Modifications become Mega-Edges in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T18:20:56-07:00","id":1324095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324094#post1324094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping that Body Modifications become Mega-Edges in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>My 'concern' with this is that Mega-Edges cost 12 XP. And some of the 1E Body Mods were much less than that in cost. Not that it means anything as there could be already built in cost factors we don't know about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T18:45:37-07:00","id":1324100,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of two potential timeline points. <br /> <br /> One is that the the Daedalus League works with the UN/NASA/EU in the removal of much of Earth's orbiting space debris. The materials gathered in this operation are utilized in the expansion of the first Earth Orbital Station, which in time comes to be known as Clarke Station. <br /> <br /> The second is about a nova with nature powers. A nova with nature powers goes on a grand spree of reforestation throughout North America. That is, to the amusement of some and the annoyance of others, wherever he goes hundreds of thousands of trees soon follow - taking root and growing to maturity overnight. By the time he basically stops the forests of America have regrown to levels not seen since the late 1600s. He is called an eco-terrorist by some and an ally to nature by others. At the end he disappears just as quietly as he appeared. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> This also led me to wondering something. Could nova powers disrupt the way that nuclear weapons work. Because if so could you imagine a nova who basically shuts down all functioning nuclear weapons, no matter where they are stored. Due to him controlling his effect this doesn't stop nuclear fission or fusion plants, just weapons. Maybe every ten years after this date all new nuclear weapons are also effected by his power - despite baseline technological attempts to make their nukes immune. <br /> <br /> And yes, I know that this wouldn't work because canon history needs nuclear weapons to exist for China to use them to cause Divs Mal and the novas to back off. But still, something like this would totally showcase how nova actions could change the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T18:59:02-07:00","id":1324103,"title":"","content":"Make a post for character ideas, you have a bunch of good ones, so we don\u2019t go off topic (as if there was anything on topic here...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:22:19-07:00","id":1324108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324079#post1324079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying to resurrect the earlier argument, but a separate issue related to Transcendence occurs to me - does anyone else think it should be possible to have Transformations at character creation without pumping your Transcendence over 3 first?<br /> <br /> I was thinking some Novas should just look less human than others from the get-go, but maybe i\u2019m thinking about it like Marvel mutants too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily (referring to thinking about it like Marvel mutants). I do think there is space to say \u201cthis change in my appearance is a feature, not a bug\u201d, and not have it count against your Transcendence. Although.. I can see a player taking it too far. But yeah, there is some creative/design space there.<br /> <br /> Off-topic but related, I was thinking about D&amp;D/Pathfinder \u2018medusas\u2019 a while back and contrasting it with the original gorgon myths. The Greeks depicted that transformation as a curse. A rather spiteful one at that. Yet, in your high fantasy rpg, it\u2019s really a superpower. Frankly, since there are male \u2018medusas\u2019 it doesn\u2019t seem like a disadvantage of all. That sort of perspective makes me one to look at a voluntary nova transformation a power rather than a penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1789-quinarch","name":"Quinarch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1789_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:23:18-07:00","id":1324109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324095#post1324095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My 'concern' with this is that Mega-Edges cost 12 XP. And some of the 1E Body Mods were much less than that in cost. Not that it means anything as there could be already built in cost factors we don't know about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd much rather make Body Mods Mega-Edges with non-standard XP costs than to try to shoehorn them into the Quantum Powers where the XP cost is the only thing about them that <i>isn't</i> non-standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:29:34-07:00","id":1324111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324109#post1324109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd much rather make Body Mods Mega-Edges with non-standard XP costs than to try to shoehorn them into the Quantum Powers where the XP cost is the only thing about them that <i>isn't</i> non-standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah totally. I agree with you on non-standard costs, but I was just saying that the main chart on experience doesn't have it listed there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T19:32:03-07:00","id":1324112,"title":"","content":"Soo unrelated to what we have been talking about but I recently reread the history chapter and I gotta say I am not really feeling the optimism. Between the various events in America, Europe, and elsewhere things seem to be leading towards bleakness. Quick example, the new Pope wants to remove the papal decree that states that novas are human and have souls. The city of London is doing all they can to screw over London Fog. And such. It just doesn't feel optimistic. <br /> <br /> Now, I say this, but I also know that in the words of the writers from the various podcasts optimism is what they want to achieve. I'm just not seeing it, not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T20:23:12-07:00","id":1324120,"title":"","content":"I made my point on KS comments, so I will leave just a comment here because you should not be ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T20:32:15-07:00","id":1324124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324120#post1324120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made my point on KS comments, so I will leave just a comment here because you should not be ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your idea of short story seeds in small side panels is BRILLIANT!!! Seriously its perfect. Its also very very necessary. Its the &quot;look yes, things might look bad, but really, its not, and here is why&quot; and then the why is a small seed that could be turned into acts that novas could bring that make the world better, or different, depending. <br /> <br /> YES! So much yes. A million times yes. <br /> <br /> Story seeds, saga seeds, are very very very much needed. But in the back of the book but as one goes through it. That way they can read a section that is 'dark' and then look to the side and see how that darkness could be brightened up by a lovely adventure that players can talk about for years afterward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T20:43:36-07:00","id":1324125,"title":"","content":"On the timeline I got a more optimistic feeling \u2014 until 2026. Even the S\u00e3o Paulo blast is not the worst part of the timeline, Fireman saves millions, becomes a martir, that\u2019s still optimistic.<br /> <br /> Than came the 2027 that is the point when the shit hits the fan (not sure if it\u2019s a English saying, but we say it here in Brazil and it is a very visual description of the Aberrants acting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T20:50:06-07:00","id":1324128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324125#post1324125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the timeline I got a more optimistic feeling \u2014 until 2026. Even the S\u00e3o Paulo blast is not the worst part of the timeline, Fireman saves millions, becomes a martir, that\u2019s still optimistic.<br /> <br /> Than came the 2027 that is the point when the shit hits the fan (not sure if it\u2019s a English saying, but we say it here in Brazil and it is a very visual description of the Aberrants acting).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. I don't mind bad events, they can be nifty. The Sao Paulo blast is all &quot;oooh, look, we have an interesting plot point to investigate, what is going on.&quot; But then we have a politicain banning novas (seriously, that wouldn't fly, you can't ban a class of people - civil rights law apply.) and the murder and then an attack in LA that makes aboslutely no sense, and they even say so, &quot;nobody knows why its done&quot; (Now obivously this is a timeline point, in secret history chapter a reason might be given, but still). and things start going bad.<br /> <br /> All that said the timeline section seems nifty, seems optimistic, seems like good things are happening.<br /> <br /> Then when you start reading the actual N!Sight chapter things fall apart quickly and practically every nation has some darker things going on.<br /> <br /> That said, if your idea is followed and story seeds are given then not all might be lost. Yes, it might be somewhat dark now (darker then I thought it was going to be), but if novas start to act then it can get better.<br /> <br /> PS. And yes, English has the syaing &quot;shit hits the fan&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T21:11:08-07:00","id":1324134,"title":"","content":"The more I read about Project Utopia's technological control division the more I want to cause that division to collapse into the ground. Painfully. <br /> <br /> The idea that they can stop novas from developing things. Yeah, so absolutely not a fan. <br /> <br /> Which leads me to the thought that if I was a Mega-Intelligence nova I would absolutely ignore it. Absolutely. But even more I would do everything I could do to destroy said operation. <br /> <br /> Sooooo, writers, could we have a section in the storyteller's chapter where ideas can be given on how restrictive said Utopia division is.I think that might be a useful thing to have present.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T21:39:36-07:00","id":1324141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324134#post1324134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I read about Project Utopia's technological control division the more I want to cause that division to collapse into the ground. Painfully.<br /> <br /> The idea that they can stop novas from developing things. Yeah, so absolutely not a fan.<br /> <br /> Which leads me to the thought that if I was a Mega-Intelligence nova I would absolutely ignore it. Absolutely. But even more I would do everything I could do to destroy said operation.<br /> <br /> Sooooo, writers, could we have a section in the storyteller's chapter where ideas can be given on how restrictive said Utopia division is.I think that might be a useful thing to have present.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If they're perfectly successful, yeah not fun. But they're not. They have to work over time to stop every potential mad scientist from releasing a nanite plague, or uploading the schimatics for memory-wipe guns onto the internet, etc etc, and they're not always going to succeed. That's a major story hook - so hardly lacking for fun story potential","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T21:44:01-07:00","id":1324143,"title":"","content":"I don't think an optimistic setting has to be without conflict. Overall everything still very much on a upward trend, at least to me. The Novas have already solved a lot of problems, but if they solved all of them there wouldn't be a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T22:01:51-07:00","id":1324147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324143#post1324143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think an optimistic setting has to be without conflict. Overall everything still very much on a upward trend, at least to me. The Novas have already solved a lot of problems, but if they solved all of them there wouldn't be a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah. I mean its not that I don't want conflict its just that I don't want there to be dark things wherever I turn. And maybe I am missing something but I don't see an upward turn as I go through the chapter I see dark thing after dark thing in most nations. The story lines they wrote aren't bad, this isn't that, its just that there seems to be more negative stuff without indication as you read that there are things going on that could fix it. Including them providing some in-text hints at options.<br /> <br /> All I'm just saying is that there could be less everything is bad and more there are bad things but these are some plays potentially in motion to not make all things bad. Oh and look, most of these plays need PC involvement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-13-2019, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T22:17:36-07:00","id":1324150,"title":"","content":"Frankly, Mega-Intelligence is probably the aspect of the setting that gives the most credence to the Null Manifesto: I'll argue up one side of the street and down the other that a Nova that \u201cmerely\u201d has Quantum Powers is still essentially human from a societal standpoint, and ought to fall under the same rules and regulations as everyone else \u2014 with the possible exception of laws that take into account the fact that many of them <i>are</i> lethal weapons. Physical Mega-Attributes are no different. <br /> <br /> But when you start getting into Social and Mental Mega-Attributes, you start getting into a class of novas that arguably don't think or behave like humans anymore. If they're capable of designing whole new governmental systems for a society that work brilliantly but that baselines can't comprehend (a la the Nova that's going to restructure China at some point in the near future), <i>are</i> they still something that's subject to a political system that was designed with baselines in mind? If Mega-Intelligent philosophers are capable of seeing and compensating for the unintended consequences that tend to stymie baseline philosophers, a case could be made for putting them in charge as the philosopher-kings of Plato's Republic; and a key principle of American Declaration of Independence (\u201cWe hold these truths to be self-evident, that all men are created equal\u201d) comes into doubt. <br /> <br /> It's a very disturbing notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-12T22:35:23-07:00","id":1324155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324109#post1324109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd much rather make Body Mods Mega-Edges with non-standard XP costs than to try to shoehorn them into the Quantum Powers where the XP cost is the only thing about them that <i>isn't</i> non-standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, Enhanced Edges aren't supernatural in Core... But maybe Novas will have exclusive Enhanced Edges for stuff like that?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you buy a dot of body-mod and get a pool of things you can get with it?<br /> <br /> Or maybe body mods will just be flair added on to bigger powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T03:07:48-07:00","id":1324175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324155#post1324155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I mean, Enhanced Edges aren't supernatural in Core... But maybe Novas will have exclusive Enhanced Edges for stuff like that?<br /> <br /> Or maybe you buy a dot of body-mod and get a pool of things you can get with it?<br /> <br /> Or maybe body mods will just be flair added on to bigger powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Novas have access to both Enhanced Edges and Mega-Edges. Mega-edges <i>are</i> supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T04:47:10-07:00","id":1324182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324150#post1324150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, Mega-Intelligence is probably the aspect of the setting that gives the most credence to the Null Manifesto: I'll argue up one side of the street and down the other that a Nova that \u201cmerely\u201d has Quantum Powers is still essentially human from a societal standpoint, and ought to fall under the same rules and regulations as everyone else \u2014 with the possible exception of laws that take into account the fact that many of them <i>are</i> lethal weapons. Physical Mega-Attributes are no different. <br /> <br /> But when you start getting into Social and Mental Mega-Attributes, you start getting into a class of novas that arguably don't think or behave like humans anymore. If they're capable of designing whole new governmental systems for a society that work brilliantly but that baselines can't comprehend (a la the Nova that's going to restructure China at some point in the near future), <i>are</i> they still something that's subject to a political system that was designed with baselines in mind? If Mega-Intelligent philosophers are capable of seeing and compensating for the unintended consequences that tend to stymie baseline philosophers, a case could be made for putting them in charge as the philosopher-kings of Plato's Republic; and a key principle of American Declaration of Independence (\u201cWe hold these truths to be self-evident, that all men are created equal\u201d) comes into doubt. <br /> <br /> It's a very disturbing notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s where the Transcendence get you. You can pretend you have super strength using an Ironman suit, or fire quantum blasts with a Q-gun, but you can\u2019t change the way you think. It\u2019s not \u201che have 15 phds\u201d it\u2019s more like \u201che can say what you are thinking by the micro expressions in your face, before you even understand your thought\u201d or \u201cshe is reading the internet... all internet... give her a minute\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T04:59:17-07:00","id":1324185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324150#post1324150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, Mega-Intelligence is probably the aspect of the setting that gives the most credence to the Null Manifesto: I'll argue up one side of the street and down the other that a Nova that \u201cmerely\u201d has Quantum Powers is still essentially human from a societal standpoint, and ought to fall under the same rules and regulations as everyone else \u2014 with the possible exception of laws that take into account the fact that many of them <i>are</i> lethal weapons. Physical Mega-Attributes are no different.<br /> <br /> But when you start getting into Social and Mental Mega-Attributes, you start getting into a class of novas that arguably don't think or behave like humans anymore. If they're capable of designing whole new governmental systems for a society that work brilliantly but that baselines can't comprehend (a la the Nova that's going to restructure China at some point in the near future), <i>are</i> they still something that's subject to a political system that was designed with baselines in mind? If Mega-Intelligent philosophers are capable of seeing and compensating for the unintended consequences that tend to stymie baseline philosophers, a case could be made for putting them in charge as the philosopher-kings of Plato's Republic; and a key principle of American Declaration of Independence (\u201cWe hold these truths to be self-evident, that all men are created equal\u201d) comes into doubt.<br /> <br /> It's a very disturbing notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you on that, those are the biggest reasons for a nova to accept the Null Manifesto. Quantum powers potentially could eventually be copied with science, same with the physical mega-attributes. But the others are much much harder. The only way I can think of scientifically for a baseline to get Mega-Intelligence would be fusing with an AI, a step that quite a few people I've talked to say would mean they aren't human anymore.<br /> <br /> Related to this I really wonder what the Transhumanism community is doing in all of this, especially ones that are actively working on technology, even more so ones that are working on technology that isn't mentioned in the timeline yet like life extension (for example, the SENS foundation led by Aubrey de Grey). It's entirely possible that none of them erupt, especially with only 2000 novas worldwide. Personally I think they would end up as something similar but not the same as the Teragen, namely pushing for research into making it possible for baseline humans to become novas voluntarily.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Going back to a further post, I am also highly excited for a Daedalus League campaign. Personally I'm a fan of Molecular Manipulation type powers, perhaps a nova with that that can either move through space on their own or that has an ally with Warp or similar. Then they work on terraforming a planet, as the best place to start is in making an appropriate atmosphere, which is just molecules.<br /> <br /> Tangent time. Personally I've always seen a lot of overlap between certain types of powers, the big difference being in how you use them. Molecular Manipulation and any power that targets a single type or class of molecule, Gravity Control along with Time Manipulation and Spatial Mastery (as gravity affects space/time and all three are closely related as shown in General Relativity), and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T05:06:12-07:00","id":1324187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324175#post1324175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Novas have access to both Enhanced Edges and Mega-Edges. Mega-edges <i>are</i> supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Enhanced Edges are the 6th dot on the old backgrounds from Adventure, Mega Edges are the old Enhancements (as far as we can understand it).<br /> <br /> Body mods as we see in 1e, will possibly cost non standard XP as it did on 1e. It\u2019s unfair to compare Bioluminecence to Quantum Blast or Mega-Cunning.<br /> <br /> The requisites to get the body mods is another question, if you need a minimum quantum or a minimum stamina, or a minimum mega-stamina, it should be case by case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T08:36:10-07:00","id":1324214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324175#post1324175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Novas have access to both Enhanced Edges and Mega-Edges. Mega-edges <i>are</i> supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesss, but mega edges are 12 XP and we\u2019re talking about things that ain\u2019t really worth 12 XP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T09:46:49-07:00","id":1324220,"title":"","content":"Thus, non-standard XP costs for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T16:01:36-07:00","id":1324292,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking up a nova character using the power ideas from 1e with the costs of 2e and I realized that if Quantum minimums for powers are still as they were my character would have to spend 64 xp to get to Quantum 5 in order to get the powers he wants. I not saying this is bad per say but it is interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T18:26:11-07:00","id":1324319,"title":"","content":"I think with Steve Kenson on board, we don't have to worry about irregular and/or confusing powers. What I'm looking forward to are the Templates that Steve mentioned, for people whoa re Tanks/Bricks, Speedsters, Mentalists, Masterminds, etc. Seems odd, but given how superheroes have saturated modern media, it does make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T18:29:28-07:00","id":1324321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324319#post1324319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think with Steve Kenson on board, we don't have to worry about irregular and/or confusing powers. What I'm looking forward to are the Templates that Steve mentioned, for people whoa re Tanks/Bricks, Speedsters, Mentalists, Masterminds, etc. Seems odd, but given how superheroes have saturated modern media, it does make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I agree. The mention that there will be templates was quite encouraging, as was the fact that they aren't required they are just suggestion to make design easier. But yeah, he knows his super power creation stuff and so I figure its going to be a much smoother design then 1e. <br /> <br /> I'm imagining a character with all Mega-Attributes plus one or two other powers, and its looking fun! <br /> <br /> Is it Tuesday yet? hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T18:41:27-07:00","id":1324323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324321#post1324321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm imagining a character with all Mega-Attributes plus one or two other powers, and its looking fun!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It is. Very much.<br /> <br /> Take the Mega-Enhancements (Mega-Edges probably now?) that let you change your appearance at will. I did it, and my character never, ever had the same appearance twice. Nobody knew what &quot;Nathan&quot; looked like, or if that was even his name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","user":"Jetstream","date":". 07-13-2019, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T18:57:56-07:00","id":1324327,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3487_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3487\" data-vbnamecard=\"3487\">Jetstream</a> and really any others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So besides the Mega-Attributes I'm thinking he will have the equivalent of Information Manipulation* and Spatial Manipulation plus something energy related, though I don't know what that is. Which leads me to the question - what sort of energy do you think would fit a character with said power groups. <br /> <br /> *From this I see him gaining powers related to telepathy (mind information) and cyberkinesis (technology information. Actually, when one thinks about it, there is much that can be done with the power theme of 'Information.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T19:51:15-07:00","id":1324333,"title":"","content":"If you use the idea of Data = Correspondence from Mage the Ascension, than you are pretty much on the same place (pun...)<br /> <br /> Space rupture is a nice \u201cenergy\u201d for blasts and shields, but if you mean real energy, I don\u2019t know, electricity is related with both brain and computers... but it\u2019s not very much information per se.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T20:04:07-07:00","id":1324335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324327#post1324327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3487_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3487\" data-vbnamecard=\"3487\">Jetstream</a> and really any others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So besides the Mega-Attributes I'm thinking he will have the equivalent of Information Manipulation* and Spatial Manipulation plus something energy related, though I don't know what that is. Which leads me to the question - what sort of energy do you think would fit a character with said power groups.<br /> <br /> *From this I see him gaining powers related to telepathy (mind information) and cyberkinesis (technology information. Actually, when one thinks about it, there is much that can be done with the power theme of 'Information.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm... Soincs/Sound, maybe? That can lend itself to more expansion into subtle, mess-with-people powers, which you seem to be going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T20:06:09-07:00","id":1324336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324333#post1324333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use the idea of Data = Correspondence from Mage the Ascension, than you are pretty much on the same place (pun...)<br /> <br /> Space rupture is a nice \u201cenergy\u201d for blasts and shields, but if you mean real energy, I don\u2019t know, electricity is related with both brain and computers... but it\u2019s not very much information per se.</div> </div> </div> </div>They say that novas often gain powers in areas they lacked, so maybe he was a man who didn't really like to drive or travel long distances, and so with Spatial Manipulation he can make the there here very easily.<br /> <br /> Hmm, so I could see either maybe Gravitic Control (since gravity is a fundamental force and also related to space OR I could see something like Elemental Mastery (Electricity). With Electricity being related to the way both mind and machine works, and other such related things. Hmm. I'm not sure which works the best for me.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324335#post1324335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm... Soincs/Sound, maybe? That can lend itself to more expansion into subtle, mess-with-people powers, which you seem to be going for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Sound. Interesting. I could kind of see it. Hmm. Gotta think on how he would represent that. Hmm<br /> <br /> That said, what do you think between the idea of Gravity and Electricity? <br /> <br /> On the mess-with-people powers yeah, kinda. Though not intentionally at first. I think it was more the idea that information interests him, which then he segways into machines and then (maybe after he starts his business) into finding ways to, well, manipulate people. <br /> <br /> Its just a random character thought, lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-13-2019, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T20:15:52-07:00","id":1324340,"title":"","content":"Between Gravity and Electricity I would go for gravity, it\u2019s more related to space, but honestly not sure about the connection between space and information (other than Mage)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-13T20:23:10-07:00","id":1324342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324340#post1324340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between Gravity and Electricity I would go for gravity, it\u2019s more related to space, but honestly not sure about the connection between space and information (other than Mage)</div> </div> </div> </div>There really isn't - his ability to have space powers is more a wish fulfilment power than related to the other. Also known as I want him to have it and so he is having it. lol<br /> <br /> Hmm <br /> <br /> You know I might just go with Information Manipulation and Spatial Manipulation at first, then in time he can expand to the other directions of say Gravity and Cyberkinesis and maybe Electrical Mastery and the other powers linked to either information or space. And you know stuff. <br /> <br /> I don't want to think too deeply because obviously lots of things could change come Tuesday when we see powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T01:31:20-07:00","id":1324382,"title":"","content":"Re: Dormancy<br /> <br /> I'm more of a tangential comics fan than a true comics nerd, but I've always been a big rpg nerd, so I tend to see Dormancy in terms of the narratives it enables for players/GMs.<br /> <br /> As a player:<ul><li>Live double lives, potentially in conflict (A famous Elite maintains a residence in a small, nova-phobic town, attends church, and home-schools his kids)</li> <li>Play a character who has difficulty working with the baseline world (ala the Thing), but can set that part aside for a time, at the expense of not having easy access to the juice. It's somewhat obvious, but with a good ST the hard choices are delicious.</li> <li>Choose to infiltrate a place like the Church of Michael Archangel as a baseline, and see how far you get without kewl powerz at your side</li> <li>Potentially play a pre N-day Nova who just hid for weeks/months/years, like nu-Pax. This doesn't require Dormancy, but it seems fun to play someone so scared by their powers they subconsciously took them away. This reminds me of the Novel Diamond Mask by Julian May.</li> </ul>As a ST:<ul><li>Put characters in situations where their powers/public personas really are *not* the answer, and are in fact a liability.</li> <li>Introduce a &quot;baseline&quot; recurring NPC who is a sleeper agent. It's pretty normal in high-powered games for players to disregard normies, and I love exploiting those blind spots.</li> <li>Say &quot;yes&quot; to a character whose powers/aberrations would normally make my inner ST voice say &quot;Problem character decloaking! Red Alert!&quot; Rogue could be a serious PITA as a PC, but in the hands of a thoughtful player, such a character with Dormancy wouldn't necessarily steal all the shine.</li> </ul>Re: Post-Human<br /> <br /> I wouldn't assume having &quot;physical&quot; powers isn't an existential experience. Imagine being blind for half your life and then gaining sight. Your experiences change, and experiences drive our self. In that case, your new experiences more closely mirror the mainstream human experience. Now, instead consider that you can move in three dimensions with a thought. Eventually, that capability becomes a part of you, much like sight, except hardly anybody shares that experience.<br /> <br /> There's a big difference between being a guy with an advanced flame thrower on his arm, and literally controlling heat and flame with a thought If you can think of a place you've been, and instantly be there, how does that change you? Do you walk from room-to-room regularly? Do you tend to forget that other people have to get in a car to go places, and might not want to meet you at 5:15 across town?<br /> <br /> These are maybe small things, but it's those little experiences/differences that cause people to change. And many Novas, due to their &quot;fingerprint&quot; of capabilities, might have *nobody* who really knows that it's like to be them.<br /> <br /> That's both amazing and lonely. Maybe it drives them to the Null Manifesto. Maybe they become hermits. Maybe it takes them to a dark and dangerous place.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> I think part of the tendency to disregard the psychological impact of these experiences is the damned short-hand of modern media: the word &quot;powers.&quot; It externalizes experiences that ought to be profound, intimate, even defining (in our 21st century parlance, part of one's identity), and sucks the wonder and mystery out of otherwise great narratives.<br /> <br /> I've seen this corrosive short-hand used to describe everything from magic users to demons and angels, and even a couple times in pulpy sci-fi. About the only place it makes sense is in comics, and while Aberrant is a game inspired by comics, at its best it's broader than a simple four-color spread.<br /> <br /> This isn't intended to sound preachy; people should have their own fun with their pretend-time-elf-games. The most fun I've had with Aberrant wasn't playing some dude with powers. It was the guilty Catholic teen who said to himself, in a moment of rage, said &quot;What kind of God would allow this...&quot; and found himself crowned with molten light. It was the average college guy who manipulated space-time, was fighting multiple Elites, and summoned duplicates of himself from *somewhere*. Not all of the dupes made it out alive. He was mentally f*cked for weeks.<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR:</b> Skew isn't just a guy with magnetokinesis powers; he can have a moment of rage and pull down a skyscraper. That sh*t changes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","user":"Totentanz","date":".  typo 07-14-2019, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T04:11:57-07:00","id":1324407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324382#post1324382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the tendency to disregard the psychological impact of these experiences is the damned short-hand of modern media: the word &quot;powers.&quot; It externalizes experiences that ought to be profound, intimate, even defining (in our 21st century parlance, part of one's identity), and sucks the wonder and mystery out of otherwise great narratives.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point. For the record when I said that it was potentially possible to do quantum powers with science I wasn't talking about with technology we would understand in our modern times. I was talking about ten thousand or more years from now. <br /> <br /> But yes, the psychological impact is very important, and I did disregard it because I didn't think about how most people aren't going to think of technology and science like I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T07:04:04-07:00","id":1324449,"title":"","content":"My point about drawing a distinction between physical abilities and mental abilities wasn't that physical abilities don't have a psychological impact; it's that mental Mega-Attributes objectively bring into question whether the nova still qualifies as human. Asimov's \u201cthe Bicentennial Man\u201d featured a robot who wanted to be recognized by the law as a human being; in pursuit of that objective, he replaced every part of his body with prosthetics that humans used to replace missing body parts so that he could argue that there was no part of him that disqualified a human from being human. But the one part of himself that he couldn't replace was his positronic brain; and the courts ruled that as long as his mind was that of a robot, he was still a robot. <br /> <br /> In a similar way, a nova who develops physical superhuman abilities may identify with the Null Manifesto and <i>think</i> of himself as transhuman or even post-human; but as long as his mind is still human, so is he, no matter how drastic the physical changes he undergoes. But when his <i>mind</i> starts transforming, <i>then</i> there might actually be some <i>truth</i> to his claim of no longer being human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T07:07:59-07:00","id":1324450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324449#post1324449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point about drawing a distinction between physical abilities and mental abilities wasn't that physical abilities don't have a psychological impact; it's that mental Mega-Attributes objectively bring into question whether the nova still qualifies as human. Asimov's \u201cthe Bicentennial Man\u201d featured a robot who wanted to be recognized by the law as a human being; in pursuit of that objective, he replaced every part of his body with prosthetics that humans used to replace missing body parts so that he could argue that there was no part of him that disqualified a human from being human. But the one part of himself that he couldn't replace was his positronic brain; and the courts ruled that as long as his mind was that of a robot, he was still a robot.<br /> <br /> In a similar way, a nova who develops physical superhuman abilities may identify with the Null Manifesto and <i>think</i> of himself as transhuman or even post-human; but as long as his mind is still human, so is he, no matter how drastic the physical changes he undergoes. But when his <i>mind</i> starts transforming, <i>then</i> there might actually be some <i>truth</i> to his claim of no longer being human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Transformations can also create a neurological distance that qualifies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T07:23:11-07:00","id":1324457,"title":"","content":"I don't think so. The only Transformations I'm seeing that arguably affect how the mind works are the Psychological Shifts and Disorders; and I'm very leery about reclassifying someone as \u201cother than human\u201d because he has mental problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T07:28:06-07:00","id":1324459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324457#post1324457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so. The only Transformations I'm seeing that arguably affect how the mind works are the Psychological Shifts and Disorders; and I'm very leery about reclassifying someone as \u201cother than human\u201d because he has mental problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. However, there are quantifiable difficulties in forming bonds with humans as your Transcendence increases. That suggests there's <i>something</i> going on there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T07:37:25-07:00","id":1324462,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if you are an active radiation source, your mental balance will go down really fast as you can\u2019t touch people, most of the objects and even many novas without harming or even destroying them completely. It\u2019s. It in the rules, but think about it...<br /> <br /> It applies to other transformations too, on different degree...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T11:42:22-07:00","id":1324536,"title":"","content":"Ok, finally remembered this forum existed.<br /> Mega-attributes. YES, this is great. exploration of scale and abilities based around it. I will await more, but what was shown I love.<br /> <br /> Now to discover America<br /> Transcendence- It is a bad term for what the scale(for lack of better term represents). It does not truly represent the transcendence of nova. it is more of a secondary descriptor. Quantum is the true transcendental Stat describing how far you have risen from baseline humanity. <br /> <br /> I propose the name Dissonance, instead. It fits better, describes the end state significantly more and it fits the narrative, with rising quantum your dissonance with the world rises. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T11:57:08-07:00","id":1324544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324536#post1324536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transcendence- It is a bad term for what the scale(for lack of better term represents). It does not truly represent the transcendence of nova. it is more of a secondary descriptor. Quantum is the true transcendental Stat describing how far you have risen from baseline humanity.<br /> <br /> I propose the name Dissonance, instead. It fits better, describes the end state significantly more and it fits the narrative, with rising quantum your dissonance with the world rises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dissonance, I like that. Much better than Transcendence. Also works a lot better in concept as well. If they keep it as it is I might have to mentally change it to Dissonance in my games. <br /> <br /> Nice!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T13:34:48-07:00","id":1324554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324536#post1324536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, finally remembered this forum existed.<br /> Mega-attributes. YES, this is great. exploration of scale and abilities based around it. I will await more, but what was shown I love.<br /> <br /> Now to discover America<br /> Transcendence- It is a bad term for what the scale(for lack of better term represents). It does not truly represent the transcendence of nova. it is more of a secondary descriptor. Quantum is the true transcendental Stat describing how far you have risen from baseline humanity.<br /> <br /> I propose the name Dissonance, instead. It fits better, describes the end state significantly more and it fits the narrative, with rising quantum your dissonance with the world rises.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324544#post1324544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dissonance, I like that. Much better than Transcendence. Also works a lot better in concept as well. If they keep it as it is I might have to mentally change it to Dissonance in my games.<br /> <br /> Nice!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When I played around and homeruled this game in other systems, back in the day, I used the term <b><i>Alienation</i></b>. It narrowed down the feeling I wanted to get from Permanent Taint, and it didn't include the word Taint. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-14T15:43:20-07:00","id":1324564,"title":"","content":"Oooooh yeah! 87k baby! Awesome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Was hoping that it would be achieved before Sunday evening and it was. <br /> <br /> Now I'm looking forward to seeing what sort of stretch goals exist. I for one hoping something like In Media Res Aberrant Edition is included. That or something with technology or potential plotlines. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T08:35:23-07:00","id":1324739,"title":"","content":"Instead of non-standard XP costs for Body Mod, I'd rather you pay the standard amount for a level of it and get a pool of points to spend within the power. One level might be worth five Body Mod points, which could get you tentacles, bio-luminescence, and gills, if those added up to five points.<br /> <br /> As for Dormancy, was always used in our groups for two things: removing annoying Transformations when you don't need to be using your powers (especially if they had iconic Transformations which let them have normal lives outside of being a Nova or wanted to hide in plain sight) and for hiding from someone using your quantum signature to find you. I guess that second part is less of an issue without M-R Nodes in this version. Aberrant is a game of celebrity as much as superheroism. So being able to avoid the paparazzi has its benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T17:56:40-07:00","id":1324841,"title":"","content":"The Babel Dossier is basically Warehouse 13, and I love it. So many interesting nuggets in the Paths chapter. Any kind of game style is possible, really. Be Warehouse 13 and search for lost wonders, be Team 7 and go to war, be the Suicide Squad and work in the shadows, go full-on Punisher on criminals, or just be the plain old Justice League. You can even do The Office, but you're paper-pushing for Project Utopia. So many options, it's great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-15T23:53:25-07:00","id":1324899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324841#post1324841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Babel Dossier is basically Warehouse 13, and I love it. So many interesting nuggets in the Paths chapter. Any kind of game style is possible, really. Be Warehouse 13 and search for lost wonders, be Team 7 and go to war, be the Suicide Squad and work in the shadows, go full-on Punisher on criminals, or just be the plain old Justice League. You can even do The Office, but you're paper-pushing for Project Utopia. So many options, it's great.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, I'm glad your imagination's getting fired up. <b>Aeon</b> was always a kitchen sink sci-fi setting, and we wanted to do the same thing with <b>Aberrant</b>. The first edition was kind of limited in scope -- it did its thing, and it did it well, but it didn't allow for a lot of other playstyles. I'm glad we seem to be pulling that off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T09:42:04-07:00","id":1324986,"title":"","content":"<br /> I LOVE the Mega-Attributes and the Mega-Edges, they are quite brilliant. I especially like how while reading over the abilities I was like &quot;I want that, and that, and that, and that...&quot; so many times. The fact that some of what was powers in the previous edition is edges in this one is also brilliant. It also simplifies some of the complexity of 1e, in areas that didn't really need to be that complex. Going over the abilities I can totally see how combining some of them together in a character could give the player the power spread they might want, so that is nifty. <br /> <br /> I do, of course, have to read through it in more detail to truly get the understanding of it all, but what I see I like. <br /> <br /> On Powers, well, funny enough, I like them less than the Mega-Edges, lol. BUT, like the other, I need to read over it more to see how I could build what I want to build. I figure frame works and themes would allow me to do what I want.<br /> <br /> For example I could see some Mega-Edges and some powers being used to build Information Mastery, the same with Spatial Manipulation. The difference is that in the old game you had a single category already given description for that while in this one you have to pick what fits you, then add the tags and such, to make the character's powers what you want. Its not bad, not at all, but its different enough to require a bit more thought - which is not, very much not, a bad thing. <br /> <br /> Soooo while I totally get, and understand and accept why telepathy and precog are not generlaly nova based powers in relation to the whole Trinity Continuum of Aeon and such, I also think telepathy is a supers power category that deserves to be available for games that don't involve the whole Continuum and the nature of psi and such. Which makes me wonder how one thinks one would write up a telepathy power in Quantum power terms. <br /> <br /> As a negative there is the whole maxing out a power and thus getting flux to upgrade or purchase new abilities. Yeah, not a fan of that and I won't be using that rule. Not unless there are other and better ways that mitigate flux, which I don't see at first glance. <br /> <br /> Additionally, the whole Quantum 10 going somewhere else, becoming something else, is what transcendence is, rather than how the term is being used in reference to negative flux. <br /> <br /> I also notice that there is Horror subgenre where Flux is made all the worse, I wish there was the opposite of that where Flux was given rules mitigating it even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T11:37:11-07:00","id":1325019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324986#post1324986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Soooo while I totally get, and understand and accept why telepathy and precog are not generlaly nova based powers in relation to the whole Trinity Continuum of Aeon and such, I also think telepathy is a supers power category that deserves to be available for games that don't involve the whole Continuum and the nature of psi and such. Which makes me wonder how one thinks one would write up a telepathy power in Quantum power terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>More immediately, this change calls for a change in some iconics as well. Psyche of T2M must now be a Psiad, Corbin's emotion warp field is a collection of edges out of control, Anna DeVries no longer has her emergency Mind bullets.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, I see they're trying harder to make the powers more modular, like in Mutants &amp; Masterminds 3e, which will be GREAT for customization. Though here seem to be some lingering redundancies. Like how Deadly and Aggravated as tags seem to be the same thing. Blinding and Deafening are the same applied to different senses which makes me think they could be condensed maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T11:41:34-07:00","id":1325021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325019#post1325019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More immediately, this change calls for a change in some iconics as well. Psyche of T2M must now be a Psiad, Corbin's emotion warp field is a collection of edges out of control, Anna DeVries no longer has her emergency Mind bullets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly the more I think about it the more I am not a fan of this divide. The supers genre has a long history of characters with mental abilities as ionic, and I would never say they are Psiads. I think its them trying to be a bit to niche in power, a fact which I don't really think is necessary. There are already differences, good differences, that make playing a nova different from playing a psiad. A limitation on mind effecting and future sight abilities is not necessary for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T11:54:55-07:00","id":1325026,"title":"","content":"Future-sight, that's another thing. If I can control time with Time Manipulation abilities, why is it impossible for me to look ahead or behind using time itself? It seems a little too odd that a Psiad &quot;Clear&quot; can look ahead and see what'll happen or look behind to see what already happened, when a Nova &quot;Timelord&quot; can stop, rewind, fast-forward, or recall items in time itself. Psiads/psions as I recall can't even manipulate time can they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T12:05:38-07:00","id":1325031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325026#post1325026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Future-sight, that's another thing. If I can control time with Time Manipulation abilities, why is it impossible for me to look ahead or behind using time itself? It seems a little too odd that a Psiad &quot;Clear&quot; can look ahead and see what'll happen or look behind to see what already happened, when a Nova &quot;Timelord&quot; can stop, rewind, fast-forward, or recall items in time itself. Psiads/psions as I recall can't even manipulate time can they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, and in no way something I like, the answer is that they removed time from the power capabilities of novas. (At least at first glance).<br /> <br /> Edit - So at second glance its now a theme of Elemental Mastery. Though I am not entirely sure on what can and cannot be done based on the new rules. <br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Actually, speaking of Elemental Mastery, so Space is listed as a theme which makes me wonder if I could have Information be a theme. Hmm. I have to see how the rules work exactly to see how such a thing is (hopefully) possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-16-2019, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T12:53:49-07:00","id":1325043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325031#post1325031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, and in no way something I like, the answer is that they removed time from the power capabilities of novas. (At least at first glance).<br /> <br /> Edit - So at second glance its now a theme of Elemental Mastery. Though I am not entirely sure on what can and cannot be done based on the new rules.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Actually, speaking of Elemental Mastery, so Space is listed as a theme which makes me wonder if I could have Information be a theme. Hmm. I have to see how the rules work exactly to see how such a thing is (hopefully) possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be part of the power rules pertaining to construction of themes and addition of techniques missing(hopefully), but informaton should be valid. Grab elemental mastery pertining to infromation and build in the necessary techniques, dd mega intellect and edges for hacking and so and you are golden .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T13:33:04-07:00","id":1325054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325043#post1325043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There seems to be part of the power rules pertaining to construction of themes and addition of techniques missing(hopefully), but informaton should be valid. Grab elemental mastery pertining to infromation and build in the necessary techniques, dd mega intellect and edges for hacking and so and you are golden .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, more examples on how it all works might be helpful. That said we have only had access to it for a few hours now so there is plenty of time for us (me very much so) to truly figure it out. <br /> <br /> That said its pretty awesome that one can use Elemental Mastery for Information and such. Very cool. <br /> <br /> That said, is there any XP benefit to purchasing a Mega-Edge as a technique in comparison to purchasing it on its own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T14:01:07-07:00","id":1325059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325054#post1325054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, is there any XP benefit to purchasing a Mega-Edge as a technique in comparison to purchasing it on its own?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think only powers can be bought as techniques. If I get it and I might highly probably not. You buy technique for one dot and use the dots of the parent power for the numbers, with the limitation /caveat of fewer tags bought and for the purpose of shutting off powers the techniques cannot be used if parent power is shut down. Narratively they should also fit the same theme and there seem to be possible rule restrictions, but that feels unclear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T14:14:31-07:00","id":1325061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325059#post1325059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think only powers can be bought as techniques. If I get it and I might highly probably not. You buy technique for one dot and use the dots of the parent power for the numbers, with the limitation /caveat of fewer tags bought and for the purpose of shutting off powers the techniques cannot be used if parent power is shut down. Narratively they should also fit the same theme and there seem to be possible rule restrictions, but that feels unclear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So it seems that the Elemental Mastery list of themes contains words that say &quot;Mega-Edge xxyy can be bought as a Technique&quot; while the power suite, power theme, and technique sections all say 'power'. So I am not entirely sure. <br /> <br /> BUT lets assume fora moment Mega-Edges can be included in a power suite. If so then one's dot in the underlying Elemental Mastery grants the powers of the Mega-Edge up to that dot. <br /> <br /> BUT if something shuts off said power then all things related to it shut off. Which could be bad if your Adapatibility Mega-Edge is part of your Space Mastery or Nature Mastery suite. <br /> <br /> All that said the benefit, you pay 12 xp for essentially a lot of dots, doesn't apply to one dot Mega-Edges, so for them simply buy it as its own is safer. <br /> <br /> This does come in handy though as if you want four different say Quantum Bolt attacks you don't have to spend 4 x dot rating in attacks you spend four powers and get them at the origional Quantum Bolt's rating. <br /> <br /> This comment is as much for others as it is for me to get a feel for what is going on. Which, really, is nifty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T14:49:58-07:00","id":1325068,"title":"","content":"I did like how I could slap the Variable tag on Q-attack to create an energy blast I can shape into a beam, cone, explosion, or piercing bolt. That's sooo much more efficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T15:02:31-07:00","id":1325070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325068#post1325068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did like how I could slap the Variable tag on Q-attack to create an energy blast I can shape into a beam, cone, explosion, or piercing bolt. That's sooo much more efficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think once we really get a feel for the tag system we are going to love it. I mean the more I go &quot;oh I can do that!&quot; the more I grin on how awesome and personal the powers can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T15:06:44-07:00","id":1325071,"title":"","content":"If you ever play M&amp;M you get an advantage. The idea of buying multiple powers with one tag is part of if for a while now, and it\u2019s great.<br /> The variable tag and the technique tags are extremely useful, but can be a weakness against powers that copy/cancel/steal powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T15:41:55-07:00","id":1325074,"title":"","content":"I have access to 2nd Edition M&amp;M so while I recognizr the material its been a long time since I actively read through or used it. <br /> <br /> That said I think I'm getting the hang of it. So here is my thoughts. <br /> <br /> I am a nova. I purchased Elemental Mastery Fire. The basic effect choose is Elemental Anima. I have the power at 3 Dots and there are 2 tags. <br /> <br /> I buy Technique Tag and Quantum Attack Fire. I can have up to 3 dots and 2 tags in said power. (the third tag is technically the technique slot that allows for it, so its blocked.) <br /> <br /> Now related, instead of using 2 tags for said power, I can have one of those tags be Technique for a second Quantum Attack, which is also 3 dots but only has 1 tag available. <br /> <br /> I think go back to my orgonal and purchase a third tag for Elemental Anima. This then boosts the first Quantum Attack by 1 tag, leading to three free, and the second Quantum Attack, leading to 2 tag slots free. <br /> <br /> I then decide to purchase Shroud, which is at three dots and 3 tags. <br /> <br /> I then decide to purchase a forth dot in Elemental Mastery, which increases the Anima, the two attacks, and the forth shroud by one dot, to four.<br /> <br /> But then I decide to purchase Flight but I only want it to be at 1 dots and 1 tag, despite the fact I have three dots and 2 more tags available. <br /> <br /> I only spent base effect (4 dot, 3 tags) and 3 techniques. basically saving the cost of buying 4 dots and 3 tags 3 additional times.<br /> <br /> Is this all right. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:21:39-07:00","id":1325081,"title":"","content":"I will make it a bit easier to understand.<br /> <br /> You have a Power with 3 dots and 4 tags. You add a technique to it, it\u2019s not a power, it\u2019s just a Technique, a part of the power, imprinted, disrupted, or anything as part of the power.<br /> <br /> The technique is created the same way as the power, using the same dots and tags, and it\u2019s forced to have all the technique tags (it\u2019s easier to ignore all the technique tags), so if the Power have 3 dots and 6 tags (2 of them are techniques) the Technique 1 must have 3 or less dots and 6 or less tags (2 of them technique tags) and the Technique 2 the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:32:22-07:00","id":1325083,"title":"","content":"Essentially you can cascade your powers into an array of techniques that stem from the base power at the cost of losing a slot to the &quot;technique&quot; tag each time you do this. That's not as insane as M&amp;M2e was where you could just overclock the base power and spend 2 points per sub-power to create an array of dynamic high-level powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:33:15-07:00","id":1325084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325081#post1325081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will make it a bit easier to understand.<br /> <br /> You have a Power with 3 dots and 4 tags. You add a technique to it, it\u2019s not a power, it\u2019s just a Technique, a part of the power, imprinted, disrupted, or anything as part of the power.<br /> <br /> The technique is created the same way as the power, using the same dots and tags, and it\u2019s forced to have all the technique tags (it\u2019s easier to ignore all the technique tags), so if the Power have 3 dots and 6 tags (2 of them are techniques) the Technique 1 must have 3 or less dots and 6 or less tags (2 of them technique tags) and the Technique 2 the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, are you saying the Tags that a technique has has to be the same as the tags of the core power?<br /> <br /> If that is not what you are saying, rather that the number can't go over as a maximum, then yeah, I get it.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I am ignoring all the technique tags, they are there invisible and paid for but not written out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325083#post1325083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially you can cascade your powers into an array of techniques that stem from the base power at the cost of losing a slot to the &quot;technique&quot; tag each time you do this. That's not as insane as M&amp;M2e was where you could just overclock the base power and spend 2 points per sub-power to create an array of dynamic high-level powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its funny reading the book about technique tags needing to be shared sounded so complicated but if you just assume its there but invisible then it all works out. I mean you are spending 12 XP for each new technique, so the rules are followed. You just aren't writing out Technique on each sub power and wasting space. <br /> <br /> That all said I hope I am right in that the Tags of a technique do not have to be the same tags of the base power, and the amount of dots and tags do not have to equal, but simply can't go over. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-16-2019, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:39:27-07:00","id":1325085,"title":"","content":"No, the tags don\u2019t need to be the same just the tags named technique (to differ it from the Techniques, the power bought with the technique tag)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:41:54-07:00","id":1325086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325083#post1325083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially you can cascade your powers into an array of techniques that stem from the base power at the cost of losing a slot to the &amp;quot;technique&amp;quot; tag each time you do this. That's not as insane as M&amp;M2e was where you could just overclock the base power and spend 2 points per sub-power to create an array of dynamic high-level powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are basically overclocking it for every technique, but the idea is the same as M&amp;M.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:43:03-07:00","id":1325087,"title":"","content":"Now here are two side questions - <br /> <br /> 1) Can I add a Mega-Edge to a Power Array? <br /> <br /> The Elemental Mastery power makes it seem like I can. <br /> <br /> 2) Can I add Tags to Mega-Edges. <br /> <br /> One of the mentions in the section about tags makes it seem like I can. <br /> <br /> If 2 is a YES then can I say use the Area Tag to make a Mega-Edge that has a single target now target an area? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T16:56:33-07:00","id":1325090,"title":"","content":"1) I think yes, but not Mega-Attributes.<br /> 2) I think there are a few that can receive tags, and, if the objective is to be flexible, they all should be able to receive tags.<br /> 2.5) probably, but maybe it\u2019s going to be a bit too powerful. As a SG Inwould allow but if you overuse it I would ask for more XP as the area tag is Worthing more tags than you spent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T17:01:56-07:00","id":1325092,"title":"","content":"My house rules so far are:<br /> Novas Q1 or 2 are Tier 2 characters, from Q3 are Tier 3, and Q6 Tier 4<br /> Novas Tier 3 can have up to 6 dots in Attributes and 7 with Superior Trait Edge.<br /> Novas Tier 4 can have up to 7 dots in Attributes and 8 with Superior Trait Edge. <br /> Mega-Attributes are limited only to the Quantum value and not to baseline Attributes.<br /> Transcendence 10 don\u2019t mean you are out of the game, but you get 2 additional severe Transformations and are treated as permanent quantum instability (unless you have que quantum Stability Mega-Edge)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-16-2019, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T17:04:10-07:00","id":1325094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325090#post1325090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I think yes, but not Mega-Attributes.<br /> 2) I think there are a few that can receive tags, and, if the objective is to be flexible, they all should be able to receive tags.<br /> 2.5) probably, but maybe it\u2019s going to be a bit too powerful. As a SG Inwould allow but if you overuse it I would ask for more XP as the area tag is Worthing more tags than you spent.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yeah, I would never think Mega-Attributes could or should be in a theme. <br /> <br /> Though that said I guess someone like the Hulk might have them in a theme. hmm. <br /> <br /> But no, I am fine with saying the Mega-Attributes are so basic on a quantum level that they have to be on their own. <br /> <br /> 2) I think the ability to make Mega-Edges super flexible is a positive one. <br /> <br /> But I also like the idea on being able to take a Mega-edge that effects one person at base and say now it affects all within range. That's pretty cool. <br /> <br /> On the increase of XP costs, in some ways I can see that, but at the same time it seems that the XP costs in Aberrant are very consistent. I mean even Body Modification costs 12 XP for each feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T17:09:53-07:00","id":1325100,"title":"","content":"Thank the OPP Elder Gods that we've got example NPCs coming out with the Proteus Nova Companion! We <b>NEED EXAMPLES</b> of how to wrangle some of these powers into a usable format so that we and our fellow players know what to expect from a power at the table. I'd like to see Telekinesis Mastery, Light Mastery, Entropy Mastery, Magnetic Mastery, etc. kind of written out so that I know how the developers pictured these powers looking. How is Invulnerability done now? Deflection? Not quite sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T17:30:09-07:00","id":1325108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpectacularTentacular</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325100#post1325100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank the OPP Elder Gods that we've got example NPCs coming out with the Proteus Nova Companion! We <b>NEED EXAMPLES</b> of how to wrangle some of these powers into a usable format so that we and our fellow players know what to expect from a power at the table. I'd like to see Telekinesis Mastery, Light Mastery, Entropy Mastery, Magnetic Mastery, etc. kind of written out so that I know how the developers pictured these powers looking. How is Invulnerability done now? Deflection? Not quite sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this. <br /> <br /> There are so many options, and they are all great options, that its hard to know exactly what can and cannot be done, or more to the point, how to do it. So yeah having NPCs described and statted out in ways that let us see the writeup of their powers is going to be really really super awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T19:53:57-07:00","id":1325131,"title":"","content":"So question. While most of the powers make perfect sense I feel like I am missing something when it comes to Teleport and Warp. Both powers have no dice rolls. They just are. Which means what stops a nova with Warp from looking the moon, spending 2 quantum, and then opening up a portal between here and there. <br /> <br /> I mean the Range stat for Warp isn't even how far you can go, its how close the entrance portal is. <br /> <br /> I would have thought some sort of die roll would be needed with successes based on distance and such. <br /> <br /> So I am curious as to what I am missing, or if I am missing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T21:31:00-07:00","id":1325149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325131#post1325131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So question. While most of the powers make perfect sense I feel like I am missing something when it comes to Teleport and Warp. Both powers have no dice rolls. They just are. Which means what stops a nova with Warp from looking the moon, spending 2 quantum, and then opening up a portal between here and there.<br /> <br /> I mean the Range stat for Warp isn't even how far you can go, its how close the entrance portal is.<br /> <br /> I would have thought some sort of die roll would be needed with successes based on distance and such.<br /> <br /> So I am curious as to what I am missing, or if I am missing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far as I can tell &quot;spend points, go to moon&quot; is a legitimate use of Teleport/Warp. Surviving the vacuum of space and the radiation there in is another matter (and different powers/edges) all together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T23:17:10-07:00","id":1325162,"title":"","content":"Warp mentions that you can open a gate to \u201ca celestial body visible in the sky\u201d. Forget the Moon; Alpha Centauri is visible in the sky. Novas with Warp can be interstellar explorers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T23:21:57-07:00","id":1325163,"title":"","content":"Also: my understanding is that a Time Master can speed up it's allow down the flow of time; but \u201cteleporting\u201d to the future or past \u2014 visiting other times \u2014 is beyond its purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-16T23:53:14-07:00","id":1325170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325163#post1325163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: my understanding is that a Time Master can speed up it's allow down the flow of time; but \u201cteleporting\u201d to the future or past \u2014 visiting other times \u2014 is beyond its purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, shall we say, suspicions about where time travel powers for each of the Inspired might pop up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:25:57-07:00","id":1325214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325170#post1325170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have, shall we say, suspicions about where time travel powers for each of the Inspired might pop up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Max Mercer is the nova-level equivalent of a Talent, that's pretty easy to guess, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:27:17-07:00","id":1325215,"title":"","content":"Can we get an extra document where the devs stat up various superheroes from fiction? Like Wolverine, Superman, Iron Man, etc.<br /> If not that, can we get some &quot;type&quot; templates like M&amp;M did? I.e. Brick, Speedster, etc.<br /> <br /> Those would be super-useful to grok the power rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T05:31:35-07:00","id":1325218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325215#post1325215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get an extra document where the devs stat up various superheroes from fiction? Like Wolverine, Superman, Iron Man, etc.<br /> If not that, can we get some &amp;quot;type&amp;quot; templates like M&amp;M did? I.e. Brick, Speedster, etc.<br /> <br /> Those would be super-useful to grok the power rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>James is working on it. Check last update in KS","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T07:12:12-07:00","id":1325236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325214#post1325214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that Max Mercer is the nova-level equivalent of a Talent, that's pretty easy to guess, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems more probability manipulation is the Talents' (and their next stage) unique thing in the Continuum (notice no Luck power in TC: Aberrant).<br /> <br /> Ian's mentioned the idea of super-science and nova powers that let you hop into alternate worlds in the past, so universe-hopping won't be off-limits to the other Inspired; full time travel we'll have to see..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T07:25:39-07:00","id":1325243,"title":"","content":"Something, that has been annoying me a bit. The more I read the 3rd preview, the more I get feeling, that if you want to have space campaign or space exploration you should go and play psion.<br /> <br /> Firstly there is the issue that is just my crappy read. It reads like with interstellar warp the creator of warp must sit on his ass and maintain the wrap, which would make it purely NPC power, but then it gets weird. If he travels through the warp he just spends the few points for few minutes of travel, but if he sits on his ass he needs to spend quantum for the whole duration of the journey to months and years. How does that interact with Quantum regeneration? Can he regenerate it?<br /> <br /> Interstellar warp has significant time travel time, ranging between weeks and months for any decent distance. It does not add to the story, for the travelers it is instantaneous.<br /> For any decent distance, you will face complications EVERY TIME YOU USE IT.<br /> <br /> It is pricey. You need to buy scale tags equals to your spaceship size and exploration without spaceship just locks the whole team into the specific build to compensate for lack of spaceship. At least tags scale for quantum and not power otherwise it would be hell.<br /> <br /> It is expensive, forces you to keep timetable. It is not a quite good exploration tool as, if you can open warp, you can move an army through and not one smallish group, which the travel power should offer at first and warp do ultimately sidesteps this level, where the exploration kinda sits.<br /> It feels like it fails to deliver the space exploration mode of play and it kneecaps it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T08:37:20-07:00","id":1325259,"title":"","content":"<br /> @TheSarcastic Sage So that is the way its supposed to go. Hmm. Okay, honestly, I am not really a fan of how simple that is. Which is funny, I know, but true nontheless. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> Yeah, that is true. I picked the moon, but your right, Alpha Centuari is visible and so 2 points of Quantum can take me there. Easy peasy. <br /> <br /> Yeah not really feeling that. <br /> <br /> So I think Warp needs to have a die roll. The number of successes necessary is based on the distance chart. The Range power isn't for how close the wormhole is to the caster but how far the exit point can be. <br /> <br /> No time dialation nor will there be complications as traversing the wormhole is nearly instant. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On power themes I thought that was going to be in the book. I was looking forward to seeing that in the book. Its not in the power chapter, which is sad. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> @Zirb42 <br /> <br /> Yeah. I agree. I think the Warp power leaves much to be desired. I think I will be implementing the rules idea that I said above. I think that it adds both an interesting factor and also makes it more believable. <br /> <br /> I will add I am not a fan of the power tag costs and the way everything is 12 XP. It seems a bit overdone, especially when one expects that using power tags is what people will do. <br /> <br /> Maybe a number of power tags can be given free based on Power Dot rating or Quantum rating for each power. With Quantum 6 and higher boosting that up even more. <br /> <br /> I also think the costs should be lower. <br /> <br /> Same with Adaptation, that Mega-Edge needs some of its requirements reduced a bit. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T08:42:33-07:00","id":1325260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325259#post1325259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@TheSarcastic Sage So that is the way its supposed to go. Hmm. Okay, honestly, I am not really a fan of how simple that is. Which is funny, I know, but true nontheless.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> Yeah, that is true. I picked the moon, but your right, Alpha Centuari is visible and so 2 points of Quantum can take me there. Easy peasy.<br /> <br /> Yeah not really feeling that.<br /> <br /> So I think Warp needs to have a die roll. The number of successes necessary is based on the distance chart. The Range power isn't for how close the wormhole is to the caster but how far the exit point can be.<br /> <br /> No time dialation nor will there be complications as traversing the wormhole is nearly instant.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On power themes I thought that was going to be in the book. I was looking forward to seeing that in the book. Its not in the power chapter, which is sad.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> @Zirb42<br /> <br /> Yeah. I agree. I think the Warp power leaves much to be desired. I think I will be implementing the rules idea that I said above. I think that it adds both an interesting factor and also makes it more believable.<br /> <br /> I will add I am not a fan of the power tag costs and the way everything is 12 XP. It seems a bit overdone, especially when one expects that using power tags is what people will do.<br /> <br /> Maybe a number of power tags can be given free based on Power Dot rating or Quantum rating for each power. With Quantum 6 and higher boosting that up even more.<br /> <br /> I also think the costs should be lower.<br /> <br /> Same with Adaptation, that Mega-Edge needs some of its requirements reduced a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehh there are free power tags associated with lot of the powers. Those are generally the tags written udner it with fewexceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T08:50:54-07:00","id":1325263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325260#post1325260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ehh there are free power tags associated with lot of the powers. Those are generally the tags written udner it with fewexceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read them is that you don't automatically get them, you have to buy them, but they are tags that exist only for said power. <br /> <br /> What I meant was like how Quantum Attack gives a point of free tag per dot, I think all powers should do that. You should get free tag slots based on both power dot and Quantum score. Then if that is not enough and you want more you purchase them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:01:31-07:00","id":1325266,"title":"","content":".<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325263#post1325263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I read them is that you don't automatically get them, you have to buy them, but they are tags that exist only for said power.<br /> <br /> What I meant was like how Quantum Attack gives a point of free tag per dot, I think all powers should do that. You should get free tag slots based on both power dot and Quantum score. Then if that is not enough and you want more you purchase them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting conundrum. My read is, that most do. The may apply line, I would read as for free, quantum limitations apply, but must buy them can be correct too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:17:30-07:00","id":1325269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325266#post1325266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> This is interesting conundrum. My read is, that most do. The may apply line, I would read as for free, quantum limitations apply, but must buy them can be correct too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My only thought on that is if all powers automatically give free tags then why would it be called out in particular powers as something special. Like the Quantum Attack power. If it was automatic then it would be assumed. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong I think it should be automatic, a benefit of power rating growth, but I don't think by canon rule it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:29:39-07:00","id":1325274,"title":"","content":"Also, does anyone else think that the XP costs for Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, Quantum Powers, and Power Tags all seem a bit too high in some cases. Especially for some Mega-Edges, like Body Modification, and some Power Tags, who cost as much as a power or a Mega-Attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:33:36-07:00","id":1325276,"title":"","content":"They over-costed everything to entice you to buy things for 1/2 cost using Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Since I'm working on a house rule that gets rid of Flux and Transcendence, I'm trying to figure out an appropriate cost for everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T09:44:40-07:00","id":1325281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325274#post1325274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, does anyone else think that the XP costs for Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, Quantum Powers, and Power Tags all seem a bit too high in some cases. Especially for some Mega-Edges, like Body Modification, and some Power Tags, who cost as much as a power or a Mega-Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>I built 2 character sheets of the same character so I could compare the changes in costs across both systems since that was my initial thought as well. What I find is that while everything seems overly expensive, you actually start in the same range as any other out of the box nova from 1e. Skills got compressed, Mega-stat enhancements got lumped into &quot;edges&quot; but you still end up with the same number more or less if not the same types. <br /> What seemed odd was how certain mega-edges requirements appear to be so high that they are impossible to attain at the start. Adaptation for example, requires M-sta 3 which requires quantum 3, which adds up to like 96 exp by itself. After you do that you have only 44 points left to buy ANY other powers, all of which cost like 16 points per dot. So you could survive in space, maybe move around in space, but you can't do much of anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:07:42-07:00","id":1325286,"title":"","content":"I am not trying to be the devil advocate here, but I can\u2019t see how you are expecting to build an interestelar explorer from day one with no difficulties.<br /> <br /> If the entire campaign runs around space exploration the travel is important, warping to other planet as soon as needed is not very space exploring it\u2019s more about visiting places.<br /> <br /> I have 2 options on the Warping time:<br /> First idea, If the idea is to travel with a space ship, build a Warping ship, not a Warping Nova, it would be a bit more space explorers than a guy that can travel to other planet instantaneously.<br /> Second idea, use a small ship, size 3 is the size of a yatch or a airline plane, enough to have a 5 man crew there for a few years with the proper technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:11:06-07:00","id":1325288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325276#post1325276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They over-costed everything to entice you to buy things for 1/2 cost using Transcendence.<br /> <br /> Since I'm working on a house rule that gets rid of Flux and Transcendence, I'm trying to figure out an appropriate cost for everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with buying with transcendence (dissonance is better name) is that without bleed out it does not work. You want highest quantum nova. this means reserving 6 out of 9 points towards that goal. Two points should be kept in reserve as not to eff up and go over alloted limit, when dice hate you and so on. Which leaves ONE point for transendence buy, two if you are carful. Minmaxing dictates you should not grab transcendence at all. It is simply too expensive in the current set up.<br /> The modular set up of powers also feels more rewarding by buying piecemal, instead of byuing whole power at once (assuming you can use once transecendence to affect one buy and not buy of one thing) ut trasendence forces you to hoard exp and to not advance as to not waste your precious buy option, even if you do not seek hig quantumand true trascendence you do have less than 8th buys with transecendence. Transendecne only works while playing descent into monsterhood and explicitly embracing it. Otherwise it is just annoying stat you mitigate.<br /> It also makes no damn sense storywise without bleedout. Chrysalis does not shed transendence, thus using it is surefire way to block true transcendence. but inventor of it did reach true transendence(unless retconned) Transendece is truly bad term.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325281#post1325281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So you could survive in space, maybe move around in space, but you can't do much of anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said it and wil repaet it space is unsoported part of the setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:13:30-07:00","id":1325290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325215#post1325215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get an extra document where the devs stat up various superheroes from fiction? Like Wolverine, Superman, Iron Man, etc.<br /> If not that, can we get some &amp;quot;type&amp;quot; templates like M&amp;M did? I.e. Brick, Speedster, etc.<br /> <br /> Those would be super-useful to grok the power rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter should be possible, the former definitely isn\u2019t - as Onyx Path doesn\u2019t have a license for DC characters like Green atoning did, or Marvel Characters like MWP did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:19:57-07:00","id":1325293,"title":"","content":"\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar258_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"258\" data-vbnamecard=\"258\">TheSarcasticSage</a> Well they also say that you can remove Transcendence and not cause any mechanical issues. Which means you could half cost everything and poof the issue is fixed.<br /> <br /> Okay, joking aside, I doubt that really is the answer. But it does amuse me.<br /> <br /> See, I don't mind Flux, I think it fits. Flux is over or improper use of quantum energies. Some penalty should exist for that. I just don't think that it should lead to the nova becoming an inhuman, non-empathy feeling monster.<br /> <br /> So my idea would be to call Transcendence by a new name - Dissonance - and have there be more active bleed off effects. Maybe Flux itself bleeds off naturally at a rate of some points per some short cycle - day maybe. While Dissonance bleeds off when you are using powers at half ratings and require week long periods. Hmm<br /> <br /> All all that said I would be very interested in hearing your ideas and house rules for such matters when you develop them.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar765_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"765\" data-vbnamecard=\"765\">Darksol-aeternium</a> That's interesting, very interesting. I like the fact that it seems things are balanced in the sense that novas from 1e and 2e can roughly do similar things at game start.<br /> <br /> Question though, did you make use of tags? Did you use them to modify your powers or at the base you kept the powers strictly standard.<br /> <br /> I agree with you on the over-cost nature of some Mega-Edges, like Adapatation as a perfect example. I wonder if someone forgot that to get Mega-Stamina 3 you also had to have Quantum 3 as a prerequsiite, besides the whole Stamina 3 (which is easy).<br /> <br /> I think reducing the requisite for Adaptation down to Mega-Stamina 2 makes a bit more sense to me. Mostly as I figure most characters would buy at least one dot of additional Quantum.<br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> But that is honestly the thing, using Warp as is is as simple as looking at the target and spending quantum. Then you get a wormhole that links between the two points that you can traverse through.<br /> <br /> Funny enough for all my talk about making things easier I think that this is too easy, and would want to add some things to it.<br /> <br /> As a note you can also increase the scale of the Warp portal by using Tags. In time you could, if you wanted to be a warping machine of a nova, make it so your normal Scale 1 sized Warp is actually say Scale 3 or so as that is 'only' two tags.<br /> <br /> Which could be fun. Characters board a nova-built plane, another character opens a warp to a distant star, and then they travel through it, exploring the far distant site.<br /> <br /> Hmm. I like the potential for an exploration campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-17-2019, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:20:48-07:00","id":1325295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325243#post1325243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something, that has been annoying me a bit. The more I read the 3rd preview, the more I get feeling, that if you want to have space campaign or space exploration you should go and play psion.<br /> <br /> Firstly there is the issue that is just my crappy read. It reads like with interstellar warp the creator of warp must sit on his ass and maintain the wrap, which would make it purely NPC power, but then it gets weird. If he travels through the warp he just spends the few points for few minutes of travel, but if he sits on his ass he needs to spend quantum for the whole duration of the journey to months and years. How does that interact with Quantum regeneration? Can he regenerate it?<br /> <br /> Interstellar warp has significant time travel time, ranging between weeks and months for any decent distance. It does not add to the story, for the travelers it is instantaneous.<br /> For any decent distance, you will face complications EVERY TIME YOU USE IT.<br /> <br /> It is pricey. You need to buy scale tags equals to your spaceship size and exploration without spaceship just locks the whole team into the specific build to compensate for lack of spaceship. At least tags scale for quantum and not power otherwise it would be hell.<br /> <br /> It is expensive, forces you to keep timetable. It is not a quite good exploration tool as, if you can open warp, you can move an army through and not one smallish group, which the travel power should offer at first and warp do ultimately sidesteps this level, where the exploration kinda sits.<br /> It feels like it fails to deliver the space exploration mode of play and it kneecaps it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m missing what the problem is. If you\u2019re playing a 21st Century Daedalus League game you\u2019re going for a settting where space travel is much harder and slower than in a 22nd Century Aeon game. That seems to fit both settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:24:08-07:00","id":1325296,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Remember when I said to dial discussion back a few notches because people were arguing in circles rather than discussing? Conversation's starting to go in that direction again.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:25:16-07:00","id":1325297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325286#post1325286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not trying to be the devil advocate here, but I can\u2019t see how you are expecting to build an interestelar explorer from day one with no difficulties.<br /> <br /> If the entire campaign runs around space exploration the travel is important, warping to other planet as soon as needed is not very space exploring it\u2019s more about visiting places.<br /> <br /> I have 2 options on the Warping time:<br /> First idea, If the idea is to travel by a space ship, build a Warping ship, not a Warping Nova, it would be a bit more space explorers than a guy that can travel to other planet instantaneously.<br /> Second idea, use a small ship, size 3 is the size of a yatch or a airline plane, enough to have a 5 man crew there for a few years with the proper technology.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, Space exploration is visiting new places and truth to be told there is no visible point to the travel time table, outside of making nova travel inferior to the psion way. We do compare to the existing template here and to say not to misses the point. There is already an inherent disadvantage in the complications adding another disadvantage is just annoying. one feels like<br /> <br /> Okay, unless there is a significant shift in the next chapter both teleport and Warp use the same speed table and same travel principle. Unless there is explicit mention of it in the technology chapter, that is the default speed and method of travel of the Nova powers and their derivates and it is piddly in comparison to psions(and truth to be told by nearly any high-speed travel device in fiction, which this is supposed to represent), without any other benefit-with possible exception of free form. But it does not feel freeform enough in this regard. it really would need to be, where you want to, if you can guess its existence, instead of what you can see.<br /> <br /> Problem with small scale ship is, it is still expensive. It just makes one character the bus of the group, instead of forcing everyone to grab the same cashback. It is a better solution. It is just also a crummy one. We need tech option, but there do not seem to be actual cheapness we can get from the tech, It seems to cost the same from what we got in power tags. Maybe you can pool tech, unlike powers, but it seems dubious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:36:06-07:00","id":1325303,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s all ideas to work with, I suggest you look for Star Frontier and StarDrive settings, great ideas for space exploring.<br /> <br /> The Warp thing is basically an hyperspace, you open it, while you are inside others can trace you and detect the exit building a proper defence around it for your arrival (or trace you by the exit and trace a rout to attack your base).<br /> <br /> Maybe they can force close it (from the exit), or as your Warp core is operating you notice you are not producing quantum enough to keep it working until the end of the Warp. Those ideas would make you stop somewhere or lost in space.<br /> <br /> Maybe they have a technology to go faster thru your own wormhole than you, so once you scape they enter it and reach you before you arrive your destine.<br /> <br /> Another idea is create a tag that allow you to fly at warp speed while in space, needing to trace a way as it\u2019s almost impossible to manoeuvre at this speed. Than you can build a spaceship that fly to alpha centaur in 4 minutes (1 minute less than Warp), but you need to trace the way to the place, not being able to use only memory to jump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-17-2019, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:47:58-07:00","id":1325306,"title":"","content":"Just to point that psions are not better at travelling:<br /> A psion takes 8-psi hours to do an interstellar travel (in the same galaxy). The maximum range of a jump for a psion is the range they can create a connection, 10 ly x psi, for a proxy it\u2019s 70 ly.<br /> <br /> So to go 25ly the Nova takes 5 minutes and the psion takes 2 hours (a pretty strong psion).<br /> To go 125ly the Nova takes 1 hour and the psion takes 2 jumps each taking 2 hours.<br /> The table go up and down, but the psion never get the Nova.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T10:54:50-07:00","id":1325308,"title":"","content":"Let's talk about some other problems with Warp and Teleport.<br /> <br /> Isn't it strange that Warp gives you an unlimited range from the start, but you have to extend your range with Tags for Teleport? Shouldn't they work the same way?<br /> <br /> Also using Warp/Teleport to an interplanetary Location you can see in our sky is really WEIRD. Remember how long it takes for the light from those stars to reach us. We don't see the stars as they are now, but as they were long ago. And you don't want to travel where they were long ago, but to the place they are now (if they even still exist - they might have turned supernova and we don't know because the light of the supernova is still on its way to earth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4081-thomas-weinbrenner","name":"Thomas Weinbrenner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:00:27-07:00","id":1325310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325293#post1325293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar765_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"765\" data-vbnamecard=\"765\">Darksol-aeternium</a> That's interesting, very interesting. I like the fact that it seems things are balanced in the sense that novas from 1e and 2e can roughly do similar things at game start.<br /> <br /> Question though, did you make use of tags? Did you use them to modify your powers or at the base you kept the powers strictly standard.<br /> <br /> I agree with you on the over-cost nature of some Mega-Edges, like Adapatation as a perfect example. I wonder if someone forgot that to get Mega-Stamina 3 you also had to have Quantum 3 as a prerequsiite, besides the whole Stamina 3 (which is easy).<br /> <br /> I think reducing the requisite for Adaptation down to Mega-Stamina 2 makes a bit more sense to me. Mostly as I figure most characters would buy at least one dot of additional Quantum.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>In order to make the comparison easy I deliberately didn't modify the 1e version's power and didn't add any tags to the 2e version. Which is just as well, there would not have been any points left to add frills to either one using standard chargen. End result had the same amount of Taint/Transcendance in both cases (4 btw), and both built up to the same quantum level in anticipation of future expenditures (Q5). Idea was a guy who goes out into space to help with the Deadalus League's orbital space stations, 1e was capable of having Adaptation immediately whereas 2e will need to wait a long while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:32:47-07:00","id":1325322,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325310#post1325310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In order to make the comparison easy I deliberately didn't modify the 1e version's power and didn't add any tags to the 2e version. Which is just as well, there would not have been any points left to add frills to either one using standard chargen. End result had the same amount of Taint/Transcendance in both cases (4 btw), and both built up to the same quantum level in anticipation of future expenditures (Q5). Idea was a guy who goes out into space to help with the Deadalus League's orbital space stations, 1e was capable of having Adaptation immediately whereas 2e will need to wait a long while.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel the need to point out, that is a rather significant difference for the proposed scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:38:36-07:00","id":1325323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325308#post1325308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's talk about some other problems with Warp and Teleport.<br /> <br /> Isn't it strange that Warp gives you an unlimited range from the start, but you have to extend your range with Tags for Teleport? Shouldn't they work the same way?<br /> <br /> Also using Warp/Teleport to an interplanetary Location you can see in our sky is really WEIRD. Remember how long it takes for the light from those stars to reach us. We don't see the stars as they are now, but as they were long ago. And you don't want to travel where they were long ago, but to the place they are now (if they even still exist - they might have turned supernova and we don't know because the light of the supernova is still on its way to earth).</div> </div> </div> </div>Warp is for travel by default. Teleport is tactical by default. You can upgrade teleport to be a travel power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:46:35-07:00","id":1325327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325310#post1325310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In order to make the comparison easy I deliberately didn't modify the 1e version's power and didn't add any tags to the 2e version. Which is just as well, there would not have been any points left to add frills to either one using standard chargen. End result had the same amount of Taint/Transcendance in both cases (4 btw), and both built up to the same quantum level in anticipation of future expenditures (Q5). Idea was a guy who goes out into space to help with the Deadalus League's orbital space stations, 1e was capable of having Adaptation immediately whereas 2e will need to wait a long while.</div> </div> </div> </div>That Adaptation issue is a sad part, but somehow makes sense.<br /> To just being able to stay in space with no harm, the character need just Immunity and Mega-Stamina 1. But he would not be able to survive after he lose his breath. If he have Breath Control edge (not mega edge) he can hold breath for a quite long time as he can use the Mega Stamina bonus. Not the same thing, but enough to fix a small hole in the shiphull or help an astronaut enter the ship.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:48:33-07:00","id":1325330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thomas Weinbrenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325308#post1325308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's talk about some other problems with Warp and Teleport.<br /> <br /> Isn't it strange that Warp gives you an unlimited range from the start, but you have to extend your range with Tags for Teleport? Shouldn't they work the same way?<br /> <br /> Also using Warp/Teleport to an interplanetary Location you can see in our sky is really WEIRD. Remember how long it takes for the light from those stars to reach us. We don't see the stars as they are now, but as they were long ago. And you don't want to travel where they were long ago, but to the place they are now (if they even still exist - they might have turned supernova and we don't know because the light of the supernova is still on its way to earth).</div> </div> </div> </div> Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3487_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3487\" data-vbnamecard=\"3487\">Jetstream</a> said, if I get it. Teleport is for nightcrawling around, but it can be boosted to being travel power. Warp is the default travel power.<br /> <br /> It also seems to work more on principle I want to go there, the exact location is ultimately unimportant, but wording it like that is rather problematic, so you have rather poetic, where you can see. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T11:53:59-07:00","id":1325334,"title":"","content":"From playing Aberrant for a long time in 1e and looking at 2e\u2019s character creation I would say 150 xp is pretty on par with 30 nova points. But where on the short end for me when I was thinking of making a comic book hero more powerful then street level. The thing is however Aberrant is not comic book heros. Yes they can approach that and in some ways surpass them in the new scale system. However making a starting hero you think is perfect is not possible u less you are thinking street level. <br /> So no starting superman but a Luke Cage is possible and he can grow into Superman if that is what you want. <br /> <br /> Now I would say in the older system 30 nova points are more flexible as far as background, skills and attributes go. 1 nova point was worth 3 attribute dots, 6 skill points or 5 background points. Where at 150 xp is 5xp = 1np and attributes cost 10xp in A2e so in old A1e that would be the equivalent of 2np vs 1np for 3 attributes. There is also no freebies in this system. I don\u2019t know about other people but for me freebies always went into young quantum by 2 with 1 point left over. <br /> <br /> So sure in a lot of ways you could make a more rounded staring character in 1e however also in 1e extras always upped the powers cost a level. Having all powers cost same as mega edges and stats does raise the cost of 1st level powers and body mods however at the same time it lowers level 3 powers as well. <br /> <br /> Optional rule: you could always have body mods cost 5xp to represent that most only cost 1np in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:04:16-07:00","id":1325339,"title":"","content":"Nova Points were also extremely easy to manage and calculate, in my personal opinion. Besides it just is easier and faster to manage smaller numbers than large ones for majority of players as well. So some players are immediately intomitated by having 150xp to spend while spending 30 NP\u2019s sounds a lot more managable.<br /> <br /> In general I have found that, my players at least, seem to find it easier to create characters on simplified points Vs creating characters using free exp. But that is just my experience on the matter others may differ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:23:53-07:00","id":1325350,"title":"","content":"Next sample character I made playing with the new rules; a newbie DeVries elite calling himself (for the sake of example) \u201cDestructicator\u201d<br /> <br /> All base attributes are the same for both versions.<br /> 1e version has M-Str, M-Sta, and M-wits 1; Enhancements are Crush, Regen, and Quickness.<br /> 2e version substitutes M-wits for M-Resolve and Quickness for Multitasking (as there is no direct \u201cadd actions\u201d enhancement).<br /> <br /> <br /> Skills compressed of course, but the resulting overlap caused the 2e version to have 3 specialties in Aim, Athletics, and Close Combat. 1E version has various skills but no specialties at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Both are Quantum 3, however the 1e version has zero taint and the 2e version could not exist without 2 points of it. This is because while 3 flavors of Q bolt cost 15 NP and is fairly negligible in cost, a single Q-bolt with Area, Beam, and Variable tags cost 72 exp by itself.<br /> <br /> Attunement 2 was a matter of 2 background points for the 1e version, 2e version could not afford to take it.<br /> <br /> Finally, 1e version has 1 dot of the power Invincibility: Physical, which doesn\u2019t exist in 2e at all. To try and make up the difference I used Quantum Field which looks mechanically like an expy of Armor. The edge Hardy tries to make up more of the difference. Based on some games I\u2019ve watched of Scion: Origins I suspect actual damage calculations aren\u2019t quite as deadly as before so this might not be too much of a change.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T12:38:43-07:00","id":1325361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325339#post1325339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nova Points were also extremely easy to manage and calculate, in my personal opinion. Besides it just is easier and faster to manage smaller numbers than large ones for majority of players as well. So some players are immediately intomitated by having 150xp to spend while spending 30 NP\u2019s sounds a lot more managable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggest we name a \u201cNova dot\u201d as one dot in a Nova trait (12xp, 6 if transcended). Once you transform XP in Nova dots it\u2019s easier to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T15:09:15-07:00","id":1325403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325350#post1325350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both are Quantum 3, however the 1e version has zero taint and the 2e version could not exist without 2 points of it. This is because while 3 flavors of Q bolt cost 15 NP and is fairly negligible in cost, a single Q-bolt with Area, Beam, and Variable tags cost 72 exp by itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Use Techniques, and Quantum attack gives you free tags. You might have added something incorrectly.<br /> <br /> Techniques are basically the trick from Mutants and Masterminds where you buy a power once and then use it to justify five other powers, at the cost of only being able to use one of them at a time. They are great for 'multimode' things like varied Quantum Attacks, and buying 3 dots of Q-Attack and two power tags to make new techniques with your three <i>free</i> power tags is Some Good.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T15:23:00-07:00","id":1325407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325403#post1325403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use Techniques, and Quantum attack gives you free tags. You might have added something incorrectly.<br /> <br /> Techniques are basically the trick from Mutants and Masterminds where you buy a power once and then use it to justify five other powers, at the cost of only being able to use one of them at a time. They are great for 'multimode' things like varied Quantum Attacks, and buying 3 dots of Q-Attack and two power tags to make new techniques with your three <i>free</i> power tags is Some Good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This system brings a few extra tricks to the character creation. Things we see in M&amp;M.<br /> <br /> But here you can actually use all the powers at same time (with the proper limitations), having a side effect only on the fact as it is a single power and can be copied and dissipated as one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T15:26:42-07:00","id":1325409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325403#post1325403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Use Techniques, and Quantum attack gives you free tags. You might have added something incorrectly.<br /> <br /> Techniques are basically the trick from Mutants and Masterminds where you buy a power once and then use it to justify five other powers, at the cost of only being able to use one of them at a time. They are great for 'multimode' things like varied Quantum Attacks, and buying 3 dots of Q-Attack and two power tags to make new techniques with your three <i>free</i> power tags is Some Good.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get a rather similar number.<br /> 12 for the power+ beam free from dot<br /> 24 for area-cannot take for free<br /> snother12 for a variable in the form of another dot, but you need another dot for a double variable, which would allow a switch from area to beam so another 12 for 24<br /> This is 60.<br /> Assuming you need to buy variable for every dot and not tag gets me 72 points/ or want to add range.<br /> End result<br /> Q attack 3 dots<br /> Beam 1<br /> Area 2<br /> Variable 1+1= 2 switch between area and beam version.<br /> <br /> Note i would allow another variant of q attack for 12 as a technique originating from this , but it is significant investment and iI do not feel that chargen actually supports this. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T16:12:40-07:00","id":1325419,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6491\" data-vbnamecard=\"6491\">zorb42</a>; <br /> Interesting... I think I added it up differently than you did. I assumed that nothing was free (I must have missed that reference) and payed only for the 1 dot version of area, but it yielded the same number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T16:24:18-07:00","id":1325420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325419#post1325419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6491\" data-vbnamecard=\"6491\">zorb42</a>;<br /> Interesting... I think I added it up differently than you did. I assumed that nothing was free (I must have missed that reference) and payed only for the 1 dot version of area, but it yielded the same number.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume, that the number behind the tag is a number of points/dots(standard price for point) it cost in this case area costs 24 points on the base level, as it has 2 behind it. I assume that the various can/may spend points per dots in power mean free points in power tags. For example, Q attack gives tag point per dot, which you can invest only in the tags written in the power, but can use the experience to buy any of the extra or other tags not written in the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6491,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","user":"zorb42","date":". 07-17-2019, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T17:12:54-07:00","id":1325432,"title":"","content":"I have a quite possibly dumb question. When increasing scale, how do you know when to use Narrative (Multiplier) vs Dramatic (Enhancements). I am specifically right now looking at Mega-Cunning and how it interacts with Initiative. If you have characters with M-C 0, 1, and 4 in a scene, what are they all adding to Initiative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T17:25:16-07:00","id":1325437,"title":"","content":"I am very confused about the seven categories of Scale and when they apply. I get the idea that Might Scale helps when you hit a person or Speed is when you compare how fast you are going. What about Durability? Especially when it comes to the Mega-Edge with the same name (That should be changed). Mega-Stamina adds to Durability Scale, but does that apply to your Defense or your Soft Armor? <br /> <br /> Also, with the Durability Mega-Edge. Does it add your Q/2 in Soft Armor, even though the Soft Armor tag states that it adds just one to your Soft Armor? <br /> <br /> Please help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T17:36:15-07:00","id":1325438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325437#post1325437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very confused about the seven categories of Scale and when they apply. I get the idea that Might Scale helps when you hit a person or Speed is when you compare how fast you are going. What about Durability? Especially when it comes to the Mega-Edge with the same name (That should be changed). Mega-Stamina adds to Durability Scale, but does that apply to your Defense or your Soft Armor? <br /> <br /> Also, with the Durability Mega-Edge. Does it add your Q/2 in Soft Armor, even though the Soft Armor tag states that it adds just one to your Soft Armor? <br /> <br /> Please help!</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the scale aspect. From my understand it seems that if your durability scale is 5 durability a rocket launcher would just get to roll damage with zero enhancement. At durability 6 you can take a warhead like others would take a punch from a normal person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T17:42:39-07:00","id":1325439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325432#post1325432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a quite possibly dumb question. When increasing scale, how do you know when to use Narrative (Multiplier) vs Dramatic (Enhancements). I am specifically right now looking at Mega-Cunning and how it interacts with Initiative. If you have characters with M-C 0, 1, and 4 in a scene, what are they all adding to Initiative?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is basically, when the effect is trivial or there is no chance to fail, use narrative, if you need to roll dices to define, use dramatic.<br /> <br /> For example. How much can you lift? Mega Might 1 can lift about 5 times more than usual. Need to punch someone relevant? Add +2 enhancements to the roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T17:47:55-07:00","id":1325441,"title":"","content":"The scales are:<br /> Durability: The capacity of resist damage.<br /> Leadership: Amount of people affected by your social capacity/influence<br /> Might: The amount of weight you can lift <br /> Mental: The capacity of deal with information<br /> Power: The capacity of causing damage<br /> Size: The size (volume in general, but possibly length or area)<br /> Speed: Distance over time","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T17:54:46-07:00","id":1325444,"title":"","content":"I guess for Initiative I'd likely treat everyone above the baseline (ha) if the scene as getting their Dramatic Bonus. So if people had Regular Cunning, and one had Mega 1, and one Mega 2, I'd give the Mega-Cunning characters 2 and 4 enhancements, respectively. The other read would be the Mega-2 character gets 2 Enhancements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T18:03:29-07:00","id":1325447,"title":"","content":"About Durability Scale:<br /> It should add the scale difference to the Soft Armor against attackers of lower scale, but it is not said anywhere (only in Scion, somewhere).<br /> Also, if someone attack you with a power more than 3 scales bellow, it don\u2019t harm you at all.<br /> <br /> About The Durability Mega-Edge and the Quantum Field:<br /> I have no idea what they mean by armor rating. Two options to test:<br /> - As there is no soft armor tag on the list, I assume quantum/2 should be the soft armor value.<br /> - Ignire the armor rating and use 2 as soft armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T18:06:42-07:00","id":1325448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tragedyjones</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325444#post1325444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess for Initiative I'd likely treat everyone above the baseline (ha) if the scene as getting their Dramatic Bonus. So if people had Regular Cunning, and one had Mega 1, and one Mega 2, I'd give the Mega-Cunning characters 2 and 4 enhancements, respectively. The other read would be the Mega-2 character gets 2 Enhancements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mega Cunning grants 2 enhancements per scale on the initiative test. That\u2019s what I understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T18:06:54-07:00","id":1325449,"title":"","content":"The other thing to remember, that I forgot for the longest time, is the difference between scale and range bands. I only throw that in there because I believe some powers have an area set in range bands. Like explosive quantum attack or of you add area to quantum field, SG permitting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T18:17:21-07:00","id":1325450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fuzzykuma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325449#post1325449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing to remember, that I forgot for the longest time, is the difference between scale and range bands. I only throw that in there because I believe some powers have an area set in range bands. Like explosive quantum attack or of you add area to quantum field, SG permitting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Range and Areas are usually measured by the range band they occupy. It\u2019s a really important thing to remember, as you avoid trying to scale up by multiplying when you should just ad one range band.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T20:37:50-07:00","id":1325476,"title":"","content":"In the Mega-Edge Revealing Read this is stated &quot;The nova observes the target and makes an Empathy + Cunning roll with a difficulty equal to the target\u2019s Composure and a maximum number of successes equal to the nova\u2019s Mega-Cunning.&quot; Does the last part mean that even if you get 4 successes if you only have Mega-Cunning 1 you can only count it as if you had one success? <br /> <br /> Why the limitation? <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Another question. If I was to have a Elemental Mastery power and have it be Information Mastery as a theme what do you think would be the core power I choose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:07:36-07:00","id":1325480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325476#post1325476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Another question. If I was to have a Elemental Mastery power and have it be Information Mastery as a theme what do you think would be the core power I choose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the list of what we have to work with in Manuscript 3, you have a choice of either Digital Scan or Universal Translator. This I base off of the original write-up for Scripture's weird Information Manipulation power from the APG. All the rest of the techniques for that power boil down to a limited scope Transmutation effect that only affects stored information whether in written or digital form. The really bizzarre ones that mess with the memories stored in minds probably wouldn't even be available to novas, but amount to a kind of specialized hypnotic effect that deletes, distorts, or otherwise changes memories/intended communications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:07:51-07:00","id":1325481,"title":"","content":"So you don\u2019t read beyond your mental capacities. The successes that are counting are the ones beyond the difficulty, as far as I understand.<br /> <br /> Information Mastery is very complex, I not completely aware of what it can do. I think you should start with Shroud, as you are forbiding the information to leave. But... tell more about this idea of information Mastery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:30:25-07:00","id":1325485,"title":"","content":"I don't understand why I can't include all my successes. If I have Mega-Cunning 1, Empathy 3 and Cunning 4 and roll 4 successes against a baseline with Composure 2 I should be able to use more than 1 of my successes. I should learn more. No other power basically wastes successes like that. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On the Elemental Mastery doesn't the core ability have to be Elemental Anima, Quantum Anima, or Quantum Attack? Which is where my question lies, which of the ones they descibe should I use. <br /> <br /> Honestly, with this being as difficult trying to figure out I'm probably going to just say he purchases Digital Scan and Digital Manipulation (he has the slot) and keep my Elemental Mastery power to Space Mastery. <br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> As for what Information Mastery is, well its the ability to sense, manipulate, and control information - in machines, people, and the world around. (I say people too as I am ignoring the whole theme of novas don't have mentalist abilities - I am not making new powers at this time, I am just ignoring that theme). <br /> <br /> But I really wanted to figure out the best way to do the things I want as written. And Revealing Read seemed like it was a perfect reading information power, except for that odd limitation of no more succeses then Mega-Cunning. (Which at this time is 1, since the nova is only Quantum 1).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:39:24-07:00","id":1325488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Choose one of the following base effects for the nova\u2019s Elemental Mastery: Environmental Anima, Quantum Anima, Quantum Attack, or Shroud, all using the chosen element as the medium. </div> </div> </div>Should is there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:41:43-07:00","id":1325489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325488#post1325488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Should is there...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Opps. My bad. hehe<br /> <br /> I hadn't thought of the idea of basing it on Shroud. The concept of blanking an area so that one can't know what is inside. Hmm. It could work. <br /> <br /> Though I think I am going to go with Revealing Read even if I am not entirely satisfied with how the successes are applied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T21:47:45-07:00","id":1325492,"title":"","content":"You probably should work on the Mentalist kit, with the Revealing read, Hypnotic Presence (for memory manipulation), Telecommunication, Digital Scan, maybe digital manipulation. Start with manipulating and accessing the information in the source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-17T22:00:23-07:00","id":1325494,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well I came up with this 150 XP spread in terms of Nova Experience. Obviously its mostly a creative endeavor rather than an actual being played character. That said I wonder if it would be a fun and viable character. Hmm<br /> <br /> o Quantum 1<br /> <br /> o Edges: Attunement 1, Photographic Memory 1, Keen Sense (all), Fame 1, Wealth 1, Always Prepared 1<br /> <br /> o Mega-Attributes: Mega-Intellect 1, Mega-Cunning 1, Mega-Stamina 1, Mega-Presence 1, Mega-Manipulation 1, Mega-Composure 1<br /> <br /> o Mega Edges: Digital Manipulation 1, Digital Scan 1, Hypnotic Presence, Inventor 1, Revealing Read 1,<br /> <br /> o Quantum Power<br /> Spatial Mastery - Quantum Anima 1<br /> <br /> Origin is Suburbia and Role is Corporate, and I have not thought of Society yet.<br /> <br /> I could see one of his future purchases being Mega-Resolve. At some point he will probably also get Mega-Dexterity, mostly so he can move fast when crafting and such.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> By the way if someone said to me &quot;I want to use the Mega-Edge Detection to detect thoughts!&quot; I would totally allow it. Which means the mind sensing part of telepathy is solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-18-2019, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T02:47:04-07:00","id":1325525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325306#post1325306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to point that psions are not better at travelling:<br /> A psion takes 8-psi hours to do an interstellar travel (in the same galaxy). The maximum range of a jump for a psion is the range they can create a connection, 10 ly x psi, for a proxy it\u2019s 70 ly.<br /> <br /> So to go 25ly the Nova takes 5 minutes and the psion takes 2 hours (a pretty strong psion).<br /> To go 125ly the Nova takes 1 hour and the psion takes 2 jumps each taking 2 hours.<br /> The table go up and down, but the psion never get the Nova.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, from whence does the max range of connection come? I cannot find it at all in the text and it seems to be nonexistent, could you at least give me the name of the passage here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:16:28-07:00","id":1325560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325525#post1325525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, from whence does the max range of connection come? I cannot find it at all in the text and it seems to be nonexistent, could you at least give me the name of the passage here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 221, Interestellar Psi Powers. Also must note that the range I described requires a Clair to extend the connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:26:39-07:00","id":1325562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325560#post1325560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Page 221, Interestellar Psi Powers. Also must note that the range I described requires a Clair to extend the connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explicitly doesn\u2019t apply to teleportation. It\u2019s in the first sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:35:41-07:00","id":1325566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325562#post1325562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That explicitly doesn\u2019t apply to teleportation. It\u2019s in the first sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need the connection to jump. \u201cThe universe is open for the psion to explore. He can teleport to any location where he has a noetic connection, including near a distant star he sees in the sky.\u201c<br /> All the stars we see in the sky are pretty close, for astronomical definitions, that\u2019s something less than 50 ly for sure. Further stars just using potent telescopes, otherwise you can\u2019t define what is a star and what is the other as they are visually too close<br /> <br /> Unless you say that a Upeo can jump to Olympus just because he can see the moon, than ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-18-2019, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:47:00-07:00","id":1325568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325566#post1325566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need the connection to jump. \u201cThe universe is open for the psion to explore. He can teleport to any location where he has a noetic connection, including near a distant star he sees in the sky.\u201c<br /> All the stars we see in the sky are pretty close, for astronomical definitions, that\u2019s something less than 50 ly for sure. Further stars just using potent telescopes, otherwise you can\u2019t define what is a star and what is the other as they are visually too close<br /> <br /> Unless you say that a Upeo can jump to Olympus just because he can see the moon, than ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>The furthest star we can see is 16 thousand light years away. The vast bulk of stars we see in the sky are up to 1000 light years away, not 50, and a teleporter can jump to any one of them from visual connection alone. If he\u2019s never been there before, his jump will just take him \u2018somewhere\u2019 near the star and he\u2019ll have to begin surveying from there. If he\u2019s visited a place further out than that he can use that connection to teleport even further.<br /> <br /> This is specifically what the rules intend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:53:01-07:00","id":1325571,"title":"","content":"Ok. Upeo is better than Novas at space exploration, they take 1 to 5 hours to travel to other galaxies (as they are visible)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:02:14-07:00","id":1325579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325571#post1325571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok. Upeo is better than Novas at space exploration, they take 1 to 5 hours to travel to other galaxies (as they are visible)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, part of the reason why the Aberrant era doesn\u2019t have all the extrasolar space colonization that AEon has - psi teleportation is better for long range, as long as you can form a noetic connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:10:02-07:00","id":1325583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325579#post1325579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, part of the reason why the Aberrant era doesn\u2019t have all the extrasolar space colonization that AEon has - psi teleportation is better for long range, as long as you can form a noetic connection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that is was related to the fact that Earth was a pretty good place to live, and there was no big reason to move away from it.<br /> <br /> But your point make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:11:11-07:00","id":1325584,"title":"","content":"Whole Nova population of Earth leaves the Planet eventually, after the Ultimatum, so I would still say Novas should outshine Psionics in this. Then again according to 1st ed they did and they also were powerful, canonically more so than Psionics, Telepaths. But it seems the 1st edition doesn\u2019t matter much when designin the 2nd....<br /> <br /> I thought after the core and Aeon that powerful Psychics were cool and I was enthusiastic that if they are so powerful in 2nd ed how cool will Novas be then... Sadly the answer was that Novas get hit by series of Nerfs to boost he Psionics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:29:48-07:00","id":1325590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325584#post1325584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whole Nova population of Earth leaves the Planet eventually, after the Ultimatum, so I would still say Novas should outshine Psionics in this. Then again according to 1st ed they did and they also were powerful, canonically more so than Psionics, Telepaths. But it seems the 1st edition doesn\u2019t matter much when designin the 2nd....<br /> <br /> I thought after the core and Aeon that powerful Psychics were cool and I was enthusiastic that if they are so powerful in 2nd ed how cool will Novas be then... Sadly the answer was that Novas get hit by series of Nerfs to boost he Psionics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it taking longer to appear at the other side of their warps be a narrative problem for Novas leaving after the Ultimatum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T06:56:08-07:00","id":1325597,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s about the statement that psi is better for space exploration than quantum.<br /> <br /> 1st edition was pretty frank about quantum being stronger and messier than Psionics, which was a scalpel to quantum chainsaw. That is to say both could do similar things and where Psionics were more precise they were in general weaker in effect than quantum powers now Novas are sad to be worse at space exploration, a thing that a starter character Nova could do in 1st ed, all you needed was mega-sta 1 + adaptation as the free enhancement and teleport or warp and the rest of your Nova points were gravy. <br /> <br /> Aberrant Players Guide even went into details about Nova psychics Vs Aeon Psionics but now 2nd ed just denies Nova psychics alltogether.<br /> <br /> Just venting my frustration as what was to be my years highlight, the game I expected the most, has just crashed down with allsorts of weird design decisions. I might still get the 2nd ed but dont know will I move onto it, continue with 1st edition or take 2nd edition and House rule it like hell untill it resembles 1st edition in style and theme but with 2nd ed mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T07:11:17-07:00","id":1325601,"title":"","content":"The thing is, for all the people declaring the nerfing of the novas and whatever when it comes to teleportation/warp, in 1e the novas were never in the psion\u2019s league anyway. Those declaring how good novas were at teleporting/warping distances aren\u2019t paying attention to the actual 1e rules.<br /> <br /> In 1e, psionic teleporters could teleport *anywhere* regardless of distance, as long as they had some familiarity with it. And that familiarity could be as vague as someone else describing it. Sure it would be more difficult, but *anywhere*, absolutely no limit on distance.<br /> <br /> Novas, on the other hand, were limited by their dice pools and successes. Yes, they could get big pools with sufficient Mega and Quantum, but they needed 14 successes just to get 1 light year. It went up from there, but looking at all those visible stars from Earth being under 1000 light years, that\u2019s 17 successes. The maths on 1e nova dice pools were pretty weird with normal dice and mega dice and each dot of Quantum giving an automatic success, but to reasonably expect 17 successes for a Q5 nova you\u2019re looking at, what, 20ish dice? (Eyeballing it here.)<br /> <br /> That\u2019s 1e. Novas were never the undisputed champions of long distance teleporting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T07:34:04-07:00","id":1325607,"title":"","content":"While true I would add that one should remember that said Nova got their Quantum in autosuccess to those distances. So said Quantum 5 Nova would need 12 success and Mega-Dice counted as double success, triple if 10. But the fact is that Psionics who ports to space dies, without appropriate space suit, where as Adaptation would suffice to let Nova survive and port again if he needs more distance. The point being that space exploration should be much more of a Nova thing due to space, and foreign planets, not being a hostile environment for many of them.<br /> <br /> Also the Psionics took, in 1st ed, +5 difficulty for his Psi Roll to Long Jump into unfamiliar place, +4 if he had already spend a day there Etc. So actual exploration was hard but once you become familiar with the place it become easier. You had to live months in a location to eliminate the penalty alltogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T09:46:33-07:00","id":1325628,"title":"","content":"Okay so there seems to be some confusion on how Techniques go. I thought I got it but maybe I was wrong.<br /> <br /> Here is how I think it goes.<br /> <br /> The nova has Space Mastery. He choose Quantum Anima as his base effect. He bought 3 dots and 2 tags in it. He has spent 60 XP for the power. (not consideration spending 32 XP to raise Quantum to 3.)<br /> <br /> He then spends 12 XP for a Technique, lets call it Teleport. He automatically gets Teleport 3 and 2 tag slots.<br /> <br /> Right.<br /> <br /> Now technically speaking both the Quantum Anima and Teleport effects have 3 Tags, but one of them is the technique tag and thus basically auto-locked.<br /> <br /> Okay, lets say he then buys for 12 XP another Technique, Quantum Attack this time, for Space Mastery. Again, he gets it at 3 dots and has 2 tags from Space Mastery and another 3 tags from the writeup of Quantum Attack. He could use any of those five tag slots to gain a sub-technique for the Quantum Weapon technique. Right?<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On Warp, well since stuff like wormholes and quantum tunneling are by definition quantum forces then it stands to reason Novas would be really good at it. <br /> <br /> While I don't want to get into an argument the fact that there seems to be Psion prevalence on stuff really saddens me. Especially when I remember reading the new Aeon book during the kickstarter and going &quot;yeah, they upgraded the noetic power system, awesome!&quot; Now I have learned that its at the act of downgrading nova power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-18-2019, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:27:22-07:00","id":1325644,"title":"","content":"You know that tag for Warp that lets you see through the opening? How does that interact with the travel time for interstellar warps? In particular, the warps are two-way: you can step through to the destination and then step back to the origin. If it takes an appreciable amount of time to traverse the warp, does that mean that stepping through and back again takes twice as long? If so, how does the light from the destination arrive at the origin without taking the same amount of time?<br /> <br /> Perhaps light is an exception, and goes through the warp instantaneously regardless of distance. If so, someone who traverses a long-distance warp where you can see the destination will seem to disappear when he steps through and then will appear on the other side after the requisite transit time has passed. <br /> <br /> The most workable alternative would be that the scene you see through a one-hour warp is what was there an hour earlier \u2014 which would mean that for the first hour that the warp is open, you wouldn't be able to see through it, because the light from the other side won't have had time to traverse the warp yet. Note that even if light traverses the warp instantaneously, sound would be delayed. <br /> <br /> That said, the simplest solution would be to forbid this tag for off-planet warps: if it takes time to traverse the warp, you can't see where you're going until you get there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:32:18-07:00","id":1325647,"title":"","content":"Honestly Dataweaver the simplest and easiest solution is to remove the time delay aspect entirely. That way its more like a stargate wormhole - you go in the warp portal, you zoom around a tunnel a bit, you come out the exit warp portal, moments, maybe a minute or two, have passed. <br /> <br /> But I am also a fan of having it so Warp actually requires certain levels of successes for certain distances, with maybe Scale being used to represent how far one can go or how the success numbers translate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:44:33-07:00","id":1325651,"title":"","content":"I am trying on a easier way to explain. <br /> When you want to buy a power with a technique you create a Power Suit and get a free technique to it.<br /> The power suit don\u2019t have any trait, just have a number of dot and tags to be used by the techniques, for example:<br /> <br /> Power Suit (Fire Mastery) have 2 dots and 3 tags + 4 technique tags<br /> Base Power (Environmental Anima, Heat) 2 dots, Range, Variable and Continuous tag<br /> Technique 1 (Quantum attack) 2 dots (grant 2 free tags, incendiary), deadly, disintegrating, bean<br /> Technique 2 (Quantum aura) 2 dots incendiary, deadly<br /> Technique 3 (Quantum Field) 2 dots hard armor (3)<br /> Technique 4 (Flight) 2 dots and 3 non used tags<br /> <br /> What do you think?<br /> <br /> Edit: adjusted a bit to make different numbers and called the base power to not call free technique.<br /> Calculated again the tags, incendiary is a 2 tags tag.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-18-2019, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:48:47-07:00","id":1325652,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> why doe Power Suit have 4 tags but the actual techniques only have 3, that confuses me. .<br /> <br /> My other thought is to call Technique 1 the core or base effect, as that is basically what it is.<br /> <br /> But yes, as a general thing this makes sense to me and is basically what I have thought it was.<br /> <br /> Oh. As a thought because the rules says that no Technique can go over the base effect I look at that as it being allowed for a Technique to go under the base effect. <br /> <br /> So in you example case. <br /> <br /> Technique 5 (Flight) 2 dot, 3 tags <br /> <br /> Which represents that the player did not want to use the third dot for said power, for whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-18-2019, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:58:17-07:00","id":1325655,"title":"","content":"The alternative to getting rid of the time delay is to just not allow the clear tag to work on interstellar warps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T10:58:19-07:00","id":1325656,"title":"","content":"As an aside what do you guys think of a modification to the Calming Composure and Dreadful Presence Mega-Edges. <br /> <br /> For Calming Composure the new version would increases the emotional atmosphere in the area (with the focus being picked, so maybe excitement or joy or something else).<br /> <br /> For Dreadful Presence the feeling instilled is one of the other emotional states like acceptance or want or submission, which would create a positive attitude towards the nova. <br /> <br /> Mechanically the abilities are the same, just flipped. I think it fits for if you can create calm then you should be able to create joy and if you can manifest dread then why not submission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:10:35-07:00","id":1325657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325644#post1325644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that tag for Warp that lets you see through the opening? How does that interact with the travel time for interstellar warps? In particular, the warps are two-way: you can step through to the destination and then step back to the origin. If it takes an appreciable amount of time to traverse the warp, does that mean that stepping through and back again takes twice as long? If so, how does the light from the destination arrive at the origin without taking the same amount of time?<br /> <br /> Perhaps light is an exception, and goes through the warp instantaneously regardless of distance. If so, someone who traverses a long-distance warp where you can see the destination will seem to disappear when he steps through and then will appear on the other side after the requisite transit time has passed. <br /> <br /> The most workable alternative would be that the scene you see through a one-hour warp is what was there an hour earlier \u2014 which would mean that for the first hour that the warp is open, you wouldn't be able to see through it, because the light from the other side won't have had time to traverse the warp yet. Note that even if light traverses the warp instantaneously, sound would be delayed. <br /> <br /> That said, the simplest solution would be to forbid this tag for off-planet warps: if it takes time to traverse the warp, you can't see where you're going until you get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 8, first or second sentence, interstellar warps cannot be Clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:11:18-07:00","id":1325659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325652#post1325652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> why doe Power Suit have 4 tags but the actual techniques only have 3, that confuses me. .<br /> <br /> My other thought is to call Technique 1 the core or base effect, as that is basically what it is.<br /> <br /> But yes, as a general thing this makes sense to me and is basically what I have thought it was.<br /> <br /> Oh. As a thought because the rules says that no Technique can go over the base effect I look at that as it being allowed for a Technique to go under the base effect. <br /> <br /> So in you example case. <br /> <br /> Technique 5 (Flight) 2 dot, 3 tags <br /> <br /> Which represents that the player did not want to use the third dot for said power, for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I corrected as I didn\u2019t add the 4th tags of the techniques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-18-2019, 02:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:12:42-07:00","id":1325660,"title":"","content":"I just got the third update, powers and such. Can there be an Entropy Control, or a Probability Control added? A power that produces good luck or bad luck. Or could it be under the elemental control umbrella? I love powers like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:17:16-07:00","id":1325664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325644#post1325644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that tag for Warp that lets you see through the opening? How does that interact with the travel time for interstellar warps? In particular, the warps are two-way: you can step through to the destination and then step back to the origin. If it takes an appreciable amount of time to traverse the warp, does that mean that stepping through and back again takes twice as long? If so, how does the light from the destination arrive at the origin without taking the same amount of time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. In the section about Interstellar Warp Distances it states that 'Interstellar warps cannot be Clear'. (Its a single line at the top of page 8 of the 3rd preview, just above the table listing milestones and travel time for various lengths of Interstellar Warps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:17:40-07:00","id":1325665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325651#post1325651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying on a easier way to explain.<br /> When you want to buy a power with a technique you create a Power Suit and get a free technique to it.<br /> The power suit don\u2019t have any trait, just have a number of dot and tags to be used by the techniques, for example:<br /> <br /> Power Suit (Fire Mastery) have 2 dots and 3 tags + 4 technique tags<br /> Base Power (Environmental Anima, Heat) 2 dots, Range, Variable and Continuous tag<br /> Technique 1 (Quantum attack) 2 dots (grant 2 free tags, incendiary, aggravated), deadly, disintegrating, bean<br /> Technique 2 (Quantum aura) 2 dots incendiary, aggravated, deadly<br /> Technique 3 (Quantum Field) 2 dots Environmental (2), hard armor (1)<br /> Technique 4 (Flight) 2 dots and 3 non used tags<br /> <br /> What do you think?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this as an example as I think it makes sense. But even more if this is how the rule works then awesome. I am glad as it means I understand it. Which is brilliant. hehe<br /> <br /> But yeah, having an example like this really does help organize things. Its also cool because for 48 XP the nova gained the abilities equal to 60 XP (that is 3 dots, 3 tags) times 5 uses equal 300. NICE!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-18-2019, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:21:03-07:00","id":1325667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wtaylorjr2001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325660#post1325660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just got the third update, powers and such. Can there be an Entropy Control, or a Probability Control added? A power that produces good luck or bad luck. Or could it be under the elemental control umbrella? I love powers like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Elemental Mastery does list 'Entropy' as a suggested elemental theme. I could see 'Probability' being used as a theme for it as well. On the other hand, I've read somewhere (on the various forums/discord where this is being talked about) that 'Luck' as a 'power' is considered something Talents do and therefor not something novas or psion/psiads do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:23:00-07:00","id":1325669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325597#post1325597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s about the statement that psi is better for space exploration than quantum.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Which fits the world as presented. Interstellar colonization was always a big part of the 1e Trinity/Aeon setting, and never presented as a big thing in Aberrant. The rules fitting the setting as presented is a big plus for me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:32:54-07:00","id":1325676,"title":"","content":"Let me second the notion that Warp should have a maximum range that can be enhanced to off-planet distances by Scale rather than a built-in \u201cyou can Warp to anywhere you can see\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:33:13-07:00","id":1325677,"title":"","content":"On Probably Control I think a good way to look at it as adjusting potential for success for the nova and failure for an enemy. So this might be Environmental Anima that makes the area colder to reduce chance or warmer to better the outcome. Or Quantum Anima to control dice to come up 10s. Or a Mega-Edge that effects the ability to plan and gain successes at task.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise nothing says the nova can't think he is adjusting the power of Chance or Luck while mechanically he is simply using powers to direct things in his favor.<br /> <br /> Look at the Time Theme in the Elemental Mastery power as an idea as it gives suggesstions on how to artificially age a person. Tricks like that could easily be used to manipulate 'chance'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:34:54-07:00","id":1325680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325669#post1325669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which fits the world as presented. Interstellar colonization was always a big part of the 1e Trinity/Aeon setting, and never presented as a big thing in Aberrant. The rules fitting the setting as presented is a big plus for me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Novas colonized space before Psions were even a thing. They just did so after the Aberrant timeline since Novas did not see a reason to leave before the ultimatum as they focused making their home a better place for themselves. There was a section on space exploration in Aberrant Players Guide though. So while some Novas left earth to explore the great unknown Aberrant as a game did not go deep into the themes of space exploration partially because that was Aeon Trinitys area and partially because it still was somewhat a superhero game and even though superheroes may visit space on occasions the action usually is on earth.<br /> <br /> I dont personally remember when Eden was colonized but I do think it was during the Nova age which would again prove that Novas are pretty good at space exploration, terra forming and colonization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:40:05-07:00","id":1325681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325680#post1325680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that Novas colonized space before Psions were even a thing. They just did so after the Aberrant timeline since Novas did not see a reason to leave before the ultimatum as they focused making their home a better place for themselves. There was a section on space exploration in Aberrant Players Guide though. So while some Novas left earth to explore the great unknown Aberrant as a game did not go deep into the themes of space exploration partially because that was Aeon Trinitys area and partially because it still was somewhat a superhero game and even though superheroes may visit space on occasions the action usually is on earth.<br /> <br /> I dont personally remember when Eden was colonized but I do think it was during the Nova age which would again prove that Novas are pretty good at space exploration, terra forming and colonization.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which is harmed by it taking longer for Novas to warp to different solar systems. It just makes it harder to actively involve 2008/2028 general baseline population in said colonization - which perfectly fits the setting as portrayed. Novas who opt to go off the space are choosing to make a long hard journey it will take a long time to return from. How does that not fit the setting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-18-2019, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:41:10-07:00","id":1325682,"title":"","content":"Entropy Control can be done using Elemental Mastery (it\u2019s even described on the examples of elements).<br /> <br /> Luck is missing by name, but you can use Foresight for a interesting luck effect. It can also Jinx by editing a bad luck to the target. Maybe you may need an authorisation form the SG to do so.<br /> <br /> Probability control, that\u2019s one power that is fun to play and is missing completely as I remeber.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:47:13-07:00","id":1325683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325681#post1325681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of which is harmed by it taking longer for Novas to warp to different solar systems. It just makes it harder to actively involve 2008/2028 general baseline population in said colonization - which perfectly fits the setting as portrayed. Novas who opt to go off the space are choosing to make a long hard journey it will take a long time to return from. How does that not fit the setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we are arguing about different things. I am arguing against the statement that Psi is better for space exploration and you are about the time it takes to teleport/warp. My characters main powers are teleport and warp and have been for the past 10+ years so I am at peace with the travel times as per 1st ed. Though at many times the travel time has been handwaved away by the ST if it isn\u2019t integral to the plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:47:48-07:00","id":1325685,"title":"","content":"So do you think I could add a Tag for 12 XP to a purchase of Telecommunications Mega-Edge to make it usable on Baselines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:48:19-07:00","id":1325686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325677#post1325677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Probably Control I think a good way to look at it as adjusting potential for success for the nova and failure for an enemy. So this might be Environmental Anima that makes the area colder to reduce chance or warmer to better the outcome. Or Quantum Anima to control dice to come up 10s. Or a Mega-Edge that effects the ability to plan and gain successes at task.<br /> <br /> Fluff wise nothing says the nova can't think he is adjusting the power of Chance or Luck while mechanically he is simply using powers to direct things in his favor.<br /> <br /> Look at the Time Theme in the Elemental Mastery power as an idea as it gives suggesstions on how to artificially age a person. Tricks like that could easily be used to manipulate 'chance'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether the character is really manipulating probability or 'subconsciously' using tk/quantum anima to manipulate things, I also think Environmental Anima would make a good base for a Probability based Elemental Mastery. Stick primarily with adding and removing conditions (making things more or less likely to happen in someone's favor) or manipulating environmental damage (heightened or reduced odds of getting hit by environmental hazards). It would probably count as a non-terrestrial environment though. I could see those sort of 'changing the odds' descriptions justifying several techniques as well (such as Quantum Deflection, Quantum Field, Entangle Quantum Attacks, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:49:56-07:00","id":1325687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325685#post1325685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do you think I could add a Tag for 12 XP to a purchase of Telecommunications Mega-Edge to make it usable on Baselines?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can, but not by default...<br /> The default is Novas don do Telepathy, but there is always that universe where they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T11:59:25-07:00","id":1325689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325669#post1325669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which fits the world as presented. Interstellar colonization was always a big part of the 1e Trinity/Aeon setting, and never presented as a big thing in Aberrant. The rules fitting the setting as presented is a big plus for me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Several significant problems<br /> <br /> Because 2nd edition is not just part of the trinity timeline. It is its own thing its own superhero setting. Space exploration interaction and so on is impossible with these timetables while adding the conditions.Aliens are the traditional game-changer and so on. Here, You can NEVER react in time towards anything happening at a realistic space distance. Moments of heroism, coming in nick of time are impossible. Avengers endgame is impossible here. the time table kills it as a theme. <br /> <br /> It kills dead crossover theme in space. Psion will always run circles around novas and thus always win. They can witness the moving in and have weeks to months of preparation time before Nova force shows up on location. It is clear dominance of psions, that goes beyond ridiculous into comical. It is a difference of months to hours of travel.<br /> <br /> It is empty time. it is time, which does not happen for those in transit. there are no true distraction, no plans no nothing to do unless you fail at which point the game stops and you start a new one. World changes without the input of player characters, but characters remain static during that time.<br /> <br /> SPACE exploration and meeting aliens is a named subgenre of the book. Rules of warp as presented make it unsupported. This makes a significant part of the setting nearly impossible to do. it cripples one whole superhero theme, you are supposed to play.<br /> <br /> Do you want to do space exploration? Play psion should not be the obvious answer in the Aberrant game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T12:05:27-07:00","id":1325691,"title":"","content":"TC:Aberrant is first and foremost part of the Trinity Continuum. Being able to use the game in other ways is a nice bonus, but not too the extent of compromising that. This is true but just in terms of space travel, but also in terms of time travel, probability manipulation, telepathy, and precognition. <br /> <br /> There are hack that can be made to change these facts, some of which are even trivial to apply; but I wouldn't expect to find them in the TC:Aberrant manuscript.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T12:05:41-07:00","id":1325692,"title":"","content":"I'm curious as to what people think of the Mega-Attribute prerequisite dots for many Mega-Edges. Do you think they are too high, too low, or just right. I ask because I am going through it and are like &quot;ooh I want that Mega-Edge&quot; and then I realize it requires Mega-Cunning or Mega-Intellect at 2 or 3 dots and that means Quantum 2 or 3 and that means its unavailable to my character at the starting point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T12:18:22-07:00","id":1325696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325691#post1325691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TC:Aberrant is first and foremost part of the Trinity Continuum. Being able to use the game in other ways is a nice bonus, but not too the extent of compromising that. This is true but just in terms of space travel, but also in terms of time travel, probability manipulation, telepathy, and precognition.<br /> <br /> There are hack that can be made to change these facts, some of which are even trivial to apply; but I wouldn't expect to find them in the TC:Aberrant manuscript.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and thus there needs to be viable parity between splats. Psions can counter novas without requiring to get Nova. This is not true here. Nova will always fail miserably in the space exploration schtick in comparison without a way to mitigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T12:43:47-07:00","id":1325702,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver is completely correct.<br /> <br /> You can have an universe where the psions are worse then novas in every way. 1e it was true? No, it was not, not even close.<br /> <br /> You can have a universe where Aberrants could do Psychic stuff. 1e it was true? Yes, with a small note about the way it was happening.<br /> <br /> You can have a universe where Aberrants manipulate probability. 1e it was true? Yes it was (I had a really nice plan for a character with the ultimate positive thinking using luck, but not happening now)<br /> <br /> You can also have a universe where novas have magical powers and work as Mages, while psions are treated as hedge wizards. Or novas are gods and psions are wizards... it was definitely not true in 1e, and indoor think anyone here what that (except me, maybe).<br /> <br /> What they can work with is a \u201cwhat if\u201d book with lots of tiles that don\u2019t apply to their universe but can apply to others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T13:06:11-07:00","id":1325710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325691#post1325691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TC:Aberrant is first and foremost part of the Trinity Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the real problem with this 2nd edition. Aberrant 1st, just like Aeon Trinity, was first and foremost it\u2019s own game. 2nd edition should be first and foremost an Aberrant game and only secondly, or distantly, part of the greater Continuum.<br /> <br /> While the possibility of a crossover has always been there they were seperate game lines with their own systems. Now I was hoping that the Continuum and the Storypath System would make crossover easier not meld the two games at the cost of each other, or in this case mostly at the cost of Aberrant. They should be their own games that are combatible if one wants to use them thus, which means no niche protection should be necessary. Novas should still be able to have Telepathic powers since in Aberrant there are no Psions present for the most part. Similarly when playing Aeon Aberrants are mostly antagonist and those have their own rules. Besides if Telepathic Psions cant use their powers to fight Telepathic Aberrants attempts at mind controlling the Planet it does Aeon some injustice aswell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T13:15:07-07:00","id":1325713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325689#post1325689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Several significant problems<br /> <br /> Because 2nd edition is not just part of the trinity timeline. It is its own thing its own superhero setting. Space exploration interaction and so on is impossible with these timetables while adding the conditions.Aliens are the traditional game-changer and so on. Here, You can NEVER react in time towards anything happening at a realistic space distance. Moments of heroism, coming in nick of time are impossible. Avengers endgame is impossible here. the time table kills it as a theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it\u2019s own setting with no relation to Aeon, you lack Psions as a comparison point, so who are Novas worse than at space exploration?<br /> <br /> Alien worlds are a part of superhero comics, but Earth carrying out interstellar colonization generally is not. Novas still have the power to explore space and make alien contact etc - things like the time delay doesn\u2019t affect the player pic if you\u2019re doing an exploration game because it doesn\u2019t impact the people warping. It just impacts how much time it takes to get back - which fits with space exploration not having impacted Earth in 2028 yet.<br /> <br /> Inability to respond to alien threats \u201cin time\u201d assumes you\u2019re giving the aliens faster travel means - that was a decision you made, the setting doesn\u2019t do it.<br /> <br /> None of the main characters in Endgame have the inherent power to traverse solar systems or galaxies. Of the two supporting characters who do - 1 is using magic which is emphatically something the Aberrant setting does not do. I admit it makes it harder to play Captain Marvel specifically, but that doesn\u2019t really impact the Endgame example as she was just a supporting cameo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SPACE exploration and meeting aliens is a named subgenre of the book. Rules of warp as presented make it unsupported. This makes a significant part of the setting nearly impossible to do. it cripples one whole superhero theme, you are supposed to play. </div> </div> </div>How does the clock jumping further ahead back on Earth, or there being plothook Complications, make such games I supported?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T13:16:34-07:00","id":1325714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325710#post1325710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is probably the real problem with this 2nd edition. Aberrant 1st, just like Aeon Trinity, was first and foremost it\u2019s own game. 2nd edition should be first and foremost an Aberrant game and only secondly, or distantly, part of the greater Continuum.<br /> <br /> While the possibility of a crossover has always been there they were seperate game lines with their own systems. Now I was hoping that the Continuum and the Storypath System would make crossover easier not meld the two games at the cost of each other, or in this case mostly at the cost of Aberrant. They should be their own games that are combatible if one wants to use them thus, which means no niche protection should be necessary. Novas should still be able to have Telepathic powers since in Aberrant there are no Psions present for the most part. Similarly when playing Aeon Aberrants are mostly antagonist and those have their own rules. Besides if Telepathic Psions cant use their powers to fight Telepathic Aberrants attempts at mind controlling the Planet it does Aeon some injustice aswell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hold this exact same position. Especially considering that its supposed to be a Continuum rather than a single path in time. In fact this is the sort of thing I thought we were getting when they said no metaplot and no automatic forced path towards Aberrant War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T13:18:07-07:00","id":1325715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325710#post1325710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is probably the real problem with this 2nd edition. Aberrant 1st, just like Aeon Trinity, was first and foremost it\u2019s own game. 2nd edition should be first and foremost an Aberrant game and only secondly, or distantly, part of the greater Continuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re kind of trying to have it both ways though, since as a stand-alone game, Psions aren\u2019t a thing in Aberrant, so there\u2019s no comparison point to complain Novas aren\u2019t as good at interstellar warping than.<br /> <br /> Psiads are a thing, but it remains unclear for the moment whether Teleporation and Quantakinesis are on the table for Psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T13:31:24-07:00","id":1325720,"title":"","content":"Quick clarification: obviously, TC:Aberrant <i>is</i> \u201cit's own game\u201d first and foremost; but part of its identity is that it's part of the Trinity Continuum \u2014 which means that it's about psiads and Talents as well as Novas, and the Nova rules have to take that into account. <br /> <br /> When I said \u201cit's first and foremost part of the TC\u201d, I was contrasting that with \u201cit's a do-whatever-you-want-with-it superhero game\u201d. Which is not to say that you can't bend it to be more all-purpose than it is; you can, and it's not even all that hard to do. And some of that is even supported in the book with its Tones and Subgenres. <br /> <br /> But don't expect the writers to rewrite it as the Storypath edition of Mutants and Masterminds. Whether or not it \u201cshould\u201d be that, it isn't going to be; and arguments that it should be aren't constructive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T13:39:56-07:00","id":1325723,"title":"","content":"My one addition to this discussion is that while Psiads have a place in the current Aberrant setting Psions do not. For this reason I don't think there is anything wrong with the idea of saying Psiads should be able to stand toe to toe with Novas in an Aberrant setting game but its a different can of worms to say Psions should stand toe to toe with a Nova game.<br /> <br /> Here is the thing this point does change things, because Psiads are able to learn multiple dots in multiple Modes of multiple Aptitudes. This is different from Psions who are stuck at one Aptitude and one dot in other modes. This means a Psiad can reach power levels on an individual level potentially much higher than what Psions can reach, without them breaking the Doyn blocks and becoming something else.<br /> <br /> As another thing there really shouldn't be an automatic assumption that Novas will have to handle Psions in the Psion home turf, that is the Aeon game. The Continuum shouldn't mean that the Nova Age automatically ends in fire and then comes the Psion Age.<br /> <br /> It also really makes me think I wish that the Aeon game was more about Psiads than Psions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-18-2019, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T13:56:46-07:00","id":1325728,"title":"","content":"As we commented before, I prefere Psiads as they can fit much better in any game, same for novas capable of handling Psychic powers and luck powers, but it\u2019s not TC, it is a generic game options, like was said a SP version of M&amp;M.<br /> <br /> House ruling was always a thing in RPG, it is one of the things that brought us to the point we are, so many small companies with great ideas. Pick your favourite game and houserule the hell out of it, don\u2019t expect the guys like Ian, that are creating a setting to make their setting more or less generic.<br /> <br /> Imagine if in 96 someone said to the guys, ok I want to play superman, and it doesn\u2019t make sense if he is not an Alien, and suddenly we have humanoid aliens living in the Aberrant world. Would it be the same game? For sure No! Maybe we would have liked it, but it would not be the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-18-2019, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T14:00:52-07:00","id":1325729,"title":"","content":"I'm waiting for two things: the \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion and its section in psiads, and whatever TC:Aberrant has to say about psiads. <br /> <br /> As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> says, there <i>is</i> a <i>continuum</i>, not a <i>universe</i>: just because TC:Aberrant is the history of TC:\u00c6on, that doesn't mean they TC:\u00c6on is the destiny of TC:Aberrant. If you want to devise an alternate bench of the Continuum where the Nova Age also see the appearance of Prometheus Chambers and the simultaneous rise of psions, go for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T14:03:22-07:00","id":1325730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325689#post1325689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> SPACE exploration and meeting aliens is a named subgenre of the book. Rules of warp as presented make it unsupported. This makes a significant part of the setting nearly impossible to do. it cripples one whole superhero theme, you are supposed to play.<br /> <br /> Do you want to do space exploration? Play psion should not be the obvious answer in the Aberrant game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make the point that it makes it unsupported for your (and undoubtedly some other folk's) particular take on space exploration in a superhero context. <br /> <br /> In my case I actually really like that while it isn't fully &quot;realistic&quot; it has enough nods to &quot;realistic&quot; scale of space travel and the challenges involved that it doesn't feel like a hero on another world is effectively just in the next room or town over. It means space exploration is challenging, that planning has to happen, that choices are made and some of those choices may mean a powerful group of novas are unavailable for a while because they were needed on another world. If aliens that are not detected/predicted by one or another nova and therefor planned around happen to show up, whoever is on hand will have to step up and handle it or hold the fort until others can be summoned back.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T14:09:19-07:00","id":1325731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brennanhawkwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325667#post1325667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Elemental Mastery does list 'Entropy' as a suggested elemental theme. I could see 'Probability' being used as a theme for it as well. On the other hand, I've read somewhere (on the various forums/discord where this is being talked about) that 'Luck' as a 'power' is considered something Talents do and therefor not something novas or psion/psiads do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I found it. I just got the chapters. I think Probability Control is better than a Luck power. I want to write stories in the Trinity Continuum, Aberrant, and I want to tel stories about Probability Controllers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7592-wtaylorjr2001","name":"wtaylorjr2001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T14:22:58-07:00","id":1325733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Brennanhawkwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325730#post1325730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would make the point that it makes it unsupported for your (and undoubtedly some other folk's) particular take on space exploration in a superhero context.<br /> <br /> In my case I actually really like that while it isn't fully &quot;realistic&quot; it has enough nods to &quot;realistic&quot; scale of space travel and the challenges involved that it doesn't feel like a hero on another world is effectively just in the next room or town over. It means space exploration is challenging, that planning has to happen, that choices are made and some of those choices may mean a powerful group of novas are unavailable for a while because they were needed on another world. If aliens that are not detected/predicted by one or another nova and therefor planned around happen to show up, whoever is on hand will have to step up and handle it or hold the fort until others can be summoned back.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But that is my primary problem of the time scale, ouside of psion comparison. It was my was my first problem, even before the psion issue. You cannot do this properly. Travel simply takes too long and Nova powers and figts are too high end \u00b4.In sane distances(thousand to 20 thousand, that fits aeon distances and I do consider what distances should be) travel time is measured between day and months. Nova fights are quick devastating and impactful. Fights where you can throw nuke level powers at chargen(maxing out should allow this). These are not fight that should last days. Those are wars that should last hours and leave devastation beyond itself. If B team can resist this level of force for several days(even a day)- which means multiple at least one reacharge on attacker side. You did not need A team to begin with. Power scale of Nova fight does not work on the timetable avaiable, even if nova can keep up the battle going forth. Psions have time travel of hours allowing these scenarios. Like I said Abberant is not setting, where Avengers endgame stylized ending is truly possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T14:51:08-07:00","id":1325739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325733#post1325733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that is my primary problem of the time scale, ouside of psion comparison. It was my was my first problem, even before the psion issue. You cannot do this properly. Travel simply takes too long and Nova powers and figts are too high end \u00b4.In sane distances(thousand to 20 thousand, that fits aeon distances and I do consider what distances should be) travel time is measured between day and months. Nova fights are quick devastating and impactful. Fights where you can throw nuke level powers at chargen(maxing out should allow this). These are not fight that should last days. Those are wars that should last hours and leave devastation beyond itself. If B team can resist this level of force for several days(even a day)- which means multiple at least one reacharge on attacker side. You did not need A team to begin with. Power scale of Nova fight does not work on the timetable avaiable, even if nova can keep up the battle going forth. Psions have time travel of hours allowing these scenarios. Like I said Abberant is not setting, where Avengers endgame stylized ending is truly possible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the fundamental difference in our thoughts on this is that I don't see 'Avengers endgame stylized ending' as necessarily what I am after in an Aberrant game. That sort of thing is cool, but I don't see pretty much ANY of the MCU space stuff as 'space exploration / travel'. It is solidly on the 'space fantasy' and 'speed of plot' side of things. Not saying it isn't cool or that it has no place in some superhero games. I just don't see it as a part of the setting presented for Aberrant which, to me, has always had much more of a vibe of 'what would happen if super-powered people were added to the &lt;quote&gt;Real World&lt;/quote&gt;' which MCU and DC does not fit with in most/many cases.<br /> <br /> If/When I get a chance to run Aberrant 2ed, if my PCs do long range space travel, the times involved would simply have to be taking into account. It's no worse than having a party insist on splitting up over interstellar (or even intrastellar) distances in a game like Traveller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T15:49:05-07:00","id":1325757,"title":"","content":"Sooo looking over the Trinity Core the storyteller section suggests that minimum 5 to maximum 10 XP should be given to players per session. Which, really when you think about it, allows for some rapid growth. Two sessions could lead to a new Mega-Attribute, Mega-Edge, Quantum Power, or Power Tag. You could also purchase regular Edges, Skills, and even an Attribute. That's not actually bad on a growth level. <br /> <br /> It also means pretty quickly players will be saying &quot;I like my power, but I want to add a tag to modify it&quot; and before one knows it even players with similar powers will be going in directions quite unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T15:53:25-07:00","id":1325759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325720#post1325720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick clarification: obviously, TC:Aberrant <i>is</i> \u201cit's own game\u201d first and foremost; but part of its identity is that it's part of the Trinity Continuum \u2014 which means that it's about psiads and Talents as well as Novas, and the Nova rules have to take that into account. <br /> <br /> When I said \u201cit's first and foremost part of the TC\u201d, I was contrasting that with \u201cit's a do-whatever-you-want-with-it superhero game\u201d. Which is not to say that you can't bend it to be more all-purpose than it is; you can, and it's not even all that hard to do. And some of that is even supported in the book with its Tones and Subgenres. <br /> <br /> But don't expect the writers to rewrite it as the Storypath edition of Mutants and Masterminds. Whether or not it \u201cshould\u201d be that, it isn't going to be; and arguments that it should be aren't constructive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Storypath edition of M&amp;M is not what I am after, I think as I havent really delved into M&amp;M yet even if I did recently buy the PDF\u2019s. What I am after is Aberrant 1st edition but with better rules system underneath it. That does mean I want Telepath Novas for example. Especially as in one of our longest running games of all time, Aberrant going on 10+ years, one of the central characters is a Telepathic Pregoc Nova.<br /> <br /> It is kinda BS that now after 19 years of Aberrant, which means our game is actually 15+ years, the developers come and tell us we are playing it wrong for having Telepathic or Precognitive Novas. Why? Because of niche protection for the main splat of <b>another</b> game.<br /> <br /> That is in a way spitting in the face of us long time fans who have to either scrap our decades old characters or house rule like hell to keep them viable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T15:59:32-07:00","id":1325762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325757#post1325757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo looking over the Trinity Core the storyteller section suggests that minimum 5 to maximum 10 XP should be given to players per session. Which, really when you think about it, allows for some rapid growth. Two sessions could lead to a new Mega-Attribute, Mega-Edge, Quantum Power, or Power Tag. You could also purchase regular Edges, Skills, and even an Attribute. That's not actually bad on a growth level. <br /> <br /> It also means pretty quickly players will be saying &amp;quot;I like my power, but I want to add a tag to modify it&amp;quot; and before one knows it even players with similar powers will be going in directions quite unique.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, that is one point that is important on the development, I am used to the \u201cup to 5, and only if role play\u201d that we used to play on VtM (I don't like the acting part). One attribute dot every 2 sessions is a really nice curve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T16:21:54-07:00","id":1325764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325759#post1325759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Storypath edition of M&amp;M is not what I am after, I think as I havent really delved into M&amp;M yet even if I did recently buy the PDF\u2019s. What I am after is Aberrant 1st edition but with better rules system underneath it. That does mean I want Telepath Novas for example. Especially as in one of our longest running games of all time, Aberrant going on 10+ years, one of the central characters is a Telepathic Pregoc Nova.<br /> <br /> It is kinda BS that now after 19 years of Aberrant, which means our game is actually 15+ years, the developers come and tell us we are playing it wrong for having Telepathic or Precognitive Novas. Why? Because of niche protection for the main splat of <b>another</b> game.<br /> <br /> That is in a way spitting in the face of us long time fans who have to either scrap our decades old characters or house rule like hell to keep them viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dial it back, man, nobody's spitting in your face. But you're not buying a <i>generic</i> system, you're buying a system attached to a setting. That setting has certain assumptions. Assumptions that, at least in part, have changed.<br /> <br /> Suck it up. Adapt to the new thing. Suggest alterations if you want. But you're not endearing yourself to anyone, least of all the devs, by basically throwing a tantrum about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T16:36:57-07:00","id":1325768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325759#post1325759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Storypath edition of M&amp;M is not what I am after, I think as I havent really delved into M&amp;M yet even if I did recently buy the PDF\u2019s. What I am after is Aberrant 1st edition but with better rules system underneath it. That does mean I want Telepath Novas for example. Especially as in one of our longest running games of all time, Aberrant going on 10+ years, one of the central characters is a Telepathic Pregoc Nova.<br /> <br /> It is kinda BS that now after 19 years of Aberrant, which means our game is actually 15+ years, the developers come and tell us we are playing it wrong for having Telepathic or Precognitive Novas. Why? Because of niche protection for the main splat of <b>another</b> game.<br /> <br /> That is in a way spitting in the face of us long time fans who have to either scrap our decades old characters or house rule like hell to keep them viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one at Onyx Path is telling you you are or were playing Aberrant 1e wrong. If you have a 15+ year campaign, you are all clearly doing something very, very right - at least for your table. And the &quot;niche protection&quot; thing is not really what is involved in the way Trinity Continuum: Aberrant is dealing with the various types of PCs you can play throughout the Trinity Continuum. There is a logic behind it that is important for how things fit together throughout the overall setting. But seriously, &quot;spitting in the face of us long time fans&quot; because we can't go in and make every possible variant of characters from first edition work? There's no reason for that kind of talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:29:39-07:00","id":1325790,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I really consider this the silliest of complaints. Should Storypath also be bound to the <i>other</i> bad decisions of the first edition? Should all the Mega-attributes just give loads of dice? Should we... well, I'm being silly. The answer, obviously, is &quot;no&quot;.<br /> <br /> The writers of 1e Aberrant ignored what was <i>supposed</i> to be true for novas in favor of adding more 'standard' superhero powers. Note you can still often achieve the <i>effects</i> of those powers; If my mega-intellect can predict a baseline's actions super-accurately because I am running a very accurate mental simulation of them in my head, does it matter that it isn't &quot;really&quot; mind-reading?<br /> <br /> It's also the easiest thing in the world to 'hack'. We have XP costs for psions. Novas get a load of XP. If you really, really don't care about the whole continuum thing... just let Novas buy psion stuff like they buy everything else. Use Quantum in place of Psi if you don't want two power stats.<br /> <br /> Similarly, space travel. Frankly, &quot;it takes me awhile to get to the next star&quot; is still a hell of a lot better than what we have in the <i>actual</i> timeline where Alpha Centauri is several human lifetimes away, but it might be understandable if baseline humanity might get nervous about setting up colonies whose only transportation is a handful of novas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:52:33-07:00","id":1325801,"title":"","content":"Ok I have another question about Scale when it is not rolled. Specifically, Durability. I know if you are &gt;2 scale above something, you cannot be harmed. But what if you are 1 or 2 Scale higher? You aren't making a roll, so you have nothing to apply Enhancements to. Would you instead increase difficulty or add complications?<br /> <br /> Specifically a Durability 4 Quantum Field Nova is being shot by a Scale 2 Rifle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:53:25-07:00","id":1325803,"title":"","content":"Seeing this in Elemental Mastery - &quot;Time Mastery Quantum Attacks may include rapidly aging a target (an Aggravated Poison Attack) or Entangle Quantum Attacks that \u201cfreeze\u201d targets in time.&quot; has me realizing that there are much more potential options in what we can do with the power system then what it first seems like. I mean the idea tha na Aggravated Poison Attack will represent rapidly aging a target is just brilliant. <br /> <br /> But the thing is its going to take some time getting used to, to wrap our heads around the variable ways to go about doing things. <br /> <br /> To the writers and developers who read this forum, and those who learn about what is said here from those who do read it, awesome work on making a system that uses the same mechanics to represent both burning someone and aging them militarily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T17:55:37-07:00","id":1325804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325803#post1325803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing this in Elemental Mastery - &quot;Time Mastery Quantum Attacks may include rapidly aging a target (an Aggravated Poison Attack) or Entangle Quantum Attacks that \u201cfreeze\u201d targets in time.&quot; has me realizing that there are much more potential options in what we can do with the power system then what it first seems like. I mean the idea tha na Aggravated Poison Attack will represent rapidly aging a target is just brilliant.<br /> <br /> But the thing is its going to take some time getting used to, to wrap our heads around the variable ways to go about doing things.<br /> <br /> To the writers and developers who read this forum, and those who learn about what is said here from those who do read it, awesome work on making a system that uses the same mechanics to represent both burning someone and aging them militarily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I don't recall if they got played as an active character or not, but I had a friend make a Speedster Nova with disintegration in 1E that literally would pluck someone apart on a molecular scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T18:32:21-07:00","id":1325811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325803#post1325803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing this in Elemental Mastery - &amp;quot;Time Mastery Quantum Attacks may include rapidly aging a target (an Aggravated Poison Attack) or Entangle Quantum Attacks that \u201cfreeze\u201d targets in time.&amp;quot; has me realizing that there are much more potential options in what we can do with the power system then what it first seems like. I mean the idea tha na Aggravated Poison Attack will represent rapidly aging a target is just brilliant. <br /> <br /> But the thing is its going to take some time getting used to, to wrap our heads around the variable ways to go about doing things. <br /> <br /> To the writers and developers who read this forum, and those who learn about what is said here from those who do read it, awesome work on making a system that uses the same mechanics to represent both burning someone and aging them militarily.</div> </div> </div> </div>You must go the other way around, choose the power you want and than try to assemble it from the powers from the book.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say I want to make a character that can the target blood, very sadistic by the way, but still in Avatar, legend of Aang. You start thinking what you can do with it, you can animate it like water if it\u2019s out of the body, you can force it out of the character body and you can command the body of the target, not all his functions, and he probably can try to resist, but yes, you can make him dance if you want.<br /> <br /> Blood mastery is the power suit<br /> For the blood out of the body go for Quantum Anima restricted to blood only (worth -2 tags probably)<br /> For taking the blood out of the body let\u2019s make a quantum attack innocuous (there is no trace linking you and the target), aggravated and deadly (well what you expected)<br /> For the body command, quantum Anima again restricted to living bodies with blood (-1 tag is enough), than give the tags manipulation, grab and strike (hands are for that), if you want to blood control a munch of people go for scale, if you want to keep slaves go for duration, things like that.<br /> <br /> Imagination is the key for flexibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T19:24:13-07:00","id":1325819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325768#post1325768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one at Onyx Path is telling you you are or were playing Aberrant 1e wrong. If you have a 15+ year campaign, you are all clearly doing something very, very right - at least for your table. And the &amp;quot;niche protection&amp;quot; thing is not really what is involved in the way Trinity Continuum: Aberrant is dealing with the various types of PCs you can play throughout the Trinity Continuum. There is a logic behind it that is important for how things fit together throughout the overall setting. But seriously, &amp;quot;spitting in the face of us long time fans&amp;quot; because we can't go in and make every possible variant of characters from first edition work? There's no reason for that kind of talk.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to agree with Rich here. I get it, I love 1e, I have a game still on going and my main character a Q8 now with telepathy can not easily be imported into ATC. <br /> I don\u2019t agree with some of the creation be choices Ian has made. So in come the house rules. I don\u2019t think they are spitting in our face. I think Ian pitch Rich a revised world with some good story hooks and Rich said yes. <br /> My personal feelings aside I love what they have done within Trinity, I love what they have done with Aeon and I\u2019ll house rule, as I do with all the RPGs I play, what dose not work for me or my group. <br /> Wait and see what happens with the fallow up books. Yes it would have been nice for a good heads up on these changes but at the same time if there going to tell us everything they are planning why would we buy the books. <br /> Some people love the changes some people hate the changes. I have house rules for 1e several pages long and still tweak things as I go. So keep playing 1e and in time look at the Nexus or other fan sites and find the home brew stuff your looking for or heck, maybe you can write it up and make some money. <br /> I feel your pain but at the same time nothing but props for OP and Ian for the great work they have done!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T20:36:45-07:00","id":1325845,"title":"","content":"Oh, so for the record if you want to purchase a Power Tag that has say a (2) after it, that's 24XP right, twelve per dot. I figure it is but I just wanted to make sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T21:29:20-07:00","id":1325865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325845#post1325845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, so for the record if you want to purchase a Power Tag that has say a (2) after it, that's 24XP right, twelve per dot. I figure it is but I just wanted to make sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, by my reading. You can reduce this cost with negative power tags, although I believe you still need Quantum to get said tags.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T23:32:59-07:00","id":1325892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325811#post1325811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You must go the other way around, choose the power you want and than try to assemble it from the powers from the book.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s say I want to make a character that can the target blood, very sadistic by the way, but still in Avatar, legend of Aang. You start thinking what you can do with it, you can animate it like water if it\u2019s out of the body, you can force it out of the character body and you can command the body of the target, not all his functions, and he probably can try to resist, but yes, you can make him dance if you want.<br /> <br /> Blood mastery is the power suit<br /> For the blood out of the body go for Quantum Anima restricted to blood only (worth -2 tags probably)<br /> For taking the blood out of the body let\u2019s make a quantum attack innocuous (there is no trace linking you and the target), aggravated and deadly (well what you expected)<br /> For the body command, quantum Anima again restricted to living bodies with blood (-1 tag is enough), than give the tags manipulation, grab and strike (hands are for that), if you want to blood control a munch of people go for scale, if you want to keep slaves go for duration, things like that.<br /> <br /> Imagination is the key for flexibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is rather wobbly to me, for the restricted tag of-2 to apply target would not have blood half Time. You always need grab unless IT is spilled blood As bllod always moves.<br /> <br /> You can forgo Q attack and go for strike tag here.<br /> It is all also kinda expensive,even with free tags, but that is to be expected here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T02:35:30-07:00","id":1325915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325768#post1325768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No one at Onyx Path is telling you you are or were playing Aberrant 1e wrong. If you have a 15+ year campaign, you are all clearly doing something very, very right - at least for your table. And the &amp;quot;niche protection&amp;quot; thing is not really what is involved in the way Trinity Continuum: Aberrant is dealing with the various types of PCs you can play throughout the Trinity Continuum. There is a logic behind it that is important for how things fit together throughout the overall setting. But seriously, &amp;quot;spitting in the face of us long time fans&amp;quot; because we can't go in and make every possible variant of characters from first edition work? There's no reason for that kind of talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for your response Rich.<br /> <br /> Sorry for loosing my temper a bit there but Aberrant has been one of my favourite games of all times, from any developer. And when playing such a long campaign that you think you can move onto a new better system, and a system that when looking at both earlier books of TC and Scion seems more flexible than the old one, but then you find out something you never even thought of as possible that you cannot convert all characters to the new system. When the new system is as flexible as it is the last thing you think is that it will take away character options instead of adding them.<br /> <br /> Quite the opposite seems to be the case with Exalted 3rd, where all the previous concepts (even my 1st ed Lunar who was converted to 2nd ed and now is going to be converted 3rd time without loosing parts on the way, on the contrary he/she/it only gains more flexibility each conversion) work in the new editions, with the possible future exception of Infernals but of that I am aware of years in advance. <br /> In Aberrant this bomb was just dropped casually shutting down huge amount of character concepts. Yes I can House rule it to hell and back to get all the 1st edition characters to work again, and it seems I have to, but that to me seems, forgive me, as bad design. When doing a new edition of a popular game with even more flexible system it just seems, to me atleast and it appears like I am not alone in this, like bad design to change things so that you no longer can make whole categories of characters that were viable during the games original edition. Cause it is really easy to predict that shutting down such huge areas will affect the characters people are playing and have been playing for a long time.<br /> <br /> House rules are something that form for any game played long enough but for the most part they are things that come to being after playing for a while and noticing that something works better like this on our table Etc. I have never before bought a game that I have to House rule before the first session so it can even be played. That is my current problem with Aberrant 2nd. I have to House rule it like hell before the first session so there can be a first session and that just seems like really poor game design.<br /> <br /> I do suspect that some of our 1st ed House rules may follow to the new edition and that is fine, but having to start converting rules for iconic powers is a bit disheartening to say the least. <br /> <br /> I know that the decisions have already been made and there is nothing we can do about it now, but I still do think that these things need to be said aloud. There is likely no chance for a strecth goal of a pdf that would convert the old 1st edition powers shut out by the new decisions along with perhaps a way to bleed out Transcendence so as to keep the old themes of Aberrant alive in this new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T03:09:55-07:00","id":1325922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325892#post1325892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is rather wobbly to me, for the restricted tag of-2 to apply target would not have blood half Time. You always need grab unless IT is spilled blood As bllod always moves.<br /> <br /> You can forgo Q attack and go for strike tag here.<br /> It is all also kinda expensive,even with free tags, but that is to be expected here.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the blood out of body I considered that a -1 would be Quantum Anima for water or earth, so blood would be at least -2 as it is common on a combat field.<br /> <br /> For quantum Anima the restriction -1 is based not on the number of people with blood, but in the fact that quantum Anima is telekinesis, so restricting to only creatures with blood is a big restriction. I would use restrictions for basically anything other than pure telekinesis: only metals -1, only water -1, only Earth -1, only air (in earth no restrictions, it\u2019s everywhere, in space -1), only robots -2 or even -3 according to the amount of robots around.<br /> <br /> About the number of tags and dots, I was not working on it, it was more like a conceptual idea of what it could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T05:45:57-07:00","id":1325947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325803#post1325803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the writers and developers who read this forum, and those who learn about what is said here from those who do read it, awesome work on making a system that uses the same mechanics to represent both burning someone and aging them militarily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I will always sing the praises of conditions. Being able to use injury conditions to model a broken leg or quantum-induced arthritis is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","ra