and it seems I have to, but that to me seems, forgive me, as bad design. When doing a new edition of a popular game with even more flexible system it just seems, to me atleast and it appears like I am not alone in this, like bad design to change things so that you no longer can make whole categories of characters that were viable during the games original edition. Cause it is really easy to predict that shutting down such huge areas will affect the characters people are playing and have been playing for a long time.<br /> <br /> House rules are something that form for any game played long enough but for the most part they are things that come to being after playing for a while and noticing that something works better like this on our table Etc. I have never before bought a game that I have to House rule before the first session so it can even be played. That is my current problem with Aberrant 2nd. I have to House rule it like hell before the first session so there can be a first session and that just seems like really poor game design.<br /> <br /> I do suspect that some of our 1st ed House rules may follow to the new edition and that is fine, but having to start converting rules for iconic powers is a bit disheartening to say the least. <br /> <br /> I know that the decisions have already been made and there is nothing we can do about it now, but I still do think that these things need to be said aloud. There is likely no chance for a strecth goal of a pdf that would convert the old 1st edition powers shut out by the new decisions along with perhaps a way to bleed out Transcendence so as to keep the old themes of Aberrant alive in this new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a note, most of the mental nonsense can still be done. There just isn\u2019t a \u201ctelepathy\u201d power. The telecommunication mega edge and... something... read mega-edge take care of most of that. And if it must be a distinct power, just combine em.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T11:15:00-07:00","id":1326042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1325957#post1325957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a note, most of the mental nonsense can still be done. There just isn\u2019t a \u201ctelepathy\u201d power. The telecommunication mega edge and... something... read mega-edge take care of most of that. And if it must be a distinct power, just combine em.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also add that sooner or later the Storypath Nexus will be open to works for TC:Aberrant; and when that happens, I expect \u2014 no, I <i>anticipate</i> \u2014 that someone will do the work to produce Quantum Powers and Mega-Edges covering those areas that TC:Aberrant passed by. Heck, most of them can be addressed by the rules as written with very minor changes. Want actual time travel? Reskin Teleport and Warp to bridge gaps in time rather than space. As Jetstream points out in the section quoted here, Telepathy can be managed through a minor variation on Telecommunications. Others have pointed out that, while Elemental Mastery doesn't explicitly cover probability manipulation, it <i>could</i> if the Storyguide wants to allow it. And so on. <br /> <br /> And to that end, I've actually been enjoying the posts that have been exploring just how much you can do with the rules as written, and especially \u201cmost bang for the buck\u201d house rules: X isn't possible under the rules as written; what's the smallest change we could make that would allow for X (the smallest \u2018cost\u2019), and what else could that change allow (the biggest \u2018bang\u2019)?\u201d They might be better off being spun off into a separate thread, so that this one can concentrate on e TC:Ab project itself; but they're definitely worth discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-19-2019, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T19:12:39-07:00","id":1326150,"title":"","content":"So for some reason, and I am not sure what this says about me*, but the first set of characters I come up with are mostly Mega-Attribute and Mega-Edge sorts of novas. One a businessman with crafting and management abilities and the second a doctor with social manipulation abilities. The fact is, I am not focusing on the Quantum Powers themselves, which is an interesting mindset to be in. <br /> <br /> But even more amusing to me is that the first power I did come up with is something I call &quot;Quantum Sorcery&quot; and is basically the idea of a nova who wises to understand and utilize the fundamental energies that novas use. (And yes, I know, its not really sorcery, he knows it as well in setting, but I like the imagery and name, hehe.)<br /> <br /> *I think it says that I really like the way that Talent powers are written up and that my mindset almost immediately went more towards say Stalwart (/Memerist) stuff then it does full blown nova powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-19T19:30:59-07:00","id":1326153,"title":"","content":"Quantum Sorcery: the Aberrant version of Green Lantern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T02:57:49-07:00","id":1326228,"title":"","content":"Funny interaction I seem to have stumbled upon, which solves my Warp speed issue. I just do not think it is intended behavior.<br /> <br /> It is significantly quicker to use interstellar warp jumps of first range instead of making long jumps. Warp destination is rough, what you see in the sky, so you can small jump and with Reduced cost tag it is rather feasible option. You get no complication and quick travel time. You can traverse distance of 1000 ly in 4 hours, instead of stated day(1st travels 25 ly in 5minutes. so you would need 40 jumps to traverse 1000 ly. There is nor roll and reduced cost can make itcost 0 quantum, 40 jumps take 200 minutes, which is roughly 3 hours and bit) and not pick any complications at all It gets worse. You can travel the span of the galaxy in 13 days just jumping small jumps, instead of 2 months, once more without complications. It even solves my narrative issues, as it is actual travel time.<br /> <br /> It is somewhat expensive in experience points with double reduced cost, but it makes the chart rather useless and the complication rule meaningless. Reduced cost can be bought easily and is explicitly multibuy power. You would also need a mege intellect or software to pick next target, but that is not significant expense here.<br /> <br /> Note: How do you get rid of complication without successes? Pay momentum? You will pick them quickly, if you warp travel in a normal way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T05:13:53-07:00","id":1326245,"title":"","content":"Complications are tricky because they can be avoided (different from the difficulty) but usually have some bad results for leaving them.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know which complications you want to get rid, but if it\u2019s related to the navigation, I would state there is a chance you end up too close to a star and must Warp away before die, or you need to do an extra Warp to get to the target because you went too much to the right for example, not every jump, just when you less expect it... buahaha","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T05:54:28-07:00","id":1326248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326245#post1326245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complications are tricky because they can be avoided (different from the difficulty) but usually have some bad results for leaving them.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know which complications you want to get rid, but if it\u2019s related to the navigation, I would state there is a chance you end up too close to a star and must Warp away before die, or you need to do an extra Warp to get to the target because you went too much to the right for example, not every jump, just when you less expect it... buahaha</div> </div> </div> </div>For every range band after the first one during Interstellar warp, you pick a complication. Warp does not roll and dealing with you hit different system arrived at the wrong time during every jump gets boring fast, so there should be a way to negate those complications, but you do not roll for Warp, how do you create complications, which are repeatable, not game crippling and IT does happen EVERYjump. That is once more at a sane interstellar distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T06:11:49-07:00","id":1326249,"title":"","content":"You roll for navigation, that\u2019s where you can fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T06:43:56-07:00","id":1326254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326249#post1326249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You roll for navigation, that\u2019s where you can fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay now I am confused, why would you roll for navigation? You already know the location. Warp does not have plotted course and lacks roll. I am missing something here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T07:09:43-07:00","id":1326258,"title":"","content":"You are Warping to a place that you can see where was 25 years ago, so you must calculate the future position. At least that is the kind of thing that I got.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking, do you think a Nova would need a reference point to Warp, or is it possible to pick a point in the middle of nowhere, really nowhere, like 10ly away from any star or other possible reference. It would be the most difficult place to look for him, nice place to build a small fortress of solitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T07:40:57-07:00","id":1326260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326258#post1326258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are Warping to a place that you can see where was 25 years ago, so you must calculate the future position. At least that is the kind of thing that I got.<br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking, do you think a Nova would need a reference point to Warp, or is it possible to pick a point in the middle of nowhere, really nowhere, like 10ly away from any star or other possible reference. It would be the most difficult place to look for him, nice place to build a small fortress of solitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Navigation: I would say, you do not have to because you would need to calculate distance, even when jumping to familiar places around the earth, as the location shifts too and WarP description lack the wobbliness to allow this. Warp trucks you out in the place you want to go, unless it does not thanks to Complications.<br /> <br /> Per the plain text description. I would say no. The reference point of the star is necessary. In expanded read i.e interpreting somewhat. I would allow it. That a point star iI can see and that a point dark locations I picked somewhere around there should, in my opinion, be valid.<br /> <br /> I get why is it kinda no in the text it would make the base untraceable, but finding entrance into somewhere untraceable is so superhero it hurts, so I would allow it on these grounds too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T16:50:36-07:00","id":1326366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bulshock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1324407#post1324407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very good point. For the record when I said that it was potentially possible to do quantum powers with science I wasn't talking about with technology we would understand in our modern times. I was talking about ten thousand or more years from now.<br /> <br /> But yes, the psychological impact is very important, and I did disregard it because I didn't think about how most people aren't going to think of technology and science like I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fair. I do think technology becomes an &quot;assumed&quot; part of human existence, sometimes fairly rapidly. For example, I recall a time when I didn't have access to the sum total of human knowledge in a little rectangle in my pocket, but I'm not sure how I lived without it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T18:20:27-07:00","id":1326379,"title":"","content":"For my two cents, I think imposing these new limitations on Novas is a mistake for the game line. Granted, it's a small one, but it's of the sort that in a few years, after the fanbase has patched it with homebrew, will be the butt of jokes. It's Infinite Mastery: Flux Boogaloo.<br /> <br /> People didn't look past that horrid cover of a dead, glassy-eyed kid on Aberrant 1e decades ago to be told &quot;no, telepathy and precog are for someone else.&quot;<br /> <br /> How do I know?<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;What would you do with the power of a god?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> I don't see equivocation.<br /> I don't see &quot;Play superhero DnD! Each class gets their own game and timeline!&quot;<br /> I don't see &quot;Play the Strongman for your Telepath friends!&quot;<br /> I don't see &quot;Jean Gray send-ups need not apply!&quot;<br /> <br /> If Trinity were closer to Exalted, where cross-splat play is intended and regular, then it makes sense to work the setting and the various supery boojums to create some interesting gaps and dependencies. But the opposite is true. The setting goes out of its way to separate the intended focus characters by time, and makes a point of saying the events of one game don't have to impact another. This, in fact, is the perfect setup for a series of games that deliver on their core premise *first*, and cross-pollinate *second*.<br /> <br /> Simply put, these decisions undermine the core premise of Aberrant, that of power, freedom, and consequence. It sacrifices what makes Aberrant special on the alter of Trinity, a bad move. If I'm going out of my way to distance these playable thingies from each other, why the hell would I kneecap one in service to the whole? It's easier for my customers to subtract content they don't need/like than the opposite.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only reason, off-hand, I can imagine for keeping Novas out of &quot;psychic stuff&quot; in their own freaking game is to make uber-NPC Psions to push around the PCs. Anyone who's been engaged with WW/OPP knows that playbook.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, how am I, as a ST trying to introduce new people to gaming, going to sell a game &quot;about superheroes, but without support for your favorite characters?&quot;<br /> <br /> Simple answer: <b>I'm not.</b><br /> <br /> I've got enough trouble convincing people to read a book to play a game. Anything I pitch has to be gold outta the gate, not after I make ten pages of addenda to correct a silly oversight.<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR: </b>People bought Aberrant to play telepaths/precogs/warpers/all the things. Don't sell us games about godlike power with more fine print than a credit card.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T18:36:47-07:00","id":1326382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326379#post1326379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my two cents, I think imposing these new limitations on Novas is a mistake for the game line. Granted, it's a small one, but it's of the sort that in a few years, after the fanbase has patched it with homebrew, will be the butt of jokes. It's Infinite Mastery: Flux Boogaloo.<br /> <br /> People didn't look past that horrid cover of a dead, glassy-eyed kid on Aberrant 1e decades ago to be told &quot;no, telepathy and precog are for someone else.&quot;<br /> <br /> How do I know?<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;What would you do with the power of a god?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> I don't see equivocation.<br /> I don't see &quot;Play superhero DnD! Each class gets their own game and timeline!&quot;<br /> I don't see &quot;Play the Strongman for your Telepath friends!&quot;<br /> I don't see &quot;Jean Gray send-ups need not apply!&quot;<br /> <br /> If Trinity were closer to Exalted, where cross-splat play is intended and regular, then it makes sense to work the setting and the various supery boojums to create some interesting gaps and dependencies. But the opposite is true. The setting goes out of its way to separate the intended focus characters by time, and makes a point of saying the events of one game don't have to impact another. This, in fact, is the perfect setup for a series of games that deliver on their core premise *first*, and cross-pollinate *second*.<br /> <br /> Simply put, these decisions undermine the core premise of Aberrant, that of power, freedom, and consequence. It sacrifices what makes Aberrant special on the alter of Trinity, a bad move. If I'm going out of my way to distance these playable thingies from each other, why the hell would I kneecap one in service to the whole? It's easier for my customers to subtract content they don't need/like than the opposite.<br /> <br /> In fact, the only reason, off-hand, I can imagine for keeping Novas out of &quot;psychic stuff&quot; in their own freaking game is to make uber-NPC Psions to push around the PCs. Anyone who's been engaged with WW/OPP knows that playbook.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, how am I, as a ST trying to introduce new people to gaming, going to sell a game &quot;about superheroes, but without support for your favorite characters?&quot;<br /> <br /> Simple answer: <b>I'm not.</b><br /> <br /> I've got enough trouble convincing people to read a book to play a game. Anything I pitch has to be gold outta the gate, not after I make ten pages of addenda to correct a silly oversight.<br /> <br /> <b>TL;DR: </b>People bought Aberrant to play telepaths/precogs/warpers/all the things. Don't sell us games about godlike power with more fine print than a credit card.</div> </div> </div> </div> i think that strongman line is willfully disingenuios given that Novas are also the unparalleled geniuses, charismatic superstars, etc.<br /> <br /> Speaking for myself and myself alone - the \u201ceverything you can do I can do better\u201d factor was a pet peeve of mine in 1e, and I\u2019m strongly in favor of Novas having to use Mega-Socials to control others and Mega-Mentals to deduce information with superhuman accuracy. You can still do a lot of the same things but in ways that make Novas more distinct and interesting.<br /> <br /> The fact that the developers for the Aberrant core 21 years ago ignored the line creator\u2019s intent and gave Novas a kitchen sink power list is not a reason to repeat that. It\u2019s not Mutants and Masterminds where it\u2019s a toolkit to do any superhero setting, Aberrant has distinct themes and setting and Novas have a distinct place in the Continuum. Don\u2019t compromise that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-20-2019, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T18:39:36-07:00","id":1326383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326382#post1326382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i think that strongman line is willfully disingenuios given that Novas are also the unparalleled geniuses, charismatic superstars, etc.<br /> <br /> Speaking for myself and myself alone - the \u201ceverything you can do I can do better\u201d factor was a pet peeve of mine in 1e, and I\u2019m strongly in favor of Nova having to use Mega-Socials to control others and Mega-Mentals to deduce information with superhuman accuracy. You can still do a lot of the same things but in ways that make Quantum more distinct and interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also, let's not forget that you can reskin these Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges into psychic abilities, because that's how your character views them as working. And I'm sure that the Powers can also be reskinned accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T19:25:49-07:00","id":1326388,"title":"","content":"Setting-wise, I can understand the No Telepaths or Precogs bit. Understand, yes, agree with, not so much. This is a continuum filled with quantum possibility, our paths aren't narrow. The Abby War may very well not happen. Some genius may sniff out Doyen interference and take the fight to them long before Psions ever get created. Anything can, and should be able, to happen.<br /> <br /> That said, perhaps we could see some rules covering telepathy and precog followed by a recommendation to withhold those powers if the SG wants to run a campaign more inline with the setting? We already have genre guidelines, put those powers in 4 color(where they belong) while mentioning their removal in cinematic perhaps? Onyx gets a more fleshed out game which will no doubt sell better, and the player base gets more options. Everybody benefits.<br /> <br /> All in all, at its roots, this is a Supers game we're talking about, and telepathy is pretty much standard fare these days. Probably best not to alienate the playerbase when a few simple options would solve the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24598-shadows-and-dust","name":"Shadows and Dust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T20:40:49-07:00","id":1326395,"title":"","content":"Guys, as far as we know, the Psiad Powers are as flexible as Nova Powers (not as powerful or with the same variety of powers), and can possibly be built on a similar way of the novas, to the point it can be freely used as telepathy and precognition for novas.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s give the creation team some time and if it is not that case, let\u2019s work individually or as a team to build options to fill the gap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T21:08:20-07:00","id":1326396,"title":"","content":"As I said before, I'm waiting for the psiads section. I will not be at all surprised if that section includes Psi Powers for Telepathy and Precognition that are functionally equivalent to Quantum Powers (except that their spelling for \u201cQuantum\u201d is \u201dpee-ess-eye\u201d and maybe they cap the Scale lower than normal).<br /> <br /> As well, for those branches of the Continuum that deviated from the Aberrant-to-\u00c6on timeline, what's wrong with just allowing high-tier psiads alongside your Novas? What's with the insistence that psychic powers must be explained via M/R Coils and Quantum? It's not like this would be the first setting where different empowered humans have different power sources.<br /> <br /> Put another way:<br /> <br /> \u201cHow do I write up Jean Grey?\u201d<br /> \u201cAs a Proxie-level psiad.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-21-2019, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T21:13:50-07:00","id":1326397,"title":"","content":"Wait, I thpight Psiad powers were basically just psion powers but with little to no restriction on how many Aptitudes and Modes a Psiad can access. Are we saying that the ecpectations is an entire new power chain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T21:22:36-07:00","id":1326398,"title":"","content":"In 1e, Aberrant's psiads were written up using Quantum Powers.<br /> <br /> The point is that it is too early to have expectations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T21:23:00-07:00","id":1326399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326397#post1326397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, I thpight Psiad powers were basically just psion powers but with little to no restriction on how many Aptitudes and Modes a Psiad can access. Are we saying that the ecpectations is an entire new power chain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Modes Psions use are mechanical way to develop causes by the way doyens operated. They can use the entire set of a mode by the moment they are dunked, but they need to master it to be able to do more often.<br /> <br /> Psiads have no limitations, but also have no kickstart on their powers, so their powers can be as flexible as Nova powers, limited by the themes, of course, but still no need to follow the psion rules.<br /> <br /> So, yes, we may se some psiad pores similar to quantum powers.<br /> <br /> And I about the Superior powers, I think they are basically a subset of the Novas Mega Attributes and Mega-Edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T21:24:54-07:00","id":1326401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326398#post1326398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, Aberrant's psiads were written up using Quantum Powers.<br /> <br /> The point is that it is too early to have expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a option using Trinity modes, but if I remember correctly, it was said it would be better to use Aberrant rules for that end than the modes.s","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T22:19:06-07:00","id":1326403,"title":"","content":"I always thought the &quot;Build Psiads using Aberrant Rules&quot; was a shortcut because its the Aberrant Player's Guide and thus they didn't assume one had the Trinity Core Book. I had always thought that the &quot;Build Psiads using Trinity Rules&quot; was more in theme and accurate in terms of representing the powers. That is, Psiad powers were based on Aptitudes and Modes, just with no restriction. I even thought that this was the official standard to look at. Which meant, I figured, that when we got the Psiad Rules in the Aeon Aexpansion it wasn't going to be that long because it didn't to be, because all the powers that the Psiads would have would be the ones in the Aeon Core Book, with some slight modification. <br /> <br /> Is it official that the whole Aptitude and Mode system was a Doyn invention and not the actual structured way that a noetic practitioner manifests their powers? <br /> <br /> Are we really expecting that the Psiad rules are going to have dozens of pages of new powers described within? Even though there is a perfectly good Aeon Core Book with dozens of pages of psychic powers already written up? <br /> <br /> I mean, this is just my opinion and I could be wrong, but it kind of seems like a stretch that they are going to come up with an entire new system of psi powers when one is already there. <br /> <br /> Especially, most especially, when they are going to have (hopefully already did actually) come up with a score or two or more (never can have too many powers) for Superiors. Who are basically Stalwarts and proto-Novas, though without the full blown quantum nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-21-2019, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-20T23:23:16-07:00","id":1326406,"title":"","content":"I don't know what \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion is going to do, though I won't be a bit surprised if it's something along the lines of \u201cpsiads use Aptitudes and Modes as a baseline, but aren't as restricted by them as psions are; as well, there are some psiad-only powers that have been denied to psions due to their one-Aptitude restriction\u201d. <br /> <br /> But for the purpose of TC:Ab, that doesn't matter: what matters is how TC:Ab is going to handle psiads. We'll know <i>that</i> once the relevant part of the manuscript drops in the next couple of weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T00:23:42-07:00","id":1326411,"title":"","content":"With most power rolls now being Q+P what are people\u2019s take on not having scale enhancement with their power use? I\u2019m a bit worried that a person wanting to play heavy with Transmutation will feel a bit stunted. Even if both are at 5 dots ten dice is not that many successes when a complex object is 5 successes to pull off. <br /> I was thinking should create matter be moved from a success to a tag? As well as possibly size scale, and exotic matter? <br /> Also when Transmutation is used can the shape of the object change? So in 1e you can change a brick into a phone or a tree into a computer. Would that just be Transmutation or would you need matter manipulation as well for the shaping? The book does not cover this but could you also just build up successes over several turns? <br /> One of my players is a huge fan of the power idea of transmutation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T00:28:03-07:00","id":1326413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326403#post1326403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it official that the whole Aptitude and Mode system was a Doyn invention and not the actual structured way that a noetic practitioner manifests their powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s something Mateus has got wrong from somewhere. <br /> <br /> Your best bet to get a sense of what Psiads will look like is to take a look at p.61 of the 1e Aberrant Players Guide and extrapolate some things into 2e from there. That section isn\u2019t an accurate depiction of where 2e has gone, but Aptitudes and Modes are still a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T02:28:47-07:00","id":1326423,"title":"","content":"An aside and slightly off-topical, but given Talents run off flux, one wonders if time hopping and world creation stuff from said player's guide might be the domain of the Superior high-end Talents. Otherwise, I get an almost Amberite vibe from what the fluff implies they could do. Seek what you need in Shadow... er... the Continuum.<br /> <br /> (Not to mention, because I'm a sucker for such things, one could surmise a bittersweet happy ending for a 2e version of the Max Mercer/Divis Mal metaplot where they recognize the ways they screwed up and the frenemies reconcile enough for Max to shift Mal over a timeline that ends more nicely, or something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T04:06:49-07:00","id":1326432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326413#post1326413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s something Mateus has got wrong from somewhere. </div> </div> </div> </div>I guess there was a mix of reading and talking about in my memories. But I remember that the way they learn the powers (separating by modes and aptitudes) is artificial, more like subjects in school than real restrictions.<br /> <br /> If it follows closer to Aeon rules, it makes sense as a easier way to learn stuff (like we do in school) by subjects (in game explanation) and as a expansion on Aeon and not the entire continuum (off game explanation).<br /> <br /> But it can still be more flexible about the power they can reach without having to learning other things, for example, a guy can learn to create a energy shield without learning to create a matter shield, or a telepath that never learned how to create a network mind can copy people skills and edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-21-2019, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T04:17:47-07:00","id":1326433,"title":"","content":"I see what you\u2019re saying, but I think you\u2019ve missed the point of your own example by comparing it to school. You don\u2019t learn algebra (say, energy shield, or copying skills) without learning how to add or subtract first (kinetic shield or mind network).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T04:28:22-07:00","id":1326435,"title":"","content":"Canonically, novas with psychic powers exist, they're just one of the following:<ul><li><b>Novas with &quot;psychic powers&quot;</b>: They think they're using psychic powers, but are actually using Mega-Mental predictive Edges, telecommunication, or Mega-Social manipulative Edges.</li> <li><b>&quot;Novas&quot; with psychic powers</b>: They're actually psiads, but no one yet has the knowledge to distinguish them from novas, so they get lumped in.</li> </ul><br /> Even if Project Pandora technically understands that psiads are a different thing, even they'd be hard-pressed to distinguish between the above two groups. Except maybe one of them sets off quantum detectors and the other doesn't. Outside of Pandora, few people know, and few people care. If you have powers, you're a nova.<br /> <br /> (Although imagine if your team got taken captive and outfitted with quantum-nullifying collars, having the actual psychic still able to use her powers would be quite the ace up your sleeve.)<br /> <br /> If you don't like that setup, it's easy enough to do one of the following:<ul><li>Reskin the existing powers. The powers that say you can predict what someone's thinking based on an understanding of their psychology and acute observation of microexpressions? Just pretend it says they're actually reading the target's mind. Done.</li> <li>A lot of psychic powers already exist in Aeon. Just buy them as nova powers instead.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T04:39:11-07:00","id":1326439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326433#post1326433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see what you\u2019re saying, but I think you\u2019ve missed the point of your own example by comparing it to school. You don\u2019t learn algebra (say, energy shield, or copying skills) without learning how to add or subtract first (kinetic shield or mind network).</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s true, and if it\u2019s this way, it makes sense, I personally think that a energy shield and a matter shield are different enough to be learned separated, but I have no powers, don\u2019t know anyone who have, so in setting it can be real.<br /> <br /> I was thinking more about History and Geography, that you can learn about the way the countries changed alone the time form both the people fighting wars side and the geographical distinctions in the region and both makes sense.<br /> <br /> I am deeply curious about the way you guys are dealing with both Psiads and Superiors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T04:44:31-07:00","id":1326441,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t think of it as \u2018matter shield\u2019 and \u2018energy shield\u2019. It\u2019s \u2018kinetic energy shield\u2019 and \u2018other types of energy shield\u2019. You first learn how to stop just one type of energy (kinetic energy, movement), and once you know that you move onto stopping everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T04:59:43-07:00","id":1326448,"title":"","content":"I said it more than once, I am a big fan of Adventure, it\u2019s my favourite game in the Trinity Universe (as it doesn\u2019t exist in TC yet), I like the theme and the low level powers.<br /> <br /> While I like the idea of flexibility, like the way it was in Adventure, I have always made characters with a sequencial powers in mind, for example, there was a power for fire throwing, a power for heat sensing and a power for thermo-shielding, I always think they as a package, and even if it was not obligatory I always made this kind of connection (not just this fire related, but there are a lot of them) when creating the Mesmerists and Stalwarts.<br /> <br /> Now I \u201cwant\u201d something different. There is a voice in my mind saying \u201cyou are a walking contradiction\u201d.<br /> <br /> Thanks for your insights Bunyip!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T05:45:01-07:00","id":1326453,"title":"","content":"You\u2019re welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T05:53:11-07:00","id":1326454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326423#post1326423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An aside and slightly off-topical, but given Talents run off flux, one wonders if time hopping and world creation stuff from said player's guide might be the domain of the Superior high-end Talents. Otherwise, I get an almost Amberite vibe from what the fluff implies they could do. Seek what you need in Shadow... er... the Continuum.<br /> <br /> (Not to mention, because I'm a sucker for such things, one could surmise a bittersweet happy ending for a 2e version of the Max Mercer/Divis Mal metaplot where they recognize the ways they screwed up and the frenemies reconcile enough for Max to shift Mal over a timeline that ends more nicely, or something.)</div> </div> </div> </div>First: the Flux that Talents use and the Flux that Novas suffer are two different things, despite having the same name. Second: in 2e, Superiors aren't high-end Talents (unlike in 1e, where that's precisely what they were intended to be); they're a kind of sub-Nova. If we ever get \u201chigh-end Talents\u201d, they're more likely to be conscious probability manipulators, timeline hoppers, and/or time travelers, not people with enhanced attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T07:03:47-07:00","id":1326458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326454#post1326454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First: the Flux that Talents use and the Flux that Novas suffer are two different things, despite having the same name. Second: in 2e, Superiors aren't high-end Talents (unlike in 1e, where that's precisely what they were intended to be); they're a kind of sub-Nova. If we ever get \u201chigh-end Talents\u201d, they're more likely to be conscious probability manipulators, timeline hoppers, and/or time travelers, not people with enhanced attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, that's... not what the interviews with Steve Kenson have implied, so far; the Polyhedron podcast made it sound like no, it was the same flux being used in different ways.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I don't actually care what they're called: I just mean the ones in Mercer's class, since that's what <i>he</i> was implied to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T07:30:32-07:00","id":1326461,"title":"","content":"After the Healing power description.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Talents Also Have Flux?<br /> Technically the Flux a Talent uses as their Inspiration isn\u2019t quite the same thing as Quantum Flux. In most cases the point is moot, but for the Healing power (and indeed, all of Aberrant), we\u2019re talking specifically about Quantum Flux. </div> </div> </div>But yes, on Polyhedron Ian says it\u2019s possible that we will have the \u201cTier 3 Talent\u201d whatever we may call them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-21-2019, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T09:04:07-07:00","id":1326472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326461#post1326461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After the Healing power description.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But yes, on Polyhedron Ian says it\u2019s possible that we will have the \u201cTier 3 Talent\u201d whatever we may call them.</div> </div> </div> </div>We could just call them Paramorphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T11:39:35-07:00","id":1326499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326435#post1326435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of psychic powers already exist in Aeon. Just buy them as nova powers instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, I backed the Aeon kickstarter with the sole goal in mind of luring Onyx into kickstarting Aberrant. This in turn will leave them no option but to kickstart Adventure!. My insidious plot is working, grim testimony to my overwhelming powers of mass manipulation!&lt;insert maniacal laugh here&gt;<br /> <br /> That aside, this is exactly what I'll be doing at the table, using the Aeon stuff that is. Kind of nice to see the money really was well spent after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24598-shadows-and-dust","name":"Shadows and Dust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T12:14:56-07:00","id":1326504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326472#post1326472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We could just call them Paramorphs.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would rather not.<br /> X-morph tends to refer to the power source. Psychomorphs are psiads, psions, and mesmerists. Eximorphs are Novas, Stalwarts, Superiors(Yes I know they are probably stalwarts) Paramorphs are Talents and????. I would go with a Traveler, or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T12:55:15-07:00","id":1326509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326504#post1326504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would rather not.<br /> X-morph tends to refer to the power source. Psychomorphs are psiads, psions, and mesmerists. Eximorphs are Novas, Stalwarts, Superiors(Yes I know they are probably stalwarts) Paramorphs are Talents and????. I would go with a Traveler, or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, I'm pretty sure Paramorphs are Talents/Mercer, Eximorphs are Stalwarts/Novas, and <i>Psycho</i>morphs are Mesmerists/Psiads.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just reread the thing. I'm tired. Either way, we don't have a better word until they make one up, so why not just call them what they are? Calling them &quot;Travelers&quot; won't have any teeth until that's what the books say. Paramorph is <i>in the books.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","user":"Jetstream","date":". 07-21-2019, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T12:59:23-07:00","id":1326510,"title":"","content":"We can call them Mercers for the lack of something better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T14:04:08-07:00","id":1326523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326509#post1326509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, I'm pretty sure Paramorphs are Talents/Mercer, Eximorphs are Stalwarts/Novas, and <i>Psycho</i>morphs are Mesmerists/Psiads.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just reread the thing. I'm tired. Either way, we don't have a better word until they make one up, so why not just call them what they are? Calling them &quot;Travelers&quot; won't have any teeth until that's what the books say. Paramorph is <i>in the books.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Talents are paramorphs, but the newish splat will be something slightly else. It is tidbit, but I feel rather an important one. Same as stalwarts are not novas, but both are eximorphs. Mercers is good enough for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T14:31:09-07:00","id":1326528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326435#post1326435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canonically, novas with psychic powers exist, they're just one of the following:<ul><li><b>Novas with &amp;quot;psychic powers&amp;quot;</b>: They think they're using psychic powers, but are actually using Mega-Mental predictive Edges, telecommunication, or Mega-Social manipulative Edges.</li> <li><b>&amp;quot;Novas&amp;quot; with psychic powers</b>: They're actually psiads, but no one yet has the knowledge to distinguish them from novas, so they get lumped in.</li> </ul><br /> Even if Project Pandora technically understands that psiads are a different thing, even they'd be hard-pressed to distinguish between the above two groups. Except maybe one of them sets off quantum detectors and the other doesn't. Outside of Pandora, few people know, and few people care. If you have powers, you're a nova.<br /> <br /> (Although imagine if your team got taken captive and outfitted with quantum-nullifying collars, having the actual psychic still able to use her powers would be quite the ace up your sleeve.)<br /> <br /> If you don't like that setup, it's easy enough to do one of the following:<ul><li>Reskin the existing powers. The powers that say you can predict what someone's thinking based on an understanding of their psychology and acute observation of microexpressions? Just pretend it says they're actually reading the target's mind. Done.</li> <li>A lot of psychic powers already exist in Aeon. Just buy them as nova powers instead.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for weighing in on that! It means a lot to me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T14:34:29-07:00","id":1326529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326510#post1326510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can call them Mercers for the lack of something better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not blips? Not a baseline and not psi or nova powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T14:51:24-07:00","id":1326535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326423#post1326423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An aside and slightly off-topical, but given Talents run off flux, one wonders if time hopping and world creation stuff from said player's guide might be the domain of the Superior high-end Talents. Otherwise, I get an almost Amberite vibe from what the fluff implies they could do. Seek what you need in Shadow... er... the Continuum.<br /> <br /> (Not to mention, because I'm a sucker for such things, one could surmise a bittersweet happy ending for a 2e version of the Max Mercer/Divis Mal metaplot where they recognize the ways they screwed up and the frenemies reconcile enough for Max to shift Mal over a timeline that ends more nicely, or something.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Time hopping yes. Universe creation though is more elemental and fits Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T17:30:28-07:00","id":1326562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326535#post1326535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time hopping yes. Universe creation though is more elemental and fits Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>And is implied to be something that novas tend to do when they achieve quantum 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-21T22:57:43-07:00","id":1326622,"title":"","content":"Now that I've had the chance to read a bit more, one thing I think that was really smart was limiting what Mega-Attributes apply to initially, and then using Mega-Edges to expand on them. Getting Scale for every roll of the attribute would be the most cost efficient buy in the game, and a balance nightmare, but giving it in specific areas, and then letting a mega-edge convert that scale into Enhancement here or there etc is great. There might have been an initial shock of &quot;well what did my initial purchase do&quot;, but that was emotional and short-sighted (and I needed to keep reading). It also kinda makes sense if you think you have this raw gift and needing to practice to apply it.<br /> <br /> My only complaint is that there just aren't more Mega-Edges!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T21:33:38-07:00","id":1326872,"title":"","content":"So a bit late to the party here, but there's a fairly interesting change between 1e and 2e I noticed in the manuscripts that I don't think anyone here's mentioned.<br /> <br /> Ceastus Pax is a completely different character now.<br /> <br /> Literally.<br /> <br /> In Aberrant 1e, he was named Shelby Eisenfaust, Erupted in the first year of N-Day, and was your standard Glory Hog Dickbag Superman.<br /> <br /> In Aberrant 2e, his name is Sam Williams and he Erupted <i>forty years</i> prior to N-Day. The two paragraph blurb we got for him is that he Erupted in a car accident and carried around some survivor's guilt for living when his family didn't, particularly as his new powers couldn't save them. He's also got more than a little guilt over sitting on his powers and doing nothing with them, particularly when he was &quot;brought up to believe that power brings responsibility.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> As a change, this is something I definitely approve of. &quot;What if Superman was an asshole?&quot; is a question that's been asked and answered and it's more than a bit tiring to see at this point. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T21:34:58-07:00","id":1326875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1326872#post1326872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a bit late to the party here, but there's a fairly interesting change between 1e and 2e I noticed in the manuscripts that I don't think anyone here's mentioned.<br /> <br /> Ceastus Pax is a completely different character now.<br /> <br /> Literally.<br /> <br /> In Aberrant 1e, he was named Shelby Eisenfaust, Erupted in the first year of N-Day, and was your standard Glory Hog Dickbag Superman.<br /> <br /> In Aberrant 2e, his name is Sam Williams and he Erupted <i>forty years</i> prior to N-Day. The two paragraph blurb we got for him is that he Erupted in a car accident and carried around some survivor's guilt for living when his family didn't, particularly as his new powers couldn't save them. He's also got more than a little guilt over sitting on his powers and doing nothing with them, particularly when he was &quot;brought up to believe that power brings responsibility.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> As a change, this is something I definitely approve of. &quot;What if Superman was an asshole?&quot; is a question that's been asked and answered and it's more than a bit tiring to see at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I don't believe it was ever established when Shelby erupted. I recall it being implied, but never stated, that he was probably a pre-N-day nova. Antaeus too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T22:05:53-07:00","id":1326883,"title":"","content":"Interesting, last week we were talking Pax and the words used wet Glory Hounding Dick, and you call Glory Hog Dickbag. I would use the word Jerk, but it\u2019s interesting how everybody hates him...<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t read much about the new guy, but I hate him... even he looking like a nice guy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T22:07:41-07:00","id":1326885,"title":"","content":"Speaking of those who erupted pre-N-Day do you think, probably in a person non-canon way, that those who were around were boosted by the energies unleashed by that event. That and do you think maybe it was more difficult to increase powers pre-N-day then after. <br /> <br /> From a rules standpoint the idea that say instead of costing 16 XP for Quantum and 12 XP for Mega-Attributes, Mega-Edges, and Quantum Powers lets say it cost 20 XP to raise Quantum and 16 XP for nova abilities, or even more. The second, well first example, is that maybe upon the moment of N-Day those that already existed were given a boost - maybe even something like 75 or 150 XP. <br /> <br /> This isn't asking about canon, which I don't think they would give an answer, just more personal thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T14:36:56-07:00","id":1327072,"title":"","content":"They actually had a bit on this back in 1e. I think it was in the book with Eden? Can't recall but it was official. Anyway it went something like there's a background count in the world. The more Novas you have the higher the count and the easier it is to learn to use Q. Hence, when the Novas left after the war people stopped erupting, yet in places like Eden the process continued.<br /> <br /> So yeah, harder to learn your Q abilities pre N-Day. Also, don't forget the Doyen field around Earth, that was keeping eruptions down and probably skewing the learning curve as well.<br /> <br /> I wonder what would happen if a group got together with Primoris in the 30's and told him that little green men were altering the fate of mankind? &quot;You are NOT prepared!&quot;.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24598-shadows-and-dust","name":"Shadows and Dust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T18:30:44-07:00","id":1327108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadows and Dust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327072#post1327072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They actually had a bit on this back in 1e. I think it was in the book with Eden? Can't recall but it was official. Anyway it went something like there's a background count in the world. The more Novas you have the higher the count and the easier it is to learn to use Q. Hence, when the Novas left after the war people stopped erupting, yet in places like Eden the process continued.<br /> <br /> So yeah, harder to learn your Q abilities pre N-Day. Also, don't forget the Doyen field around Earth, that was keeping eruptions down and probably skewing the learning curve as well.<br /> <br /> I wonder what would happen if a group got together with Primoris in the 30's and told him that little green men were altering the fate of mankind? &amp;quot;You are NOT prepared!&amp;quot;.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Now now, let\u2019s not be insulting. Divis Mal is much more competent than Illidan Stormrage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-23T21:58:17-07:00","id":1327134,"title":"","content":"Okay, going through crafting.<br /> This is some proper ridiculousness.<br /> One dot in megaintellect alows you to be MacGyver. The crafting speed is glorious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T08:54:24-07:00","id":1327191,"title":"","content":"The core already has rules for quickly jury rigging something which works pretty well for being MacGyver. But yeah, I really do like the speed boost here and everything they have for being Mad Scientists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T11:58:17-07:00","id":1327221,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no question - Tony Stark in Aberrant is a Mega-Intelligent Dark Star Nova.<br /> <br /> Bruce Wayne you could make a Dark Star, but does work as a very high XP Talent - especially given the Bigger They Are gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T12:03:19-07:00","id":1327222,"title":"","content":"I could see Tony having say a dot in all Mega-Attributes plus multiple in the mental and social. Plus multiple tech and soxial Mega-Edges. He might even have Digital Manipulation, to represent hus tech savvy nature. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T12:25:12-07:00","id":1327230,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't give Tony any physical Mega-Attributes; he gets those from his Q-Tech. In fact, to me the defining feature of Tony is that he shows just how far you can go with a Quantum rating (defining how potent his tech can be), a single dot in Mega-Intelligence (allowing him to create Q-Tech), and everything else invested into Q-Tech and non-Nova traits: no other Mega-Attributes, no Mega-Edges or Quantum Powers of his own. He is <i>almost</i> a baseline human; but that slight deviation from the baseline allows him to be Iron Man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-24-2019, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T13:21:48-07:00","id":1327243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327230#post1327230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't give Tony any physical Mega-Attributes; he gets those from his Q-Tech. In fact, to me the defining feature of Tony is that he shows just how far you can go with a Quantum rating (defining how potent his tech can be), a single dot in Mega-Intelligence (allowing him to create Q-Tech), and everything else invested into Q-Tech and non-Nova traits: no other Mega-Attributes, no Mega-Edges or Quantum Powers of his own. He is <i>almost</i> a baseline human; but that slight deviation from the baseline allows him to be Iron Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the MCU maybe. But in 616 there\u2019s significant evidence of broader super-genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T14:34:14-07:00","id":1327261,"title":"","content":"Oh? Please elaborate. My own familiarity with Tony Stark (both in the MCU and in 616) has all of his genius being oriented around technology: mostly in terms of the technologies involved in his Armor, but also with such things as some cybernetics and some nanotech. Recall that TC:Ab characters have access to Skill Tricks and Enhanced Edges; it's not like the only options for expressing genius are Mega-Intelligence and Mega-Edges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T14:53:36-07:00","id":1327266,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://scatteredquotes.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/TheAvengers-6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:07:25-07:00","id":1327272,"title":"","content":"Tony don\u2019t need a High Quantum, he can have the MEdges Q-Tech and Technologist on Highest ranks possible.<br /> <br /> I would say something like Q 2, MInt 2, MCun 2 MRes 2, Technologist 2, Q-Tech 9. It gives 220 XP (16 + 24 + 24 + 24 + 24 + 60), he is among the most powerful supers in Marvel, it\u2019s fair amount of XP. With about 11 ranks of Q-Tech and virtually any amount of Novatech and Coretech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:15:33-07:00","id":1327277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327266#post1327266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://scatteredquotes.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/TheAvengers-6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>He had some XP to spend and got an Speciality on Thermonuclear Astrophysics. Maybe a special mega edge that allows to have extra Specialities as he is a super genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:20:26-07:00","id":1327280,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. With that in mind, the MCU Tony might even qualify for several dots of Mega-Intelligence. Maybe an \u201cinstant expert\u201d Mega-Edge (I don't yet have them memorized, but I seem to recall seeing one in TC:Ab). But I don't see him needing much more than that. <br /> <br /> The point, though, was that Mega-Intelligence and Q-Tech covers a <i>lot</i> of ground, and you can have a very successful Nova with \u201cjust\u201d that. Then you get to James Rhodes, who I'd classify as either a baseline or a Talent with access to Nova-Tech: his War Machine armor can't be mass-produced and requires a Nova (Tony) to build it; but it's sufficiently refined from Tony's Iron Man armor that the operator probably doesn't need to be a Nova (or even Inspired).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:24:36-07:00","id":1327283,"title":"","content":"I still think that in Aberrant terms he will have at least one dot in all Mega-Attributes, plus a few knoweldge, social, and technology based Mega-Edges. The nature of what he puts his body through flying that suite to me says some super capability. Additionally, he goes toe to toe with the the Winter Soldier with little more than a guantlet hand, which shows to me some physical capability. He took his company and turned it from a weapons producer to an all around every producer, which showcases to me social and manipulation. He builds an iron man suite in a cave with a pile of scraps, which shows intelligence. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I would not give him a high quantum nor would I give him high mega-stats, minus intelligence, but I do think he has his bases covered. <br /> <br /> Then, when he gets Extremis I would boost his stats up quite a lot, maybe even give him some additional abilities. Though I would add that from an Aberrant perspective all Extremis did was activate his already existing nova potential rather than be the source of his power. <br /> <br /> In some ways I wonder if pre-Extremis one might best write him up as say a Superior (stalwart) and then after that he becomes a full on nova. <br /> <br /> PS. Why yes, I am totally a Tony Stark fanboy. lol<br /> <br /> PPS. The other Avengers are cool as well. <br /> <br /> PPPS. I am TOTALLY a Bucky Barnes/Winter Soldier fanboy too. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T15:26:30-07:00","id":1327284,"title":"","content":"On James Rhodes, I like the idea of him being a Talent, though I also like the idea that Tony built a suite and then used a few points or something to make it &quot;James Rhodes Only&quot; as a feature of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T17:04:22-07:00","id":1327294,"title":"","content":"The TC Scale rules were designed specifically to reflect the cinematic reality that lets things like Tony going up against the Winter Soldier without innate Mega-Strength to happen \u2014 especially since Tony <i>was</i> wielding his armor's gauntlet, which according to the logic of cinematic reality (as opposed to the ruthless logic of realistic physics) should give him access to an least a measure of his armor's Mega-Strength. Ditto with his armor experiments in the first movie: his survival of accidents that realistically should have killed him aren't evidence of Mega-Stamina; they're just good old-fashioned cinematic damage. Extremis potentially changes things; but not as much as one might think. I would argue that it granted him the Mega-Edge that lets you interface directly with machines, a healing factor, and maybe a dot each of Mega-Intelligence and Mega-Cunning (which also would have been his first dot in Mega-Cunning). <br /> <br /> But more importantly, those Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges would arguably be Q-Tech, not Nova powers, where the distinction matters. Tony could have applied the Extremis process to someone else according to the rules given in TC:Ab's Technology chapter, even to a Talent or baseline (though that would have required him to put the effort into shifting it from Q-Tech to Nova Tech, and the baseline would have had to cope with Flux); you can't really do that with Nova powers. <br /> <br /> I'm also a Tony Stark fanboy. But to me, what makes him awesome isn't that he's a \u201cdark star\u201d or \u201cstealth Nova\u201d, but rather it's that he showcases just how much technology can do. In Aberrant terms, what makes him cool is that he has just one (very subtle) superhuman ability (Mega-Intelligence, and <i>maybe</i> one or two related Mega-Edges), but he leverages the heck out of them until he's among the most powerful heroes on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-24-2019, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T17:43:09-07:00","id":1327301,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... This has got me wondering which group is going to be the first to try to turn a Baseline into a Nova artificially. And just how badly the whole project is going to explode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:22:19-07:00","id":1327319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327301#post1327301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm.... This has got me wondering which group is going to be the first to try to turn a Baseline into a Nova artificially. And just how badly the whole project is going to explode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, I could see a Teragen faction making the attempt. You know there has to be at least some Terats who wouldn't mind uplifting the rest of humanity to be like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T18:48:04-07:00","id":1327327,"title":"","content":"That would be where the \u00c6on-era Aberrants come from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T22:11:42-07:00","id":1327356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327261#post1327261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? Please elaborate. My own familiarity with Tony Stark (both in the MCU and in 616) has all of his genius being oriented around technology: mostly in terms of the technologies involved in his Armor, but also with such things as some cybernetics and some nanotech. Recall that TC:Ab characters have access to Skill Tricks and Enhanced Edges; it's not like the only options for expressing genius are Mega-Intelligence and Mega-Edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically my brain went to the period of the comics before the Extremis Arc and Tony being revamped as... Robert Downey Jr.... back when his central shtick was that he was the \u201chard man of hard decisions\u201d (the original Civil War happened in this era). Anyway, a running thing was his probability calculations predicting the future and how (for example) registration was inevitable, and he\u2019d have to spearhead it if he wanted it to take a more benign form than the worst case scenario (the justification the comics used for the horrible things they had him do in Civil War).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T22:32:57-07:00","id":1327358,"title":"","content":"Is that the only time he ever did that? Because if so, I'm willing to put it in the same category as Superman's Super-ventriloquism: a power that was used once for the sake of the plot and has never been seen before or since. <br /> <br /> Frankly, if Tony could accurately predict the future, the Marvel Universe would have developed a lot differently than it did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T22:43:10-07:00","id":1327359,"title":"","content":"It also makes Civil War 2 kinda awkward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-24T23:00:56-07:00","id":1327361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327358#post1327358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that the only time he ever did that? Because if so, I'm willing to put it in the same category as Superman's Super-ventriloquism: a power that was used once for the sake of the plot and has never been seen before or since. <br /> <br /> Frankly, if Tony could accurately predict the future, the Marvel Universe would have developed a lot differently than it did.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was also used as an excuse for shooting Hulk into space.<br /> <br /> Given how that turned out though, maybe it\u2019s bullshit diagetically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T03:09:13-07:00","id":1327375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327327#post1327327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be where the \u00c6on-era Aberrants come from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and, while it hasn't shown up here, in 1e there were powers to make temporary novas out of people or (at higher Quantum) even make it permanent; the metaplot was Divis Mal had been using something like it to help wash the planet in quantum flux and cause more eruptions, wasn't it? Even if it isn't spelled out in the book, it should almost certainly be something that could be done via the tech rules, at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T04:35:06-07:00","id":1327382,"title":"","content":"Yup. That was the main metaplot of why the Galatea exploded. It kickstarted the entire process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T05:10:04-07:00","id":1327387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bioagent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327382#post1327382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. That was the main metaplot of why the Galatea exploded. It kickstarted the entire process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that was the public perception. The explosion was an effect, not the cause, when one of the astronauts onboard erupted from Mal\u2019s energy wave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T05:26:59-07:00","id":1327389,"title":"","content":"hmm, I thought he used that as a Catalyst for the spread of the quantum wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T05:36:19-07:00","id":1327392,"title":"","content":"On 1e there was this discussion, Galetea was the cause or one of the first effects. Now we have the answer for that, it was the first effect.<br /> <br /> Another question related, does Mal Energy wave keeps going or the 150 new novas per year (average) is due to the presence of other novas (as suggested on 1e)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-25-2019, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T08:35:54-07:00","id":1327433,"title":"","content":"There is an Antagonist power in Aeon for the Abbies to make sub-Aberrants, most of the antagonist powers have some counterpart in the Aberrant book, but it is probably something fairly high Quantum/Transcendence so not necessarily something they can do in the early Nova age.<br /> <br /> edit: could you maybe do it with Transformation and some Tags. Probably also something similar to the caveat to Healing where it corrupts the target.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T09:10:32-07:00","id":1327444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327433#post1327433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an Antagonist power in Aeon for the Abbies to make sub-Aberrants, most of the antagonist powers have some counterpart in the Aberrant book, but it is probably something fairly high Quantum/Transcendence so not necessarily something they can do in the early Nova age.<br /> <br /> edit: could you maybe do it with Transformation and some Tags. Probably also something similar to the caveat to Healing where it corrupts the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in 1e the assumption was that the Colony (the one you are talking about) was either Anibal Buendia because of vampiric eufiber mutations or Sin-Eater of the teragen since she could control taint in others.<br /> Turning baselines permanently into novas was Quantum Transformation, a feature of Quantum Supremacy, one of those tier 6 powers that were utterly broken. In fact, that particular power wasn't even fully described thanks to improper positioning of the artwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T09:50:26-07:00","id":1327453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327444#post1327444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, that particular power wasn't even fully described thanks to improper positioning of the artwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good old times when one could not read a book because of artwork...<br /> <br /> Giving mutation is easy, just quantum flux them until it happen, mind control is easy once the target is an aberrant Telecommunication + Mega-Presence + Telepresence, the trick is giving powers to the Sub-Aberrants.<br /> <br /> Maybe bestow power, maybe the powers show up once the SubAberrant has enough flux, I don\u2019t know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T10:10:01-07:00","id":1327458,"title":"","content":"It has been a lot of new rules, and I may be just wrong here, I will admit freely. Could you work with me a scenario when having a qtech item would be better or even equal than just simply buying an equivalent power?<br /> <br /> So, I think I am getting a bit lost on the QTech rules, the ones about making items that emulate quantum powers. Using Quantum Tech needs dots of a mega edge that costs about the same as a Q Power, and the invention needs quantum points commitment just for it to be usable. Also, it takes weeks to deattune tue quantum points, so no extra flexibility here on having a lot of items that you can use as needed. You can use modules on an item, but they are quite expensive and need a lot of qtech dots. It seems like, outside of the quantum part of the (quantum + quantum tech dots), Qtech is made to be very costly, perhaps too much. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-25T10:35:29-07:00","id":1327461,"title":"","content":"The idea of Q-Tech is that the character is not going to get free powers just because it\u2019s not his powers, at least when he is the one that build it.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t see the modules as expensive, it sounds more versatile than anything. They don\u2019t cost extra experience or quantum, just need to fit it in the item, so you can take the extra strong adjust and add a fast moving adjust for a different mission. That was my understanding at least, I didn\u2019t go deep into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T08:46:18-07:00","id":1327587,"title":"","content":"Anyone else miss something to represent old Mega-Appearance? Like Mega-version of the Striking Edge or something. Currently some of the functions of Mega-Appearance have been moved to Mega-Presence, like Immediate Connection and Instant Influence both of which sound like effect that could come from appearance, and Mega-Manipulation, that among other things can give you the mundane Striking Edge. But nothing that actually represent the old Mega-Appearance. Which is kind of a problem when converting 1st ed characters with dot\u2019s in all Mega-Socials since you hit the maximums fast.<br /> <br /> Also it is kinda problem for new characters who would like to look supernaturally gorgeus without looking creepy, which is the function of Inhuman Beauty, since they can get Striking but that literally seems to hit the limit at this point even though it is an Edge available to all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T09:01:00-07:00","id":1327589,"title":"","content":"You have any rules for this convertion in mind? I created a new post for adding rules for 1e conversion, feel free to add any idea there or maybe suggestions of rules to be adapted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1327588-aberrant-1e-conversion\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1327588-aberrant-1e-conversion\"> Aberrant 1e Conversion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1327588-aberrant-1e-conversion\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1327588-aberrant-1e-conversion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hi everybody, I am trying to bring the missing rules from 1e to TC, some as edges some as changes in the Nova rules. Feel free to add all you want (Vampiric </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Already added Node Edge (to be the old Node Background).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T09:39:07-07:00","id":1327594,"title":"","content":"Well I am not yet that confident on my Storypath knowledge for that good homebrew but something on the lines of gaining scale on anything affected by your appearance, Mega-Striking if you will, or since Striking gives you 2 enhancements for things affected by appearance the Mega version could add 4(?) enhancements, and in any case have a prequisite of Striking and stacking with it.<br /> <br /> Have no idea if either of them is balanced or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T09:52:39-07:00","id":1327596,"title":"","content":"Honestly, MApp (as far as I can remember, I will check the book latter) are all covered in MPre and a few MEdges.<br /> <br /> Dreadful Presence would work for the Mega Ugly<br /> <br /> Immediate Connection, Instant Influence and Mass Influence add the &quot;instant overwhelming&quot; from MApp, maybe that's what you are missing, I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T10:04:56-07:00","id":1327599,"title":"","content":"Mega-Presence with the Restricted (-2) tag (only appearance)? That would make the PC gorgeous without making him super-charismatic, scary and whatnot. Good for photo shoots, impressing girls on the beach and so on. Not so much for being a leader of men.<br /> <br /> And if you want both (old-style) Mega-Presence and Mega-Appearance? Just buy Mega-Presence. I think it can be considered both. It's the Force-attribute of the social arena after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T10:49:52-07:00","id":1327611,"title":"","content":"My 1st edition character has Mega-Appearance 4, Mega-Charisma 5 and Mega-Manipulation 3 and I am looking to convert him to 2nd edition. Do I just loose my Mega-App dots? Or should they be divided to Mega-Manipulation and... what? Mega-Composure? So I would max out on Manipulation and gain 2 dots of Mega-Composure?<br /> <br /> I am open for suggestions. Also since Integrity and Composure are new Mega stats no 1st ed character will have them. What dots should be converted to those new attributes? Mega-Wits/Perception will turn to Cunning and perhaps Integrity, sound good? But from what stat would Composure dots come from when converting old characters? Mixture of Charisma/Manipulation divided there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T11:18:04-07:00","id":1327614,"title":"","content":"My opinion about the way they divided the 3 Social Attributes:<br /> Presence is first impact and direct effort, the target do things for you only because you told to. Sargent PS use to give orders, a Models to ask for favours, things like that.<br /> Manipulation is about convincing the target that it\u2019s a good thing. Conman tell people to guide them money because they will get money back, Lawers convince the judge the client is guilt or not.<br /> Composure is about be cool, resist temptations, convince people after long discussions, stubbornness. Guards don\u2019t move after bribes, Leaders hold followers after years of propaganda against them.<br /> <br /> The 3 original ones were scrambled a little and reshaped on the new 3 ones.<br /> Appearance went basically to Presence, as the thing you use to go straight to business in social situations, a little part went to the \u201cCoolness\u201d of Composure and a bit to the idea of distracting people of Manipulation.<br /> Manipulation basically keep it to itself, except for the direct impact that went to Presence and some timing to <br /> Charisma is decided basically among the 3 as it was about talking, listening and appearing interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T11:20:33-07:00","id":1327615,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that MApp also had some shapeshifting Enhancements that let the nova tailor her appearance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T11:22:45-07:00","id":1327617,"title":"","content":"The way you need to divide the 3 mega social to adapt is more about identifying the way you played them and not about the numbers themselves.<br /> As a general rule (and because they are prety close to each other), Inwould make MPre 4, MMan 3 and MCom 5 (maybe MPre 5, MMan 3 and MCom 4)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T11:27:40-07:00","id":1327618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327615#post1327615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that MApp also had some shapeshifting Enhancements that let the nova tailor her appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s the Morph power now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-26T12:17:10-07:00","id":1327628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327618#post1327618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s the Morph power now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morph is more powerful than Appearance Alteration or Copycat in fact it is those two combined. In my case I had Appearance Alteration which allowed me to change details like the color of my wings feathers or such minor modifications but not change who I was, I was always identifiable as myself. So that I could handle with Morph with an added limitation of not being able to use the last two options and so never hide who I am.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T05:27:15-07:00","id":1327722,"title":"","content":"So, something I noticed, and sent feedback on, is in the materials in the Technology chapter. Vitrium is a real life material already, it's a glass biomaterial used in orthopedic implants. Anyone else notice anything similar? I haven't yet read the entire chapter or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-27T19:15:46-07:00","id":1327832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327294#post1327294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The TC Scale rules were designed specifically to reflect the cinematic reality that lets things like Tony going up against the Winter Soldier without innate Mega-Strength to happen \u2014 especially since Tony <i>was</i> wielding his armor's gauntlet, which according to the logic of cinematic reality (as opposed to the ruthless logic of realistic physics) should give him access to an least a measure of his armor's Mega-Strength. Ditto with his armor experiments in the first movie: his survival of accidents that realistically should have killed him aren't evidence of Mega-Stamina; they're just good old-fashioned cinematic damage. Extremis potentially changes things; but not as much as one might think. I would argue that it granted him the Mega-Edge that lets you interface directly with machines, a healing factor, and maybe a dot each of Mega-Intelligence and Mega-Cunning (which also would have been his first dot in Mega-Cunning).<br /> <br /> But more importantly, those Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges would arguably be Q-Tech, not Nova powers, where the distinction matters. Tony could have applied the Extremis process to someone else according to the rules given in TC:Ab's Technology chapter, even to a Talent or baseline (though that would have required him to put the effort into shifting it from Q-Tech to Nova Tech, and the baseline would have had to cope with Flux); you can't really do that with Nova powers.<br /> <br /> I'm also a Tony Stark fanboy. But to me, what makes him awesome isn't that he's a \u201cdark star\u201d or \u201cstealth Nova\u201d, but rather it's that he showcases just how much technology can do. In Aberrant terms, what makes him cool is that he has just one (very subtle) superhuman ability (Mega-Intelligence, and <i>maybe</i> one or two related Mega-Edges), but he leverages the heck out of them until he's among the most powerful heroes on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVE THIS THREAD. I was thinking that MCU Stark - in armors equivalent to what War Machine was wearing in Civil War - shrugged off kinetic collisions far in excess of to what paralyzed Rhodes. Maybe Vision's miss knocked all of his systems (save communications...) off-line but it seems like he just loss flight. My Stark would have at least a dot of Mega-Stamina and some defensive Mega-edges. Not to mention his contributions in rounds 1 and 3 vs Thanos...<br /> <br /> Also, one of my happiest surprises when digging through the manuscripts, my likely happiest finding was that Novas - while way more powerful - weren't just better than everyone at everything. Kind of have a solar Exalted feel now. I was making one of my old fallbacks that I like to create in any new system - a slick gambler and prestidigitator called Johnny Prestige and LO AND BEHOLD he had to use mega-edges to do the things that luck, telekinesis, domination and premonition did last time around. It's made such a more interesting character. Very excited to build some of my old favorites, try a few intellectual property ports (Hola Hancock and Alex Mercer from Prototype) and some setting specific new friends. <br /> <br /> Congrats, so far, OPP team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T06:30:04-07:00","id":1327892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327832#post1327832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I LOVE THIS THREAD. I was thinking that MCU Stark - in armors equivalent to what War Machine was wearing in Civil War - shrugged off kinetic collisions far in excess of to what paralyzed Rhodes. Maybe Vision's miss knocked all of his systems (save communications...) off-line but it seems like he just loss flight. My Stark would have at least a dot of Mega-Stamina and some defensive Mega-edges. Not to mention his contributions in rounds 1 and 3 vs Thanos...</div> </div> </div> </div>I had MCU Iron Man firmly in mind when writing the tech rules. My thinking around the differences between Iron Man and War Machine armor is that Rhodey is a Talent rather than a nova, and Tony has shifted the paradigm between IM 1 and IM 2 to build a nova-tech prototype for Rhodey to take. (Also explains why Hammer can modify elements of it - at least enough to bolt bits and pieces on.)<br /> <br /> As nova-tech and not Q-tech, the War Machine armor is bulkier but not quite as powerful as the Iron Man armor.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: My vision of Stark in Aberrant terms has no powers except stacks of Mega-mental Attributes and all the crafting Mega-Edges. He maybe has a dot in Mega-Stamina, because he survives a lot of stuff outside the armor (especially in IM 3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 07-28-2019, 09:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T07:26:23-07:00","id":1327896,"title":"","content":"Bunyip, as you were the mind behind Tech. Can I buy Q-Tech items with Artefact Edge? Nothing say that you can\u2019t, but nothing say you can.<br /> <br /> Novatech and Core are pretty clear that are possible, also the existence Technologist Mega-Edge suggest that you can have multiple Q-Tech Attuned to you without the Q-Tech Mega-Edge.<br /> <br /> Hope I made my self clear, I rewrote it too many times because I was getting confused by my own text trying to explain reasons for yes and no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T14:11:18-07:00","id":1327963,"title":"","content":"Sorry for being late on this, and apologies if it's already been asked, but I just got a chance to back and have been playing catch up. Am I reading right in that taint is basically gone now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-28T14:14:29-07:00","id":1327964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lionmanguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1327963#post1327963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for being late on this, and apologies if it's already been asked, but I just got a chance to back and have been playing catch up. Am I reading right in that taint is basically gone now?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They just changed the name. Temporary taint is Quantum Flux. Permanent taint is Transcendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T07:06:32-07:00","id":1328275,"title":"","content":"looking at the new preview. Is this a bad joke?<br /> First what I like.<br /> Terattreat is old movement, predating the age, that is cool. This is it, that is the only part I liked.<br /> <br /> Let's start with some more objective flaws.<br /> Proteus operative statline in antagonists is not present.<br /> Future shock paragraphs are from the story guide chapter and not setting secrets,<br /> The theme of sacrifice is not present in the setting secrets, for how big deal it is made to be it is simply not here.<br /> Aberrant war lacks write up, for something presented as inevitable, it has the most boring reason. Good guys fight, the bad guys and world therefore burn. First edition had good and clear reasons for this war, here it just happens.<br /> <br /> Now the slightly more subjective parts.<br /> <br /> Max mercer is now heartless evil moster, who allows the massacre of billions so that his friend can learn a lesson. Truly a man of future and hero of many. The attempt to give him omniscient morality license fails, as all futures are possible, so trying to actually prevent aberrant war is no worse, than to allow and abide it. Only you actually try to save lives, instead of just walking away, Like A true champion of good Aeon society. I thought talents did not pick transcendence.<br /> <br /> Divis mal is non-presence(Yes, I know he was already). he is the impetus but does nothing at all. SO all his write up is kinda worthless, He is eplicitly not a character here. His role of the main author of terat is partially taken by pantheon and has no active role in the events. You can remove him entirely after he .unleashes the age and even manifesto would get published by his followers. He is unimportant to the age. So the lesson excuse makes Mercer even greater monster. <br /> <br /> All the big words, how the Aberrant war is not the future and every other word is about its inevitability. Aberrant war is the true future and if the peasant does not want it, they can invent something else. WE NEVER SEE ANOTHER OPTION, MAKING ABERRANT WAR THE DEFAULT OPTION OF THE SETTING. You could have given write up of different future here. Making another future of humanity part where it would lead to a different result. The even worse result would be preferable to show, over the Aberrant war is the default, we just say loudly it isn't, which the text reeks of. <br /> <br /> One job, one job. Do not make Aberrant war result of nova existence itself, lack of the writ up makes it clear Novas are the true and only reason for the Aberrant war. You who play nova play the inevitable evil monster, that dooms the billions to the death, mercer saw it be so. There is no conflict, no darkness, assholes present their made-up philosophy and thus war happens. Project utopia is a bunch of naive idiots, for trying to prevent it. They fail and never had a chance. Mercer knows, but for the sake of the future, he does not tell.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T07:18:12-07:00","id":1328280,"title":"","content":"I got the same feeling on the last update as you did. It was like &quot;and so?&quot;. No other potential options. No variant thoughts. No super cool revwlations that made me go &quot;oooh&quot;. <br /> <br /> In Aeon we got potentials, we got surprising new character moments. <br /> <br /> Here we learned Scripture was from the 50s but that Divis Mal is basically no longer who he was. And thats it. <br /> <br /> Its definetly not a section that will be used a lot. <br /> <br /> I was hoping for alternate possibilities for future.<br /> <br /> Like how about a variant wbwre humanity and npvas create a society where novas are given a separate and respected but not authoritarian place. <br /> <br /> Or hpw about a variant where novas win the Aberrant War. <br /> <br /> Or how about a variant where Divis Mal acts. <br /> <br /> Optiobs. That is what the setting and secrets chapter should be about. <br /> <br /> Even more its what we got in Aeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-30-2019, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:03:28-07:00","id":1328289,"title":"","content":"While I want a ton of alternate settings and divergent timelines in the future, I don\u2019t think there\u2019s a lot they could have done with the word count here in that regard. It\u2019s not like they wasted word count going step by step through the timeline to Aeon - they just presented what the looming conflicts ARE, which is a reasonable use of the chapter.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s just disappointing if you were hoping for new information as a 1e fan.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d kill for a book on optional conspiracy plotlines to use as a toolkit if you want to make the systems more nefarious but don\u2019t want to use 1e\u2019s dumb sterilization plot. All we got in that regard in the Sao Paulo blast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:05:31-07:00","id":1328290,"title":"","content":"As for Mercer, there is no way to make a guy who founded a club for rich people to go adventuring, and somehow made further fortunes \u201cadventuring\u201d (read: plundering indigenous cultures) not a dick.<br /> <br /> If i\u2019m Misrepresenting that than please someone tell me how the Aeon Society members acquired fortunes adventuring!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:10:39-07:00","id":1328292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328290#post1328290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mercer, there is no way to make a guy who founded a club for rich people to go adventuring, and somehow made further fortunes \u201cadventuring\u201d (read: plundering indigenous cultures) not a dick.<br /> <br /> If i\u2019m Misrepresenting that than please someone tell me how the Aeon Society members acquired fortunes adventuring!</div> </div> </div> </div>The core setting idea of new edition of aberrant was to not make Aeon society evil, they and project utopia were originally the second reason all went to crap, but the aim of this edition was to remove such &quot;conotations&quot; from the gameline. it is kinda Adventure relic, in the other two settings Aeon was rather shady. Aeon are the good guys and always are the good guys. Yes, it is funny how it actually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:20:52-07:00","id":1328295,"title":"","content":"I wanted something like the Fate of Humanity and Posdible Future History section in Aeon, page 363. I figured Aberrant war us one such potential but so are others. Maybe one with Hope and one with Unity. I wanted options! <br /> <br /> What I got was &quot;the aberrant war...&quot; <br /> <br /> This all said it made me realize sometgung my love of Aberrant isnt so much the greater setting. Its certain groups (Aeon, Teragen, Daedalus) and people (Divis Mal) and the potential of power. So in that case I still get what I want. I just ignore tge setting chapter and the future chapter and certain things about Transcendence. <br /> <br /> One thing I do want to do us potentially come up with a potential future for novas foxused on Hope and Unity. Maybe find a way to implement a world society of novas being separate but equal with theur own council and court but getting benefits from helping society. Sonetging like Eden but also mixed with the Second Age of the Wheel of Time and throw in a bit of the First Age of Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:25:39-07:00","id":1328296,"title":"","content":"I will not discuss the need of Aberrant War. It\u2019s THE OFFICIAL TIMELINE, you can divert from it, but don\u2019t expect them to tell you how.<br /> <br /> About Mercer being a jerk for letting billions die, I think he tried and none of the ways he tried solved the problem completely. He is immortal and can time travel, he can do the butterfly effect a few thousand times and it end up with billions dieing.<br /> <br /> For example, if you prefere you can kill Dr Primoris before he becomes Mal and not allow the Aberrant Setting to exist... nice option for Aberrant War too. But some other thing can happen, maybe the lack of Nova presence end up on a Interestellar like effect of global warming, the Doyen became a issue on the same style happens on Bullseye, ending with the kill of every single human instead of a few billions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:38:46-07:00","id":1328300,"title":"","content":"If Divas Mal doesn't unleash his quantum wave, the Doyen shield stays up, for example. That could end up having a much worse effect on humanity than billions dying in the Aberrant War. Delaying the Aberrant War may not give humanity enough time to recover before meeting aliens and lead to the subjugation of the human race. I assume Mercer has chosen the best timeline he could, even if that choice looks monstrous form inside the timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:48:52-07:00","id":1328301,"title":"","content":"The Aberrant War is the official timeline of Aeon, it is not the official timeline for Aberrant or Adventure! The official timeline for Aberrant stops at 2028. The past of the future is set but the future of the past is not. If I am playing an Aberrant game or an Adventure! game then to be told &quot;this is how it all ends&quot; is utterly ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, officially, by numerous statements, that is not how it is. The Aberrant War is not automatically the way that the Nova Age ends. Because the future for Aberrant itself is not written. Because there is no metaplot and future events have to happen in this game is the definition of metaplot.<br /> <br /> All I am asking is that in the Secrets and Setting chapter there be a section on potential futures. One should be the Aberrant War, of course, I am not saying otherwise. BUT there should be others that are given just as much wait - as in a few paragraphs as possibilities. I say the Aberrant War is Sacrifice so why not have something for Hope and something for Unity as potentials.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Funny enough on the whole Mercer is a dick thing, I don't see it. He traveled in time and saw the past, present, and future and many many variants. He probably saw numerous ones where Divis doesn't do N-Day, or where aliens attack early, or the world ends in baseline forged fire. He also saw timelines of light and darkness of weird things and bizaree things, of superheroes in costumes and ones where the government hides them. He came to this one and was like &quot;woah, what do I do, how do I do,&quot; and so just let himself live for the now in some ways. Because he realized he couldn't force or even see what this world itself was going to do. <br /> <br /> Yeah, he is a man at his wits end trying to help but not knowing how. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-30-2019, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:54:16-07:00","id":1328302,"title":"","content":"Note that the much-vaunted \u201cThe Fate of Humanity\u201d section in TC:\u00c6 didn't get into divergent timelines, either: it had \u201cA Possible Future History\u201d \u2014 \u201cspecifically, this is what happens if the characters in your campaign don't alter the course of history.\u201d TC:Ab's \u201cThe Future and the Aberrant War\u201d isn't significantly different in that respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:56:35-07:00","id":1328304,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t mean possible, ideal or obligatory when I say official, I mean the one that leads to the next step as written.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t question your liking, actually I like the results but not being part of the war. What I question is the need of any info on a future that is not the official (the one that leads to the next book of the series).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T08:57:41-07:00","id":1328305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328302#post1328302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the much-vaunted \u201cThe Fate of Humanity\u201d section in TC:\u00c6 didn't get into divergent timelines, either: it had \u201cA Possible Future History\u201d \u2014 \u201cspecifically, this is what happens if the characters in your campaign don't alter the course of history.\u201d TC:Ab's \u201cThe Future and the Aberrant War\u201d isn't significantly different in that respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T09:03:04-07:00","id":1328307,"title":"","content":"So, before I create it, I was wondering if anyone was interested in a thread for the development of potential campaign ideas for Aberrant. Maybe these ideas could start with a premise and them we, as a team, could come up with steps that could lead to them. Steps that would require the players in said campaign to act to bring said steps to fruition. <br /> <br /> I say this, ask this really,because potential campaign ideas is one of those things that I love to develop more. That and I find it more productive then commenting on roughly the same thing again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T09:04:04-07:00","id":1328308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328301#post1328301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, he is a man at his wits end trying to help but not knowing how.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is old Mercer, this one is doing it to teach Divis mal a lesson<br /> Problem is, that by not having an alternate timeline, it drives home the point of the inevitability of the Aberrant war, something they wanted to showcase is not the case, the book just utterly fails at it. It just guts the actual conflict of the first edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T09:23:58-07:00","id":1328311,"title":"","content":"In a different note, I'm mildly disappointed with the \u201cPsi Modes\u201d box. I'm not surprised by it, mind you; and I do understand where they're coming from. But I do wish it had elaborated a bit further on <i>how</i> psiads \u201caren't the same as novas, but you can use these mechanics if you don't have access to <b>\u00c6on</b> or prefer to keep the rules consistent with <b>Aberrant</b>\u201d. Oh well; if nothing else, there's always the Storypath Nexus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T09:28:40-07:00","id":1328313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328307#post1328307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, before I create it, I was wondering if anyone was interested in a thread for the development of potential campaign ideas for Aberrant. Maybe these ideas could start with a premise and them we, as a team, could come up with steps that could lead to them. Steps that would require the players in said campaign to act to bring said steps to fruition. <br /> <br /> I say this, ask this really,because potential campaign ideas is one of those things that I love to develop more. That and I find it more productive then commenting on roughly the same thing again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea. In the end, with no Aberrant War, the setting will be space exploration and fighting aliens, but in the middle there are several stories to be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T10:09:06-07:00","id":1328322,"title":"","content":"Oh God! This is gonna be a long one. feel free to skip.<br /> <br /> <br /> For people who are on this board I guess the last update was a bit lackluster. But that is because we are mostly aware of that stuff already, so nothing new. <br /> <br /> For someone who IS new to the game though, those bits are required. Write-ups of mooks are perhaps not required by veterans, but if you are starting out, getting a feel of the 'Power level' of ordinary to elite baselines (and beyond) are rather important I think.<br /> <br /> What DID suprise me is how drasticly stuff like the drug mite enhances baselines. Several dots of Mega-attributes? Again, I think I misunderstood the super-science rules, aren't nova-tech only able to give max one dot of any one super-ability?<br /> <br /> <br /> As for ALL of the previews?<br /> <br /> <br /> THINGS I MISSED<br /> * Examples of nova-tech in practical society. Has armor tech advanced with eufiber and novastolo? Has weapons tech? Or have they cancelled each other out? What about those anti-power-shackles? Rules for nova-tech drugs and medicines (I especially missed stuff like mox).<br /> * Several of the Teragen has bio-manipulation-powers of some sort. But they don't seem to exist in the rules. Or do they? Examples of re-skinning powers to create something not straightforward would be nice.<br /> * And dear God! Super-science examples. From inception to creation. Let us see the process. What are the things you need to buy with XP, and how much? How do the pre-requisites change? (A rank 9 Q-tech item needs science 9?) How was Mite created? How does it work? And how was it 'down-graded' to nova-tech?<br /> <br /> <br /> THINGS I MISSED (but might be better in a Players Guide?)<br /> * How big is a hyperfusion engine? Do cars have them or do they have batteries <i>powered </i>by hyperfusion? Can a baseline carry one around? Is it expensive to buy and own?<br /> * What is <i>left</i>? If you are super-intelligent, what do you do? The climate is saved. There is super-cheap energy. HIV/cancer is gone. Aeon/Utopia seems to be sponsoring industri and cheap housing everywhere. Even today hunger is more a socio-political problem rather than 'we are running out of capacity to grow food&quot;. The world seems saved pre-game. What challenges are left for the super-smarties (and how do they produce story hooks)?<br /> * What is it like to be a nova? In the original rules you got a 'stream-lined physiology' where you got some bonus dots, required extra food, low body-fat (quite trim) and some every-day quirks like how alcohol was not very effective now. Is this still a thing? Shooting energy bolts is quite noticeable, but are there small differences common to ALL novas?<br /> <br /> <br /> ODDITIES<br /> * Nova numbers seem to be a quarter of what they were in the previous edition? Changed things a bit. Now any individual nova are more important and noticeable. It's harder to get lost in the 'nova crowd'. Organisations are smaller unless bolstered by more baselines. Is the Amp Room still only open to novas? Might be small crowd, more a country club than an actual party place.<br /> * Longevity/immortality seems rare now, especially compared to psions (for whom it comes easy, or so the boards claim). Clashes a bit with story/fluff since every 'pre-N-day Nova' seems not to age (much, if any). Also, the Mega-edge slow aging at one dot does nothing (not intended I don't think).<br /> <br /> <br /> THINGS I REALLY LIKED<br /> * The underlying storypath system. It really cuts down on huge amounts of dice. Enhancements and dramatic scale makes things simpler and you get a better 'feel' for it.<br /> * The more positive tone. You can actually work for Utopia now, and not feel like you are stabbing the world and the future in the back because you are 90's grimdark stupid (old Proteus).<br /> <br /> <br /> THINGS I <i>DIDN'T</i> LIKE<br /> * Not enough clarity in the rules sometimes. This is a thing in development though, so rather natural. It seems to be a bit 'fluff and shorthand' in places. I'm looking at you, 'Instant Expert', which I interpreted to be valid for pretty much _any_ action, but was corrected that it only applies the FIRST time you do any TYPE of action (so, only the first time you try to pick a lock, not the second time you try to pick a lock). That's quite a difference in utility. This might entirely be me though, english isn't my first language. Most of it reads cleanly though, especially Quantum Powers. As I've mentioned before, super-science is what I find hardest to wrap my head around.<br /> Narrative scale is the most notorius culprit in this though. There seems to be underlying assumptions from the &quot;Story-path explained&quot; document that has not been included at all in the actual books? Narrative scale multiplier seems to have been omitted and it seems to have warped into two different systems behind the scenes. I think I've seen it on the boards as &quot;multiply with (difference in scale)+1&quot; yet sometimes (like in the Quantum Agent power) it alludes to the old &quot;2,5,10,100, etc&quot; multiplier. Well, probably a development artefact, or perhaps both scales are in play but used in different instances (like, 'success-multiplier' and 'numerical multiplier')? I'm far from the only one who have mentioned it. I understand you aim for a 'cinematic take' where rules should be a bit 'hand-wavey' and flexible, but without a solid, well-explained frame-work I actually find it <i>more </i>difficult to use narrative scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> typo-inspired name for eufiber batteries: Betteries.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1226-gammelbraxen","name":"Gammelbraxen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:17:56-07:00","id":1328331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gammelbraxen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328322#post1328322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For someone who IS new to the game though, those bits are required. Write-ups of mooks are perhaps not required by veterans, but if you are starting out, getting a feel of the 'Power level' of ordinary to elite baselines (and beyond) are rather important I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone new to the game - yes, these sections are super important. That said, this section was still a little lack lustre. I was hoping for the opposing Novas to see something more detailed than Cloak 2 (Sonic) and some Mega Attributes. I was hoping for an example of how Techniques work and some more creative use of the power creation system to back up the lack of examples there. I do suppose the NPC book stretch goal -should- cover this but its a real shame its not in the core book. I just hope we get an Aberrant AbExpansion like how Aeon is getting one that can cover these missing bits. <br /> <br /> STILL<br /> <br /> I am overall very happy with Aberrant. Bumped my pledge up to the physical copy edition instead of just the PDF in the last 10 minutes. Storypath is really quickly becoming one of my favourites and seeing how Aberrant uses it for another genre - good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:25:04-07:00","id":1328334,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m hoping the Proteus Dossier on Nova npcs doubles as an implicit \u201chere is how to build this power set with the rules\u201d book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:30:15-07:00","id":1328335,"title":"","content":"It really needs to. Like the comic that has been published with.... err Swamp Thing in it (Sorry I forgot his name!) I have little idea how to make at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Find my Homebrew so far here: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18X_mkFwDcM0sSN9R2GoQ72Q5FqW1deFgEM3HIGneABQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> So far its Demon Merits, Vampire 1e to 2e ports and a Knowledge collection mechanic for the Ordo Dracul!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24597-lordofiron","name":"LordofIron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24597_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:32:40-07:00","id":1328336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328334#post1328334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m hoping the Proteus Dossier on Nova npcs doubles as an implicit \u201chere is how to build this power set with the rules\u201d book.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it does, If like to see it include one or two psiads in the Dossier: say, a telepath and a precog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:38:18-07:00","id":1328339,"title":"","content":"I honestly believe that in a year or two we will be looking back at this point and be all &quot;Oh wow remember when we didn't know how to make anything!&quot; and then we laugh as we use the very open rules to basically make anything we want. <br /> <br /> Though I think that will happen today is not that day. (Epic Aragorn speech) <br /> <br /> So yeah can I third the whole need for examples, many many examples, for how the powers work. <br /> <br /> As a random thing, I like how regular character stats are shortened and given only the most necessary but that powers are written out the way they need to be. I say this because I plan on using the Proteus Compendium as a sort of power loot system. hehe<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Oh, as a random note, I just realized that the whole adventure book we funded was exapnded to include some storyteller info and such. So cool. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> PS. ADVENTURE! is coming. As in it was announced. Which is sooooooooo cooooooool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:49:16-07:00","id":1328341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328336#post1328336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it does, If like to see it include one or two psiads in the Dossier: say, a telepath and a precog.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean for people without Aeon? Because there\u2019s much less ambiguity about those mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:53:56-07:00","id":1328342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328341#post1328341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean for people without Aeon? Because there\u2019s much less ambiguity about those mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I mean for people without \u00c6on. Specifically, the psiad entries would serve as TC:Ab's version of the Psiad rules found in the 1e Aberrant Player's Guide (excepting the \u201cPsiads in Trinity\u201d box, which is getting its TC upgrade in \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T11:57:05-07:00","id":1328344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328342#post1328342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I mean for people without \u00c6on. Specifically, the psiad entries would serve as TC:Ab's version of the Psiad rules found in the 1e Aberrant Player's Guide (excepting the \u201cPsiads in Trinity\u201d box, which is getting its TC upgrade in \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is rather funny. he rules for secondary splat in the book, will be in the supplement for another splat book and different setting and you can bet there will not be anything tying it to Aberrant, while psiads are rather significant force here and if you play team tomorrow in the spec ops setting you work for one, but there are no rules for them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T12:25:42-07:00","id":1328350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328290#post1328290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mercer, there is no way to make a guy who founded a club for rich people to go adventuring, and somehow made further fortunes \u201cadventuring\u201d (read: plundering indigenous cultures) not a dick.<br /> <br /> If i\u2019m Misrepresenting that than please someone tell me how the Aeon Society members acquired fortunes adventuring!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly a take, and I'm not sure where you got any of this.<br /> <br /> Going by their 1e Adventure! bios:<br /> <br /> Mercer's parents were wealthy. While they were anthropologists, and thus visited many exotic locales with the young Max, it's specifically stated their wealth came from investments. Max attended Harvard and got two PhDs in as many years. As his parents aged, he managed their fortune, and invested in several museums. He apparently managed that money quite well: the fiction on page 3 says &quot;He\u2019d made a sheik's fortune 11 or 12 times over in his young life from radical new mechanical patents and stock market wizardry and, each time, had given it away, wholly or in increments - to charities, trusts and reform societies.&quot; Page 23 has Whitley writing about Max &quot;sketching up a new two-way radio device for Professor Dixon to perfect&quot;. It's likely those mechanical patents are the source of a lot of the Aeon Society's continuing income.<br /> <br /> The only thing we know about Donighal's past is that his father was a teacher. Perhaps the elder Donighal was a teacher at Harvard, and that's how Michael met Mercer. A Harvard professor probably made a decent enough income.<br /> <br /> None of the rest of the core Society are presented as particularly wealthy, or having &quot;acquired fortunes.&quot; Annabelle Lee Newfield was a tobacco-spitting 16 year old girl when she signed up. Whitley Styles is heir to a big company, but the company's co-owner is blocking him from taking his legacy. Prof Dixon might be making money on his inventions, but he spends it all on the hooch. It's likely that Mercer pays for their living expenses as a salary for being part of the Society. Despite the implications of the name, the &quot;Aeon Society for Gentlemen&quot; was never a club for rich people to go adventuring. It's a society for people with the will and ability to change the world for the better.<br /> <br /> I can certainly see the argument for Jack Tallon having plundered indigenous cultures in his pre-Aeon life as an adventurer, but he's notably Aeon's oldest member and is increasingly obsolete, and again is never really portrayed as having acquired a fortune in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 07-30-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T12:31:14-07:00","id":1328352,"title":"","content":"That's a really awesome historical and background set up. Very cool. I like the nature of them and how things grew. I also like that bit more then them being a super plunderer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T12:31:33-07:00","id":1328353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328308#post1328308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is old Mercer, this one is doing it to teach Divis mal a lesson<br /> Problem is, that by not having an alternate timeline, it drives home the point of the inevitability of the Aberrant war, something they wanted to showcase is not the case, the book just utterly fails at it. It just guts the actual conflict of the first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh-huh. I bet the official timeline in the back of Aeon does too.<br /> <br /> Wait. Wait, it says here that a fundamental truth about time travel is that the future is always in flux and that the Aberrant War is simply likely. It even outlines advice on how to stop the radicalization of the Teragen and Geryon's attack.<br /> <br /> What the hell? This criticism makes no sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T12:49:02-07:00","id":1328358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328353#post1328353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Uh-huh. I bet the official timeline in the back of Aeon does too.<br /> <br /> Wait. Wait, it says here that a fundamental truth about time travel is that the future is always in flux and that the Aberrant War is simply likely. It even outlines advice on how to stop the radicalization of the Teragen and Geryon's attack.<br /> <br /> What the hell? This criticism makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>With note. It might make it even worse- that is opposite of endorsement. It is always like that, you can change it, but it might not work. It states in the previous sentence, that even de-escalating here is unlikely to stop the problem. It provides no way to deredacalize terragen. It provides opposite. There is no way to do so, as it is multiple parties playing the game, without anyone having any control. You cannot deescalate this well and the book does not provide ways to do so. Divis mal wi not act and pantheon lack the power to actually do so, not to mention, that it goes directly against philosophy of one race.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mercer: Exactly future is in flux, by not acting against Aberrant war Mercer is condoning it. He plays a light hand allowing millions to die to teach Divis Mal a lesson. It is the most likely scenario like it was said many times in the book. Mercer expects it to happen and yet does explicitly not act against it allow events to play out in the greatest mass slaughter in the history of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T12:49:16-07:00","id":1328359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328350#post1328350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's certainly a take, and I'm not sure where you got any of this..</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aeon history writeup in the 2e Barrrant text that says they made fortunes \u201cadventuring\u201d.<br /> <br /> As there is no way to do that without taking it from someone else I drew the natural conclusion based on historic equivalent adventurers. As I keep asking, no one can give me any other way by which one can make a fortune \u201cadventuring\u201d.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s great that in 1e Mercer built his fortune via invention, but I was going off what the 2e Aberrant text said about the Aeon Society\u2019s history.<br /> <br /> Edit: ok, rereading the text it says \u201cfortunes they had made during their adventures\u201d, so I guess one can argue that just means it happened concurrently, not that they made it FROM their adventures, but that feels like a technical dodge away from the what the sentence naturally suggests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-30-2019, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T13:02:29-07:00","id":1328363,"title":"","content":"We could really use 2e mechanics for mox and adrenocilin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T13:12:03-07:00","id":1328365,"title":"","content":"Why would the writing be written to dodge anything? The text says what it intends to say pretty clearly: the Aeon members, in a variety of ways and for a variety of reasons, made fortunes during their adventures. If your read is that they are all plunderers, that's your interpretation and the text allows it, but it doesn't specify that your interpretation is the correct one. Since Ian relayed the 1e examples, and we've been pretty clear that we're not looking to &quot;darken&quot; the main three Trinity Continuum game lines, the implication is that plundering colonialists is not the way we're going to go. But, of course, it hasn't been written yet, so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T13:36:23-07:00","id":1328371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328365#post1328365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the writing be written to dodge anything? The text says what it intends to say pretty clearly: the Aeon members, in a variety of ways and for a variety of reasons, made fortunes during their adventures. If your read is that they are all plunderers, that's your interpretation and the text allows it, but it doesn't specify that your interpretation is the correct one. Since Ian relayed the 1e examples, and we've been pretty clear that we're not looking to &quot;darken&quot; the main three Trinity Continuum game lines, the implication is that plundering colonialists is not the way we're going to go. But, of course, it hasn't been written yet, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: Are there still no plans on alternate timeline books?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:04:48-07:00","id":1328374,"title":"","content":"Interesting....<br /> <br /> Teragen are now specifically the creation of Mal rather than the co-opted overgrown brainchild of Mathematician and Orzaiz.<br /> <br /> Apparently nobody trusts Gabriel...prolly all the de-christianization going around.<br /> <br /> So... Proxy Bhurano created QK herself then? That's actually better than more Doyen meddling. (I swear &quot;doyen&quot; must be space-speak for &quot;galactic dickhead&quot;)<br /> <br /> I assume all the additional emphasis on Psiads is the result fo Mal's secondary hammersmith event not being nova-specific?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:21:32-07:00","id":1328379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328371#post1328371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Question: Are there still no plans on alternate timeline books?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you define what you mean by alternate timeline books? This is the Trinity Continuum after all, so that term might have several meanings. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:25:10-07:00","id":1328381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328365#post1328365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the writing be written to dodge anything? The text says what it intends to say pretty clearly: the Aeon members, in a variety of ways and for a variety of reasons, made fortunes during their adventures. If your read is that they are all plunderers, that's your interpretation and the text allows it, but it doesn't specify that your interpretation is the correct one. Since Ian relayed the 1e examples, and we've been pretty clear that we're not looking to &amp;quot;darken&amp;quot; the main three Trinity Continuum game lines, the implication is that plundering colonialists is not the way we're going to go. But, of course, it hasn't been written yet, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, if I can clarify what I meant - I didn\u2019t mean to suggest the author of the line was intending that the Aeon members made their fortunes through plunder and was trying to cover it up, What I meant was that that was the implication, however unintentionally, of connecting adventuring to making a fortune, and while it could be read as \u201cby doing unrelated things like invention or entertainment contemporaneously to their adventuring,\u201d that was not a natural way to read the sentence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:28:53-07:00","id":1328382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zorb42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328358#post1328358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With note. It might make it even worse- that is opposite of endorsement. It is always like that, you can change it, but it might not work. It states in the previous sentence, that even de-escalating here is unlikely to stop the problem. It provides no way to deredacalize terragen. It provides opposite. There is no way to do so, as it is multiple parties playing the game, without anyone having any control. You cannot deescalate this well and the book does not provide ways to do so. Divis mal wi not act and pantheon lack the power to actually do so, not to mention, that it goes directly against philosophy of one race.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mercer: Exactly future is in flux, by not acting against Aberrant war Mercer is condoning it. He plays a light hand allowing millions to die to teach Divis Mal a lesson. It is the most likely scenario like it was said many times in the book. Mercer expects it to happen and yet does explicitly not act against it allow events to play out in the greatest mass slaughter in the history of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, your issue is that Storytellers may be dicks and refuse to acknowledge that the core premise of the timeline is &quot;here is the default, these is ways you can make a storyhook out of it, and no, Divis Mal is not going to do it because he's not the good guy.&quot;<br /> <br /> I read something about how horrible it was in Aeon that the Doyen were as powerful as psychic gods should be and if they wanted to, they could become nearly impossible to fight if they got directly involved. Everyone in that thread pointed out that was wrong too, because the Doyen are explicitly cowards who want to <i>avoid </i>that kind of confrontation, and if the ST is making it so they they're possessing everyone, there's a bigger and more immediate problem than a Doyen having final boss stats. This is a problem with the ST not wanting their players to have a positive impact, not the book - and to be frank, the Teragen is an organization that, if it refuses to radicalize and embrace the fascistic underpinnings of the whole One Race thing, is the kind of thing that will expel a group that is really pissed off that they won't, and make their own team. With blackjack and hookers. Cue the Teragen as a whole becoming good guys to stomp out their crazed splinter.<br /> <br /> That thing about Mercer has more merit, but I read that as &quot;he has no idea what to do and thinks humanity will be able to handle this on its own.&quot; Which is to say, he's a later-chronicle patron who feeds the players info after it becomes clear they have a major shot at averting or taming the Aberrant War. He's not perfect, but he is kind of a person who strikes me as fundamentally hands-off and reluctant to push his luck, even if that's the better option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:31:07-07:00","id":1328383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328379#post1328379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you define what you mean by alternate timeline books? This is the Trinity Continuum after all, so that term might have several meanings. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>The book about the thing, that did not happen in canon timeline and aberrant secrets does indeed prove you have one in the continuum after all. For example, setting, where aberrant war dos not happen, setting where psiads are main splat instead os something else. Aberrants atake over humanity and so on. Alternate events hapenning ad shaping the world. You know actually showing the continuum, instead of just talking about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6491-zorb42","name":"zorb42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T14:44:31-07:00","id":1328388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328379#post1328379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you define what you mean by alternate timeline books? This is the Trinity Continuum after all, so that term might have several meanings. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm looking for two things in this regard:<br /> <br /> 1. A \u201ccross-time\u201d setting book featuring protagonists who can and do travel to the past, future, and alternate timelines. This should get into the implications of time travel, such as whether timelines can ever be changed (as opposed to even the slightest variation splintering off a new branch) and if so how. <br /> <br /> 2. Setting books that are <i>not</i> set in the Adventure-to-\u00c6on timeline: alternate futures for TC:Ad and/or TC:Ab, for instance. The unnamed setting in TC is one example of this sort of thing: it's basically an alternate future of TC:Ad where N-Day didn't happen. <br /> <br /> Basically, the premise of TC is that time isn't linear; it has branches. The question is whether you are going to be actively supporting that notion, or if it's mostly going to be relegated to background color.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T15:04:36-07:00","id":1328389,"title":"","content":"On alternate timeline stuff I would like <br /> <br /> 1. Alternate ways for Adventure! or Aberrant could end. Alternately, what if we switch where Hope, Sacrifice, and Unity lay so that maybe Adventure! is Unity and Aberrant is Hope and Aeon is Sacrifice. To me this showcases its all a continuum and not a straight line from one to another. <br /> <br /> 2. The when of power appearance. So maybe the Adventure! era is about Psions or Novas and the Aberrant era sees the Inspired or Psions and the Aeon era is about Inspired or Novas. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T16:25:03-07:00","id":1328397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328388#post1328388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I'm looking for two things in this regard:<br /> <br /> 1. A \u201ccross-time\u201d setting book featuring protagonists who can and do travel to the past, future, and alternate timelines. This should get into the implications of time travel, such as whether timelines can ever be changed (as opposed to even the slightest variation splintering off a new branch) and if so how.<br /> <br /> 2. Setting books that are <i>not</i> set in the Adventure-to-\u00c6on timeline: alternate futures for TC:Ad and/or TC:Ab, for instance. The unnamed setting in TC is one example of this sort of thing: it's basically an alternate future of TC:Ad where N-Day didn't happen.<br /> <br /> Basically, the premise of TC is that time isn't linear; it has branches. The question is whether you are going to be actively supporting that notion, or if it's mostly going to be relegated to background color.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not branches so much as overlapping parallel timelines that can move closer to and even overlap other lines. But for our purposes, anything that works for you to have fun with it is a good metaphor. The Adventure! =&gt; Core =&gt; Aberrant =&gt; Aeon set are four timelines that are close together or even overlapping as much as works for you. Each of those will have parts to their setting that we describe but then don't describe again in the other ones - those parts may not overlap or we may just not have mentioned them. Either way, you get to choose if they exist as you play. I like to use the Hidden Gorilla Civilization pulp trope as something that I think belongs in Adventure!, but we clearly haven't included in Core or the others. What happened to it? It's no longer in synch with those other timelines we're publishing, but could be rediscovered.<br /> <br /> #1 is something both Ian and I have touched on a few times in our bigger Continuum discussions. We'd like to do something with it, but time travel has always been a tough one to get right in TTRPGing. #2 is a different subject as those are effectively doing What If books for books we already did, and right now we're focusing more on slices of the Continuum along a timeline as the next books we're doing. I'm not sure right now if What If books should be something we do, or are prime material for the Storypath Nexus Community Content site.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T16:27:12-07:00","id":1328398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328389#post1328389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On alternate timeline stuff I would like<br /> <br /> 1. Alternate ways for Adventure! or Aberrant could end. Alternately, what if we switch where Hope, Sacrifice, and Unity lay so that maybe Adventure! is Unity and Aberrant is Hope and Aeon is Sacrifice. To me this showcases its all a continuum and not a straight line from one to another.<br /> <br /> 2. The when of power appearance. So maybe the Adventure! era is about Psions or Novas and the Aberrant era sees the Inspired or Psions and the Aeon era is about Inspired or Novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>All cool ideas. Check out my response to the What If kind of concepts like those that do a different spin on the established eras. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T17:01:42-07:00","id":1328403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328397#post1328397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe not branches so much as overlapping parallel timelines that can move closer to and even overlap other lines. But for our purposes, anything that works for you to have fun with it is a good metaphor. The Adventure! =&gt; Core =&gt; Aberrant =&gt; Aeon set are four timelines that are close together or even overlapping as much as works for you. Each of those will have parts to their setting that we describe but then don't describe again in the other ones - those parts may not overlap or we may just not have mentioned them. Either way, you get to choose if they exist as you play. I like to use the Hidden Gorilla Civilization pulp trope as something that I think belongs in Adventure!, but we clearly haven't included in Core or the others. What happened to it? It's no longer in synch with those other timelines we're publishing, but could be rediscovered.<br /> <br /> #1 is something both Ian and I have touched on a few times in our bigger Continuum discussions. We'd like to do something with it, but time travel has always been a tough one to get right in TTRPGing. #2 is a different subject as those are effectively doing What If books for books we already did, and right now we're focusing more on slices of the Continuum along a timeline as the next books we're doing. I'm not sure right now if What If books should be something we do, or are prime material for the Storypath Nexus Community Content site.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a suggestion, but you could introduce the concept in a setting book on divergent timeline exploration, and then open up Storypath to such settings having kicked it off yourself.<br /> <br /> I know i\u2019d love to play with a post-apocalyptic setting, not to mention my alternate history for Psions in the Edwardian period.<br /> <br /> Also on the idea of setting stuff appropriate for Adventure! that then becomes out of sync with the Aberrant-Aeon timeline - I\u2019d LOVE to see (or write for the Nexus if it\u2019s an option) a Planetary Romance setting expansion, complete with Martian princesses, Venetian jungles, etc etc!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T17:01:48-07:00","id":1328404,"title":"","content":"I think Rich have a great point on \u201cI'm not sure right now if What If books should be something we do, or are prime material for the Storypath Nexus Community Content site\u201d<br /> <br /> I mean, they have great writers and game designers, but they cost money and take time. Our community have lots of great ideas and we can add lots of good books for the missing points in timeline, alternative timelines and those missing things we want in the book but word counting took them away.<br /> <br /> Said that, I would love a Aexpansion-ish book for Aberrant:<br /> - Some about the core-tech (or even Baseline tech) used by people in 2028 (like those in Elites 1e book)<br /> - Some about Powers used by Novas and Aberrants during Aeon era, like the capacity of creating subaberrants<br /> - Some about Pre-N-Day eruptions and how powerful they got.<br /> <br /> PS: Thanks for start working on Adventure! It\u2019s my favorite era! Keep us updated... as much as possible... please!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T17:04:56-07:00","id":1328405,"title":"","content":"Kind of in Mercer's defense here. Yeah he knows the Aberrant War is going to happen, but since he read the Aeon Secrets chapter he also knows that in a few hundred years the Doyen are defeated by a coalition of psions, novas, quin, and those primitive aliens whose name escapes me at the moment. If he stops the Abby war does this magic moment come to pass? No telling, things could be better, or maybe a whole lot worse. We got a happy ending coming, don't rock the boat, sounds like a smart play for humanity as a whole.<br /> <br /> That said, there were hints, from 1e Adventure! I think, about the Aeon society altering things. They changed &quot;something&quot;, and we got Adolph and WW2 because of it. With that in mind I can see him being reluctant to keep monkeying with Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24598-shadows-and-dust","name":"Shadows and Dust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T17:18:57-07:00","id":1328408,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, this is one reason why I'd like a \u201ctime travelers\u201d setting: it's easy to criticize Mercer when you're not in his shoes; but if you have the opportunity to do the sorts of things he can do and see just how messy it can get\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T17:22:54-07:00","id":1328410,"title":"","content":"Oh hey random aside on the Onyx Path Twitch site there is a video with Travis Legge and Eddy Webb called Trinity Continuum Q&amp;A with Eddy Webb that might be interesting for those here to watch. I would link it but I'm not at a location where I can access twich at the same time as I post this message.<br /> <br /> Its actually quite interesting so far.<br /> <br /> As a note I LOVE these things. To hear the developers, producers, writers talk about things. Discuss things. Reveal things. Its so fantastic. <br /> <br /> It also causes the release of worry. Like &quot;I am not sure about x&quot; and then in these videos they talk about x, or even they talk about y but its close enoyguh, and all worry fades. <br /> <br /> Basically, if its possible, more of these developer interviews would be awesome. Both from a mechanical perspective and a setting perspective. <br /> <br /> Example, in the video Eddy Webb talks about how he asks Ian stuff and Ian is all like &quot;yeah, but ...&quot; I would LOVE to hear as much as possible as can be shared. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 07-30-2019, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T18:50:40-07:00","id":1328422,"title":"","content":"So I just realized the fact that as the requisites for a Mega-Attribute is the Attribute and Quantum equal to the Mega-Attribute. Which means you could have a character with Intellect 1 and Mega-Intellect 1 and Quantum 1. Basically speaking he is dumb but super intelligent at the same time. This is quite interesting to me. I wouldn't use it for a player character, but it is quite interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T19:44:59-07:00","id":1328434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1328422#post1328422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I just realized the fact that as the requisites for a Mega-Attribute is the Attribute and Quantum equal to the Mega-Attribute. Which means you could have a character with Intellect 1 and Mega-Intellect 1 and Quantum 1. Basically speaking he is dumb but super intelligent at the same time. This is quite interesting to me. I wouldn't use it for a player character, but it is quite interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it as being a bit like the protagonist of Flowers for Algernon. They're intelligent, but they don't have experience in using that intellgence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-30T19:57:32-07:00","id":1328438,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was because I had just watched an episode of Legends of Tomorrow where they had to zip back and forth futilely attempting to keep something from happening in history, but I read the part about Max &quot;allowing&quot; Mal's experiment, and by extension the Aberrant War, being more about him resigning to a particular series of events. He also might not necessarily know this timeline will end up with the Aberrant war, but he knows he can't stop Mal from trying, so he is just letting it play out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T05:02:34-07:00","id":1328499,"title":"","content":"Congratulations for the Kickstarter's resounding success.<br /> <br /> I am now looking forward to Adventure next year. It was always my favorite of the three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T08:35:32-07:00","id":1335316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And once in a while it\u2019s because we choose to take a bit longer and do something right, like the meeting we had today with the TC:Aberrant team to go over the playtest feedback we got during the Kickstarter. </div> </div> </div>So this was posted on Monday in the weekly update. No real detailed info but I thought it was interesting. <br /> <br /> I do kind of wonder how our feedback might have changed things. Hopefully they looked at the things we super complained about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T14:01:53-07:00","id":1335343,"title":"","content":"They listened for sure. But it was commented more than once that some of the things we complained were intentionally put there, and so are probably not changing.<br /> <br /> My guesses on what will change is Super Science creation limits (the process is great, the quantum consuming in the way to expensive for the inventor). I know it\u2019s hard to keep the balance, but you had no chance to build a Iron Man (with more than a few armors).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T14:18:37-07:00","id":1335346,"title":"","content":"Likewise, I don't expect that Flux will be going away; but I do think it's possible that it might be made easier to manage. Radical changes aren't happening; but minor adjustments may yet occur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T14:36:42-07:00","id":1335349,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, Flux is a core part of the setting and isn\u2019t going anywhere, but the mechanics might be reworked a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T14:50:03-07:00","id":1335351,"title":"","content":"For Flux, I would make a Nova Edge (not a Mega Edge) for a better flux bleeding. It may sound almost obligatory for many people here, but I think there is two kinds of Novas, as the Nihonjin experts discovered, the ones that don\u2019t accumulate flux easily and the ones that does.<br /> <br /> Another option is to make Transcendence gained by high quantum be a minimum value and not a additional value. So you can become monstrous by the eruption and still handle transcendence on high quantum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T15:34:53-07:00","id":1335361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1335351#post1335351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Flux, I would make a Nova Edge (not a Mega Edge) for a better flux bleeding. It may sound almost obligatory for many people here, but I think there is two kinds of Novas, as the Nihonjin experts discovered, the ones that don\u2019t accumulate flux easily and the ones that does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the game is better thematically served by having in-game choices matter more than that. I\u2019d work the system off Bonds with Baselines instead of \u201cnot using the cool powers you paid for\u201d though. Those human connections are what anchors you and keep you human. Divorcing from the mortal society and treating Baselines as other leads to Transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-12-2019, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-12T15:50:56-07:00","id":1335362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1321831-tc-aberrant-kickstarter?p=1335361#post1335361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the game is better thematically served by having in-game choices matter more than that. I\u2019d work the system off Bonds with Baselines instead of \u201cnot using the cool powers you paid for\u201d though. Those human connections are what anchors you and keep you human. Divorcing from the mortal society and treating Baselines as other leads to Transcendence.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Indeed it\u2019s interesting to have a in game way to deal instead of putting the character in the fridge for a few weeks.<br /> <br /> But, it\u2019s a matter of how you see the Transcendence. There are 2 ways basically, the first is Transcendence is caused by flux and cause the feeling of not being human, the second is Transcendence is caused by the feeling of not being human and allow the grow of quantum.<br /> <br /> Both are valid approaches, but the first imply the condition of transcendence is out of our control, except for controlling the quantum use (the way I see the original rules), and the other gives the character the need of mental balance to keep human, otherwise they will became monsters (the option shown on Four Color).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}